  <channel>
    <title>Adamastor — Weekly Digest</title>
    <link>https://adamastor.blog/</link>
    <description>Adamastor is a digital publication for all things startup in Portugal. Weekly reporting and analysis on the Portuguese startup scene.</description>
    <language>en</language>
    <lastBuildDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 16:17:24 GMT</lastBuildDate>
    <atom:link href="https://adamastor.blog/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" />
    <item>
      <title>What’s moving the ecosystem: 4 signals worth your attention | Week 36</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/what-s-moving-the-ecosystem-4-signals-worth-your-attention-week-36</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/what-s-moving-the-ecosystem-4-signals-worth-your-attention-week-36</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 16:17:24 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>Hello everyone, This week 4 moments worth your attention. Starting with Lisbon AI Week kicked off Monday turning Lisbon a living lab for Artificial Intelligence. Seven days. One city. Dozens of events. From hackathons and workshops to talks on creativity, healthcare, industrial AI and the questions…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3>Hello everyone,</h3><p>This week 4 moments worth your attention. </p><p>Starting with <strong>Lisbon AI Week</strong> kicked off Monday turning Lisbon a living lab for Artificial Intelligence. Seven days. One city. Dozens of events. From hackathons and workshops to talks on creativity, healthcare, industrial AI and the questions no one has answered yet. No single venue, no headliner: Lisbon AI Week happens all over the city, hosted by the community that builds here. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://lisbonaiweek.com/">Most are free, some are ticketed, all are open to anyone.</a>  One of the most highlighted event is <strong>Lisbon AI</strong>. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://lisbonai.org/">Two days. 32 speakers. 400 builders</a>. No hype decks, no rubber‑chicken dinners. It’s code, talks, and hallway hacking. Labs, founding teams, and engineers deploying models in production; all in the same room, discussing what’s working now and what’s coming next.</p><p>On Thursday <strong>Startup Portugal</strong> marks its 10 year anniversary. A decade of programs, community building, and giving founders a stage. Ten years go fast when the country changes this quickly and the accumulated impact is finally visible in talent, capital, and ambition. A milestone worth celebrating.</p><p>On Friday Porto kicks off <strong>Techstars Startup Weekend</strong>. Three days of raw building energy. Teams formed on the spot, ideas pushed into prototype territory by sheer willpower (and caffeine), mentors sprinting between tables, and that unmistakable vibe that only appears when people gather to build without asking for permission. Porto keeps proving it’s hungry, and it’s not slowing down.</p><p>And in Europe, the clock is ticking: 100 days to get <strong>EU Inc right</strong>.  The window is open, and it won’t stay open for long. If we want a European corporate regime that actually serves founders, investors, and companies scaling here, this is the moment. There’s an open letter circulating. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eu-inc.org/100days">Co‑sign it. Make it count</a>.</p><p>See you <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><span style="color: rgb(15, 20, 25);">“From nothing came something without meaning — and suddenly it was already a poem."</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(15, 20, 25);"><strong>Jorge Palma</strong></span></p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/">Applications open</a> for the <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> next cohort</p></li><li><p><strong>Porto Techstars Startup Weekend</strong>. Three days of raw building energy, starting this Friday, 25 at LACS Porto. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://351startups.com/techstars-startup-weekend-porto-2026/">Apply for the last spots</a>.</p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);">The 11th edition of </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://boqvbrp.clicks.mlsend.com/ty/c/eyJ2Ijoie1wiYVwiOjE3ODkxMjUsXCJsXCI6MTk1Nzk2MzA0NDQyNDI2NjE1LFwiclwiOjE5NTc5NjMxODU4MDM3NzQ3Mn0iLCJzIjoiNzc5OTQ0OTRlMTc0Y2E4MyJ9"><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"><strong><u>Road 2 Web Summit</u></strong></span></a><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"> by <strong>Startup Portugal</strong> is open. Up to </span>125 Portuguese startups<span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"> get an intensive bootcamp in Porto and Lisbon, a discount on their Web Summit package, and a shot at the Galp prizes. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://boqvbrp.clicks.mlsend.com/ty/c/eyJ2Ijoie1wiYVwiOjE3ODkxMjUsXCJsXCI6MTk1Nzk2MzA0NDQ5NzY2NjQ4LFwiclwiOjE5NTc5NjMxODU4MDM3NzQ3Mn0iLCJzIjoiMjE4ZWM5MzBjMzVkNjYzMyJ9"><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"><strong><u>Apply here</u></strong></span></a><strong>.</strong></p></li><li><p>Are you set to make an impact in biotech for planetary health? <strong>Biotope Ventures</strong> want to hear from you. With our program, you'll be able to turn your innovation into a viable business. 350k early-stage funding and a tailored growth journey for biotech startups in planetary health. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://biotope-ventures.com/apply-now/">Applications close on Sep 25</a></p></li><li><p><strong>SKYHACK </strong>Lisbon's one-day hackathon by LX Launch (Sep 26). We put 50 of the sharpest builders in one room and give them 10 hours to turn a rough idea into something that actually runs. You'll work alongside mentors, founders and engineers from across Lisbon's tech scene. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://skyhack.lxlaunch.com/">Apply here.</a></p></li><li><p><strong>Urban Mobility Explained (UMX) Open Call</strong>. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eiturbanmobility.eu/call-for-proposals/urban-mobility-explained-umx-open-call-2/">Apply until Sep 29</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Founder2Founder by Algarve Evolution</strong> will select 𝟴 𝗔𝗹𝗴𝗮𝗿𝘃𝗲-𝗰𝗼𝗻𝗻𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗲𝗱 𝗰𝗼𝗺𝗽𝗮𝗻𝗶𝗲𝘀 𝗳𝗼𝗿 𝗮 𝘀𝗶𝘅-𝗺𝗼𝗻𝘁𝗵 𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗼𝗿𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗮𝗰𝗰𝗲𝗹𝗲𝗿𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗽𝗿𝗼𝗴𝗿𝗮𝗺. - A dedicated mentor - One focused growth plan - Three measurable targets - Monthly reviews to sharpen priorities, improve decisions, and turn ambition into action. For companies already in the market, ready to grow, and open to being challenged. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.algarveevolution.pt/pt/founder2founder">Apply until Sep 30</a>. </p></li><li><p><strong>Portugal XR Report 2026</strong> -  Call for Participation: For the 3rd year in a row, we're again inviting all organizations to participate in the Portugal XR &amp; Virtual Worlds Report, the reference report for XR, digital twins and converging technologies in Portugal. Thanks to your participation,  we'll be able to identify and analyse the yearly growth of the XR market, talent and investment levels in the country. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSft05ZM-fGHWOrvErRs3yT7QZC8CWAOpkuSeF9ftWGyfGL82Q/viewform?pli=1">Participation is open until Sep 30</a>.</p></li><li><p>Is expanding to Portugal your next move? Discover how with Launch in Lisbon! That is exactly what Launch in Lisbon is designed to make easier. The <strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa</strong> program supports international entrepreneurs and companies looking to launch, establish, or expand their operations in Portugal and across Europe. <span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">The program is available in both in-person and virtual formats, although virtual participation provides limited access to the full program. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/V3DPGTNcGrQ?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>Early Bird and virtual tickets are already available here</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">.</span></p></li><li><p><strong>PORTUGAL - EUDIS Hackathon 2026 Autumn</strong>, registration for the EUDIS Hackathon 2026 Autumn is now live! We are thrilled that you are ready to innovate and build with us. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tally.so/r/yPAkyp">Please complete the registration form</a> to submit your application.</p></li><li><p><strong>Start From Knowledge</strong> be the right program for your project? SFN supports the creation and development of knowledge-based startups, helping turn scientific and technological knowledge into solutions with market potential. The program is aimed at projects connected to higher education and research, supporting the journey from knowledge generated within R&amp;D institutions to the creation of new businesses. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ani.pt/start-from-knowledge/">More info here</a>.</p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://eic.ec.europa.eu/eic-prizes/european-prize-women-innovators-powered-eic-eit_en">Applications are open </a>for the <strong>European Prize for Women Innovators </strong>is an initiative powered by the European Institute of Innovation &amp; Technology (EIT) and the European Innovation Council (EIC). It celebrates the outstanding achievements of women entrepreneurs from across the EU and Horizon Europe associated countries who are driving positive change for people and the planet through their innovative ventures.</p></li><li><p>On Oct 15, the DNA Cascais auditorium will host the <strong>TechID Journey</strong> — a hands‑on immersion designed to equip women with practical skills in Artificial Intelligence, leadership development, and active employability. From Connection to Real Impact: TechID Journey Brings Together Female Leadership, Employability, and AI at DNA Cascais. The event promoted by Ponts brings together major corporate brands, recruitment companies, and media partners to accelerate female presence in the tech ecosystem. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://techid.ponts.network/">Secure your spot here</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Web Summit 26</strong> first <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://websummit.com/speakers/">speakers</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://attend.websummit.com/lis26/schedule">agenda</a> announced</p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><strong>Sword Health</strong> is acquiring Headspace.</p></li><li><p><strong>Quartz</strong>, founded by André Silva and Mateus Mesquita Alves, raised 3.2M.</p></li><li><p><strong>DeskAmigo</strong> has secured 350K in pre-seed funding.</p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/catarina-kemper/"><span><strong>Catarina Kemper</strong></span></a><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);"> </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/marcelolebre/"><strong>Marcelo Lebre</strong></a><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);"> (</span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/remote.com/"><strong>Remote</strong></a><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);">) and </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nunosebastiao/"><strong>Nuno Sebastiao</strong></a><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);"> (</span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/feedzai/"><strong>Feedzai</strong></a><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);">)were selected as finalists for Digital Entrepreneur of the Year at the 2026 Navegantes XXI Awards.</span></p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 Carlos Resende: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sapo.pt/artigo/muito-para-la-da-web-summit-o-ecossistema-empreendedor-em-movimento-6aa057495ab042010d500256">Muito para lá da Web Summit: o ecossistema empreendedor em movimento</a></p><p>📚 O <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://dinheirovivo.dn.pt/o-funding-gap-no-se-resolve-com-prmios-resolve-se-com-acesso">funding 'gap'</a> não se resolve com prémios. Resolve-se com acesso by Carolina Almeida Cruz</p><p>📚 Building LogiCola's new design language from <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://logicola.org/blog/the-new-logicola">what I found reverse-engineering the 2008 original</a> by Malik Piara</p><p>📚 Try the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startuptools.builduplabs.com/equity-split-calculator/">Build Up Labs Co-founder Equity Split Calculator</a> .The current version provides a structured starting point based on time commitment, financial investment, relevant experience, and role criticality.</p><p>📚 Venture Institute: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/venture-institute-what-eight-weeks-taught-me-diogo-mendon%C3%A7a-87b1e/">What Eight Weeks Taught</a> Me by Diogo Mendonça</p><p>📚 The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/elephant-does-read-constitution-pedro-santa-clara-ycfle">Elephant Does Not Read the Constitution</a> by Pedro Santa Clara</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.acquired.fm/episodes/home-depot">Complete history and strategy of The Home Depot</a> by acquired.fm</p><p>🎬 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/xtS7pSMEknU?si=_VPMdTBRwBOvt_3I">Estratégia de Produto Quando a Rapidez é uma Commodity</a> by Krasi Bozhinkova</p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Ecosystem Keeps Moving | Week 35</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/ecosystem-keeps-moving-week-35</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/ecosystem-keeps-moving-week-35</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:37:58 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>Hello everyone, Another week, another reminder of how alive the Portuguese startup ecosystem is. A few days ago I was in Gaia for a Founder Institute session, and it was impossible not to feel the momentum in the room; new founders, new ideas, and a genuine curiosity about how to build in Portugal.…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3>Hello everyone,</h3><p><span>Another week, another reminder of how alive the Portuguese startup ecosystem is. A few days ago I was in Gaia for a </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/"><span>Founder Institute</span></a><span> session, and it was impossible not to feel the momentum in the room; new founders, new ideas, and a genuine curiosity about how to build in Portugal. That energy, and the desire to bring more people into the community, is a big part why I restarted my biweekly page at </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sapo.pt/autores/carlos-resende"><span>SAPO</span></a><span>.</span></p><p>Something caught my particular attention: Defence Tech is emerging as a space where Portuguese startups can and should play a role. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events">The Defence Tech Meetup</a> (Sep 22), held during the REPMUS exercise, focused on Autonomy: From Orbit to Maritime Operations; a theme where Portugal has real potential. Organized by Critical Software &amp; Productized, the meetup brought together engineers working directly in the field, experts with firsthand experience from the Ukrainian reality, corporates and startups.</p><p>All of this happens at a moment when the <strong>Portuguese National Entrepreneurship Strategy 2030</strong> has closed its contribution phase. All inputs are in, and the work now moves to the diagnosis stage understanding what the ecosystem said, identifying patterns, and preparing the ground for the policy agenda that will guide entrepreneurship through the next decade.</p><p>See you <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><span style="color: rgb(15, 20, 25);">“</span><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);">The brick walls are there for a reason. The brick walls are not there to keep us out. The brick walls are there to give us a chance to show how badly we want something."</span><br><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);">Randy Pausch</span></p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/">Applications open</a> for the <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> next cohort</p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);">The 11th edition of </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://boqvbrp.clicks.mlsend.com/ty/c/eyJ2Ijoie1wiYVwiOjE3ODkxMjUsXCJsXCI6MTk1Nzk2MzA0NDQyNDI2NjE1LFwiclwiOjE5NTc5NjMxODU4MDM3NzQ3Mn0iLCJzIjoiNzc5OTQ0OTRlMTc0Y2E4MyJ9"><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"><strong><u>Road 2 Web Summit</u></strong></span></a><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"> by <strong>Startup Portugal</strong> is open. Up to </span>125 Portuguese startups<span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"> get an intensive bootcamp in Porto and Lisbon, a discount on their Web Summit package, and a shot at the Galp prizes. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://boqvbrp.clicks.mlsend.com/ty/c/eyJ2Ijoie1wiYVwiOjE3ODkxMjUsXCJsXCI6MTk1Nzk2MzA0NDQ5NzY2NjQ4LFwiclwiOjE5NTc5NjMxODU4MDM3NzQ3Mn0iLCJzIjoiMjE4ZWM5MzBjMzVkNjYzMyJ9"><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"><strong><u>Apply here</u></strong></span></a><strong>.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Portugal Fintech Report </strong>2026 marks 10 years of Portugal Fintech. This special edition of the Report tells the story of the ecosystem we built together, and it sets the stage for the next one. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://forms.fillout.com/t/qxML9JfCLEus">By answering this form</a>, you are applying your Fintech to be featured in the report as one of the top fintechs in Portugal. Fill the form until Sep 15.</p></li><li><p><strong>Access to funding</strong> is a critical factor for startups looking to scale. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://OpportunityHub.eu">OpportunityHub.eu</a> brings together funding opportunities across European countries into a single platform.</p></li><li><p>Defence Tech Meetup (Sep 22) occurs during the REPMUS exercise and is specifically focused on Autonomy: From Orbit to Maritime Operations. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/9aw7ot90">Will take place at Critical Software Headquarters in Lisbon</a> for an insightful end-of-the-day with presentations, networking opportunities for Defence, and free drinks and snacks.</p></li><li><p>​<strong>LISBON AI</strong> 2 days. 32 speakers. 400 builders. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://lisbonai.org/">Is happening next Sep 23–24</a>. Lisbon AI is the annual summit for people shipping AI in the real world. No hype decks, no rubber-chicken dinners. Just code, talks, and hallway hacking. Join top labs, founding teams, and engineers deploying models in production, to chat about where we are now and what's next.</p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">The </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eu-japan.eu/">EU-Japan Centre</a><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);"> invites European companies and clusters to apply to the Nanotech Business Mission in Japan in December 2026. The application deadline is 24 September with the mission including participation in </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.nanotechexpo.jp/en/">nano tech 2026</a><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">, a leading Japanese trade fair for advanced materials, processes and enabling technologies. Apply until Sept 24.</span></p></li><li><p>Are you set to make an impact in biotech for planetary health? <strong>Biotope Ventures</strong> want to hear from you. With our program, you'll be able to turn your innovation into a viable business. 350k early-stage funding and a tailored growth journey for biotech startups in planetary health. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://biotope-ventures.com/apply-now/">Applications close on Sep 25</a></p></li><li><p><strong>SKYHACK </strong>Lisbon's one-day hackathon by LX Launch (Sep 26). We put 50 of the sharpest builders in one room and give them 10 hours to turn a rough idea into something that actually runs. You'll work alongside mentors, founders and engineers from across Lisbon's tech scene. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://skyhack.lxlaunch.com/">Apply here.</a></p></li><li><p><strong>Urban Mobility Explained (UMX) Open Call</strong>. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eiturbanmobility.eu/call-for-proposals/urban-mobility-explained-umx-open-call-2/">Apply until Sep 29</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Founder2Founder by Algarve Evolution</strong> will select 𝟴 𝗔𝗹𝗴𝗮𝗿𝘃𝗲-𝗰𝗼𝗻𝗻𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗲𝗱 𝗰𝗼𝗺𝗽𝗮𝗻𝗶𝗲𝘀 𝗳𝗼𝗿 𝗮 𝘀𝗶𝘅-𝗺𝗼𝗻𝘁𝗵 𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗼𝗿𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗮𝗰𝗰𝗲𝗹𝗲𝗿𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗽𝗿𝗼𝗴𝗿𝗮𝗺. - A dedicated mentor - One focused growth plan - Three measurable targets - Monthly reviews to sharpen priorities, improve decisions, and turn ambition into action. For companies already in the market, ready to grow, and open to being challenged. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.algarveevolution.pt/pt/founder2founder">Apply until Sep 30</a>. </p></li><li><p><strong>Portugal XR Report 2026</strong> -  Call for Participation: For the 3rd year in a row, we're again inviting all organizations to participate in the Portugal XR &amp; Virtual Worlds Report, the reference report for XR, digital twins and converging technologies in Portugal. Thanks to your participation,  we'll be able to identify and analyse the yearly growth of the XR market, talent and investment levels in the country. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSft05ZM-fGHWOrvErRs3yT7QZC8CWAOpkuSeF9ftWGyfGL82Q/viewform?pli=1">Participation is open until Sep 30</a>.</p></li><li><p>Is expanding to Portugal your next move? Discover how with Launch in Lisbon! That is exactly what Launch in Lisbon is designed to make easier. The <strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa</strong> program supports international entrepreneurs and companies looking to launch, establish, or expand their operations in Portugal and across Europe. <span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">The program is available in both in-person and virtual formats, although virtual participation provides limited access to the full program. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/V3DPGTNcGrQ?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>Early Bird and virtual tickets are already available here</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">.</span></p></li><li><p><strong>PORTUGAL - EUDIS Hackathon 2026 Autumn</strong>, registration for the EUDIS Hackathon 2026 Autumn is now live! We are thrilled that you are ready to innovate and build with us. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tally.so/r/yPAkyp">Please complete the registration form</a> to submit your application.</p></li><li><p><strong>Start From Knowledge</strong> be the right program for your project? SFN supports the creation and development of knowledge-based startups, helping turn scientific and technological knowledge into solutions with market potential. The program is aimed at projects connected to higher education and research, supporting the journey from knowledge generated within R&amp;D institutions to the creation of new businesses. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ani.pt/start-from-knowledge/">More info here</a>.</p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://eic.ec.europa.eu/eic-prizes/european-prize-women-innovators-powered-eic-eit_en">Applications are open </a>for the <strong>European Prize for Women Innovators </strong>is an initiative powered by the European Institute of Innovation &amp; Technology (EIT) and the European Innovation Council (EIC). It celebrates the outstanding achievements of women entrepreneurs from across the EU and Horizon Europe associated countries who are driving positive change for people and the planet through their innovative ventures.</p></li><li><p><strong>Web Summit 26</strong> first <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://websummit.com/speakers/">speakers</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://attend.websummit.com/lis26/schedule">agenda</a> announced</p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p>Motorola Solutions has acquired AI <strong>startup DeepNeuronic.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Enline, Octo Health, ExpertGrain, Lampsy Health, noticed., VeriCasa, FRANK, CodePlatform, Savearth and C-MORE</strong> at San Francisco TechWeek RedBridge program.</p></li><li><p><strong>Lampsy Health</strong> won the sixth edition of KPMG's Global Tech Innovator in Portugal.</p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 Carlos Resende: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sapo.pt/artigo/muito-para-la-da-web-summit-o-ecossistema-empreendedor-em-movimento-6aa057495ab042010d500256">Muito para lá da Web Summit: o ecossistema empreendedor em movimento</a></p><p>📚 Try the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startuptools.builduplabs.com/equity-split-calculator/">Build Up Labs Co-founder Equity Split Calculator</a> .The current version provides a structured starting point based on time commitment, financial investment, relevant experience, and role criticality.</p><p>📚 100 days to get <strong>EU Inc </strong>right. Now is the moment. Let’s make it count. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://eu-inc.org/100days">Co-sign the open letter</a>.</p><p>🎧 Bitalk: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/5RUL60Vp91Yyt0jPU8ZadF?si=Iq7HQS2QRiav-M5OfYDC5Q">A primeira IA portuguesa</a> c/ Paulo Dimas</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/3TUppu7X3UJTMNGXOoVY0a?si=qPAXK2zNRfqi5-nKxrbkQg">How to turn setbacks into success</a> w/ Amy Shoenthal </p><p>🎬 Randy Pausch Lecture: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/oTugjssqOT0?si=S3dCof3D_8ZtTT1X">Time Management</a></p><p>🎬 Founder Tales com Andreia Trigo: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/DWaj5WI1llQ?si=Mo9TOqJfTQoiq6gK">Transformou uma doença rara numa startup</a></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Build a stronger ecosystem | Week 34</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/build-a-stronger-ecosystem-week-34</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/build-a-stronger-ecosystem-week-34</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 09:56:17 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>Hello everyone, September&amp;nbsp;marks&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;return&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;one&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;most&amp;nbsp;dynamic&amp;nbsp;periods&amp;nbsp;for&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;Portuguese&amp;nbsp;…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3>Hello everyone,</h3><p>September&nbsp;marks&nbsp;the&nbsp;return&nbsp;of&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;dynamic&nbsp;periods&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;Portuguese&nbsp; entrepreneurial&nbsp;ecosystem.&nbsp;What&nbsp;stands&nbsp;out&nbsp;this&nbsp;year&nbsp;is&nbsp;the&nbsp;growing&nbsp;decentralisation&nbsp;of&nbsp;activity:&nbsp;Algarve,&nbsp;Braga,&nbsp;Viseu,&nbsp;Coimbra,&nbsp;Leiria&nbsp;and&nbsp;others&nbsp;are&nbsp;stepping&nbsp;forward&nbsp;with ambition,&nbsp;proving&nbsp;once&nbsp;again&nbsp;that&nbsp;innovation&nbsp;in&nbsp;Portugal&nbsp;is&nbsp;not&nbsp;a&nbsp;two‑city&nbsp;story.</p><p>Strong&nbsp;local&nbsp;communities&nbsp;build&nbsp;a&nbsp;stronger&nbsp;ecosystem.&nbsp;They&nbsp;create&nbsp;density,&nbsp; attract&nbsp;talent,&nbsp;and&nbsp;give&nbsp;founders&nbsp;the&nbsp;confidence&nbsp;to&nbsp;start&nbsp;and&nbsp;to&nbsp;keep&nbsp;going.&nbsp;That’s&nbsp;why all&nbsp;these&nbsp;initiatives&nbsp;matter:&nbsp;they&nbsp;connect&nbsp;people,&nbsp;accelerate&nbsp;ideas,&nbsp;and&nbsp;set&nbsp;the&nbsp;tone&nbsp;for&nbsp; the&nbsp;months&nbsp;ahead.&nbsp;</p><p>The&nbsp;calendar&nbsp;is&nbsp;already&nbsp;packed,&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Adamastor</strong>&nbsp;will&nbsp;continue&nbsp;to&nbsp;curate&nbsp;the&nbsp;best&nbsp; initiatives&nbsp;across&nbsp;the&nbsp;country,&nbsp;highlighting&nbsp;the&nbsp;work,&nbsp;achievements,&nbsp;and&nbsp;momentum&nbsp;of&nbsp; our&nbsp;founders.&nbsp;Week&nbsp;after&nbsp;week,&nbsp;your&nbsp;feedback&nbsp;helps&nbsp;refine&nbsp;this&nbsp;space&nbsp;and&nbsp;keep&nbsp;it&nbsp;useful,&nbsp;relevant,&nbsp;and&nbsp;honest&nbsp;and&nbsp;for&nbsp;that,&nbsp;I’m&nbsp;genuinely&nbsp;grateful.</p><p>It’s&nbsp;good&nbsp;to&nbsp;be&nbsp;back.&nbsp;Let’s&nbsp;make&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;of&nbsp;what’s&nbsp;coming.</p><p>See you <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><span style="color: rgb(15, 20, 25);">“</span>Never doubt that a small group of thoughtful, committed citizens can change the world"</p><p>Margaret Mead</p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/">Applications open</a> for the <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> next cohort</p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);">The 11th edition of </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://boqvbrp.clicks.mlsend.com/ty/c/eyJ2Ijoie1wiYVwiOjE3ODkxMjUsXCJsXCI6MTk1Nzk2MzA0NDQyNDI2NjE1LFwiclwiOjE5NTc5NjMxODU4MDM3NzQ3Mn0iLCJzIjoiNzc5OTQ0OTRlMTc0Y2E4MyJ9"><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"><strong><u>Road 2 Web Summit</u></strong></span></a><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"> by <strong>Startup Portugal</strong> is open. Up to </span>125 Portuguese startups<span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"> get an intensive bootcamp in Porto and Lisbon, a discount on their Web Summit package, and a shot at the Galp prizes. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://boqvbrp.clicks.mlsend.com/ty/c/eyJ2Ijoie1wiYVwiOjE3ODkxMjUsXCJsXCI6MTk1Nzk2MzA0NDQ5NzY2NjQ4LFwiclwiOjE5NTc5NjMxODU4MDM3NzQ3Mn0iLCJzIjoiMjE4ZWM5MzBjMzVkNjYzMyJ9"><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"><strong><u>Apply here</u></strong></span></a><strong>.</strong></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">The</span><strong>&nbsp;Santander X Awards</strong><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">, are looking for university projects and startups with the potential to grow. Participants gain access to prizes, mentoring, training, and visibility. Applications are open until Sep 11 for </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/14lQgQZKatn?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>startups</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">&nbsp;and&nbsp;</span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/dhQ1KvMD2Uu?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>university students</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">&nbsp;here.&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><strong>Investor Talks </strong>next September 12 &amp; 13 in Portimão. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.investortalks.pt/"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Agenda and tickets available here</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">.</span></p></li><li><p><strong>Hospitality Open Innovation Program</strong> powered by Turismo de Portugal, Grupo Pestana, and Feel Group <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.hospitality.unicornfactorylisboa.com/">is accepting applications</a> until Sep 13. They are looking for startups with pilot ready solutions capable to address the following challenges: Customer Relationship &amp; Experience; Marketing Intelligence, Digital Content &amp; Data; Automation &amp; Productivity – Daily Operations; Automation &amp; Productivity – Backoffice; Physical Space Smart Sensing.</p></li><li><p><strong>Gathering Design Sprint</strong> is a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.boardingpass.co/gathering-design">4-week virtual sprint</a> teaching founders the craft of designing gatherings people remember, and want to come back to. The next Sprint launches September 14th <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.boardingpass.co/gathering-design">Enroll here</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>BSC AI Factory Incubation Programme </strong>in Porto supports startups and SMEs in the development of AI products and projects. Running at UPTEC from 5 October 2026 to 30 March 2027, the programme combines free coworking with specialist support, workshops, networking opportunities and connections to the wider European BSC AI Factory ecosystem. Selected companies can also receive support in identifying the technical, software and computing resources most appropriate to their projects. A<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://form.typeform.com/to/tgWhzCRf?typeform-source=bsc-aifactory.eu">pplications open until Sep 15</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Portugal Fintech Report </strong>2026 marks 10 years of Portugal Fintech. This special edition of the Report tells the story of the ecosystem we built together, and it sets the stage for the next one. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://forms.fillout.com/t/qxML9JfCLEus">By answering this form</a>, you are applying your Fintech to be featured in the report as one of the top fintechs in Portugal. Fill the form until Sep 15.</p></li><li><p><strong>Access to funding</strong> is a critical factor for startups looking to scale. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://OpportunityHub.eu">OpportunityHub.eu</a> brings together funding opportunities across European countries into a single platform.</p></li><li><p>For all AI builders, 20×20, <strong>RedBridge</strong>’s first PechaKucha-style night. The format is simple and a little unforgiving: 20 slides, 20 seconds each. The deck advances whether you’re ready or not. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ekbau.r.sp1-brevo.net/mk/cl/f/sh/SMK1E8tHeFuBlatR8GYFbzpYxvmC/QK1btIHZjYss">Apply to present, next Sep 17</a></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">The </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eu-japan.eu/">EU-Japan Centre</a><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);"> invites European companies and clusters to apply to the Nanotech Business Mission in Japan in December 2026. The application deadline is 24 September with the mission including participation in </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.nanotechexpo.jp/en/">nano tech 2026</a><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">, a leading Japanese trade fair for advanced materials, processes and enabling technologies. Apply until Sept 24.</span></p></li><li><p>Are you set to make an impact in biotech for planetary health? <strong>Biotope Ventures</strong> want to hear from you. With our program, you'll be able to turn your innovation into a viable business. 350k early-stage funding and a tailored growth journey for biotech startups in planetary health. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://biotope-ventures.com/apply-now/">Applications close on Sep 25</a></p></li><li><p>Is expanding to Portugal your next move? Discover how with Launch in Lisbon! That is exactly what Launch in Lisbon is designed to make easier. The <strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa</strong> program supports international entrepreneurs and companies looking to launch, establish, or expand their operations in Portugal and across Europe. <span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">The program is available in both in-person and virtual formats, although virtual participation provides limited access to the full program. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/V3DPGTNcGrQ?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>Early Bird and virtual tickets are already available here</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">.</span></p></li><li><p><strong>PORTUGAL - EUDIS Hackathon 2026 Autumn</strong>, registration for the EUDIS Hackathon 2026 Autumn is now live! We are thrilled that you are ready to innovate and build with us. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tally.so/r/yPAkyp">Please complete the registration form</a> to submit your application.</p></li><li><p><strong>Start From Knowledge</strong> be the right program for your project? SFN supports the creation and development of knowledge-based startups, helping turn scientific and technological knowledge into solutions with market potential. The program is aimed at projects connected to higher education and research, supporting the journey from knowledge generated within R&amp;D institutions to the creation of new businesses. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ani.pt/start-from-knowledge/">More info here</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Web Summit 26</strong> first <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://websummit.com/speakers/">speakers</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://attend.websummit.com/lis26/schedule">agenda</a> announced</p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><strong>Zeropact</strong> listed as TOP50 startups selected for the 7th edition of the European Startup Prize for Mobility.</p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><strong>Sword Health</strong> acquires Headspace</span></p></li><li><p><strong>Tekever</strong> acquires Flowcopter </p></li><li><p><strong>London Quantum Group</strong> (Junitec alumni) raised +1M</p></li><li><p>The startups going to San Francisco with Startup Portugal: <strong>Enline </strong>(Energy/SaaS); <strong>Octo Health </strong>(Healthtech); <strong>ExpertGrain </strong>(AgriTech/SaaS); <strong>Lampsy Health </strong>(Healthtech); <strong>noticed </strong>(AI/ML); <strong>VeriCasa </strong>(PropTech/SaaS); <strong>FRANK </strong>(InsurTech/AI);  <strong>CodePlatform </strong>(AI/ML); <strong>Savearth </strong>(Hospitality/Deeptech); and <strong>C-MORE </strong>(SaaS/Enterprise)</p></li><li><p><strong>Hope Care</strong> raised 6M</p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚Casa do Impacto: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.cmjornal.pt/c-studio/especiais-c-studio/boas-causas/detalhe/casa-do-impacto-o-hub-de-empreendedorismo-social-da-santa-casa">o hub de empreendedorismo social da Santa Casa</a> </p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://paulgraham.com/prepare.html">How Universities Should Prepare Founders</a> by Paul Graham</p><p>📚Here is the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://letter.rebuild.net">Rebuild letter</a> <span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);">calling for a new generation of social platforms.</span></p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://anelimanbay.substack.com/p/the-second-language-of-belonging">The Second Language of Belonging</a>: Eleven years in Portugal, and what a decade of learning a country does to a mind by Anel Imanbay</p><p>📚Building  a competitive Europe: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.esnalliance.eu/reports">the role of startup and scaleup ecosystems</a></p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://time.com/collection/time100-ai/2026/">TIME100 AI 2026</a>: Meet the innovators, leaders, and thinkers reshaping our world through groundbreaking advances in artificial intelligence.</p><p>🎧James Clear: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/9yEweH11FG8?si=4flPmnTGwekBqqjs">The Secret to Building Daily Habits</a>.</p><p>🎬<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/6sfpC8qRGFA?si=jrVN_VHgyP-iBXO7">The Founder Mindset</a> with Tim Ferriss</p><p>🎬<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://x.com/A24/status/2096757842435084301">YOU CAN SEE EVERYTHING</a>, a documentary by Nathan Fielder and Lance Oppenheim. Featuring Elizabeth Holmes. (Teaser) </p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Time to get back | Week 33</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/time-to-get-back-week-33</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/time-to-get-back-week-33</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 19:29:26 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>Hello everyone, Hope you all had a great summer, whether you unplugged completely, traveled, or just caught up on some long-overdue sleep. Now it’s time to get back to building, connecting, and making things happen. We’re excited to restart our weekly journey together, bringing you the most…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3>Hello everyone,</h3><p>Hope you all had a great summer, whether you unplugged completely, traveled, or just caught up on some long-overdue sleep. Now it’s <strong>time to get back</strong> to building, connecting, and making things happen.</p><p>We’re excited to restart our weekly journey together, bringing you the most relevant events, resources, and opportunities for entrepreneurs, startups, and the innovation ecosystem in Portugal.</p><p>The next few months promise to be vibrant for our community. From local meetups to global conferences, from early-stage support programs to investment opportunities, the Portuguese startup scene is buzzing with energy.</p><p>Expect to see:</p><p>Big events: several cities will host several startup gatherings that put founders, investors, and ecosystem builders in the same room. i.e. Techstars Startup Week Guimaraes; WebSummit; Lisbon AI Conference; Pitch nights; Founder Institute Portugal; Porto Impact Week 2026; Portugal Tech Week, Investor Talks, Incubex, Santander X,  EUDIS Hackathon ...</p><p>Community growth: More international founders are choosing Portugal as their base, enriching our ecosystem and creating new collaboration possibilities. ex: Techstars Community Leader Academy; Launch in Lisbon, Unicorn Factory Incubation Program, Santander X...</p><p>We will keep you in the loop with events, opportunities, and stories that matter, and we can’t wait to hear what you think, too.</p><p>Let’s turn this re-entry into a season of new ideas, meaningful collaborations, real impact, and moving the whole ecosystem forward. See you <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><span style="color: rgb(15, 20, 25);">“I have never belonged to any place, or to any person. I have always been a guest passing through, even in my own life.”<br><br>Fernando Pessoa</span></p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/">Applications open</a> for the <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> next cohort, starting in October</p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">Applications for the</span><strong> Fall Batch ’26</strong><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);"> of <strong>Unicorn Factory</strong> </span><strong>Incubation Program</strong><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">, for early-stage startups, are now open. Receive mentorship tailored to your project’s needs, participate in training sessions, access a network of over 190 mentors, and connect with 150 investors and corporate partners. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/jaISlWytDAr?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>Apply by September 6 here</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);">The 11th edition of </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://boqvbrp.clicks.mlsend.com/ty/c/eyJ2Ijoie1wiYVwiOjE3ODkxMjUsXCJsXCI6MTk1Nzk2MzA0NDQyNDI2NjE1LFwiclwiOjE5NTc5NjMxODU4MDM3NzQ3Mn0iLCJzIjoiNzc5OTQ0OTRlMTc0Y2E4MyJ9"><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"><strong><u>Road 2 Web Summit</u></strong></span></a><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"> by <strong>Startup Portugal</strong> is open. Up to </span>125 Portuguese startups<span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"> get an intensive bootcamp in Porto and Lisbon, a discount on their Web Summit package, and a shot at the Galp prizes. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://boqvbrp.clicks.mlsend.com/ty/c/eyJ2Ijoie1wiYVwiOjE3ODkxMjUsXCJsXCI6MTk1Nzk2MzA0NDQ5NzY2NjQ4LFwiclwiOjE5NTc5NjMxODU4MDM3NzQ3Mn0iLCJzIjoiMjE4ZWM5MzBjMzVkNjYzMyJ9"><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"><strong><u>Apply here</u></strong></span></a><strong>.</strong></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">The</span><strong>&nbsp;Santander X Awards</strong><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">, are looking for university projects and startups with the potential to grow. Participants gain access to prizes, mentoring, training, and visibility. Applications are open until Sep 11 for </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/14lQgQZKatn?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>startups</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">&nbsp;and&nbsp;</span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/dhQ1KvMD2Uu?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>university students</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">&nbsp;here.&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><strong>Investor Talks </strong>next September 12 &amp; 13 in Portimão. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.investortalks.pt/"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Agenda and tickets available here</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">.</span></p></li><li><p><strong>BSC AI Factory Incubation Programme </strong>in Porto supports startups and SMEs in the development of AI products and projects. Running at UPTEC from 5 October 2026 to 30 March 2027, the programme combines free coworking with specialist support, workshops, networking opportunities and connections to the wider European BSC AI Factory ecosystem. Selected companies can also receive support in identifying the technical, software and computing resources most appropriate to their projects. A<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://form.typeform.com/to/tgWhzCRf?typeform-source=bsc-aifactory.eu">pplications open until Sep 15</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Gathering Design Sprint</strong> is a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.boardingpass.co/gathering-design">4-week virtual sprint</a> teaching founders the craft of designing gatherings people remember, and want to come back to. The next Sprint launches September 14th <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.boardingpass.co/gathering-design">Enroll here</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Portugal Fintech Report </strong>2026 marks 10 years of Portugal Fintech. This special edition of the Report tells the story of the ecosystem we built together, and it sets the stage for the next one. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://forms.fillout.com/t/qxML9JfCLEus">By answering this form</a>, you are applying your Fintech to be featured in the report as one of the top fintechs in Portugal. Fill the form until Sep 15.</p></li><li><p><strong>Access to funding</strong> is a critical factor for startups looking to scale. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://OpportunityHub.eu">OpportunityHub.eu</a> brings together funding opportunities across European countries into a single platform.</p></li><li><p>For all AI builders, 20×20, <strong>RedBridge</strong>’s first PechaKucha-style night. The format is simple and a little unforgiving: 20 slides, 20 seconds each. The deck advances whether you’re ready or not. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ekbau.r.sp1-brevo.net/mk/cl/f/sh/SMK1E8tHeFuBlatR8GYFbzpYxvmC/QK1btIHZjYss">Apply to present, next Sep 17</a></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">The </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eu-japan.eu/">EU-Japan Centre</a><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);"> invites European companies and clusters to apply to the Nanotech Business Mission in Japan in December 2026. The application deadline is 24 September with the mission including participation in </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.nanotechexpo.jp/en/">nano tech 2026</a><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">, a leading Japanese trade fair for advanced materials, processes and enabling technologies. Apply until Sept 24.</span></p></li><li><p>Are you set to make an impact in biotech for planetary health? <strong>Biotope Ventures</strong> want to hear from you. With our program, you'll be able to turn your innovation into a viable business. 350k early-stage funding and a tailored growth journey for biotech startups in planetary health. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://biotope-ventures.com/apply-now/">Applications close on Sep 25</a></p></li><li><p>Is expanding to Portugal your next move? Discover how with Launch in Lisbon! That is exactly what Launch in Lisbon is designed to make easier. The <strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa</strong> program supports international entrepreneurs and companies looking to launch, establish, or expand their operations in Portugal and across Europe. <span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">The program is available in both in-person and virtual formats, although virtual participation provides limited access to the full program. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/V3DPGTNcGrQ?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>Early Bird and virtual tickets are already available here</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">.</span></p></li><li><p><strong>PORTUGAL - EUDIS Hackathon 2026 Autumn</strong>, registration for the EUDIS Hackathon 2026 Autumn is now live! We are thrilled that you are ready to innovate and build with us. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tally.so/r/yPAkyp">Please complete the registration form</a> to submit your application.</p></li><li><p><strong>Start From Knowledge</strong> be the right program for your project? SFN supports the creation and development of knowledge-based startups, helping turn scientific and technological knowledge into solutions with market potential. The program is aimed at projects connected to higher education and research, supporting the journey from knowledge generated within R&amp;D institutions to the creation of new businesses. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ani.pt/start-from-knowledge/">More info here</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Web Summit 26</strong> first <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://websummit.com/speakers/">speakers</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://attend.websummit.com/lis26/schedule">agenda</a> announced</p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">'Hanno: A Magical Tale' Videogame , created by the Madeira based <strong>One Way Eleven</strong>, won 2nd place at FYNG Indie Award 2026.</span></p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚Bridging the gap <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://interoperable-europe.ec.europa.eu/collection/eugovtech/news/back-basics">between public sector and innovators</a> by Bruno Nunes</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.healthcare.digital/single-post/20-future-portuguese-healthtech-and-medtech-leaders">20 Future Portuguese HealthTech and MedTech Leaders</a> by Nelson Advisors</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.entrepreneur.com/starting-a-business/i-learned-5-things-after-facing-over-100-investor-rejections/503595">I Was Rejected By Over 100 Investors Before I Finally Got a ‘Yes’</a> — These Are the 5 Fundraising Truths Every Entrepreneur Needs to Hear</p><p>🎧<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/6txbDwu9cEFG623ppjYkaS?si=s-VjOnjISgOxoJVawifg3g">Dig-In Making Innovation</a>. with Walter Duarte and Nuno Fernandes</p><p>🎧<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/2oXHkQoktq0G9WoEX7ZbY8?si=tcL6s_wgTt-OPfAX2GrMJw">O que faz uma Startup merecer o investimento</a> with Inês de Macedo Santos</p><p>🎬Inside Founder Institute: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jTqFC1j6450">Alumni real stories</a></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Almost back | Week 32</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/almost-back-week-32</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/almost-back-week-32</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 21:51:13 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>Hello everyone, We’re just a few days away from switching back to full power, but the ecosystem is already moving. Even before September officially begins, there’s a growing wave of events, programmes and calls taking shape, early signals that the new season is being prepared with intention. For…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3>Hello everyone,</h3><p>We’re just a few days away from switching back to full power, but the ecosystem is already moving. Even before September officially begins, there’s a growing wave of events, programmes and calls taking shape, early signals that the new season is being prepared with intention.</p><p>For those who like to get ahead of the curve, this week brings a handful of opportunities worth noting, as the community quietly warms up for what’s looking like a strong return.</p><p>Take a look at the '<u>Highlights of the Week</u>' with the next deadlines not to be missed. </p><p>A mention to <strong>José Epifânio da França</strong>. His passing leaves a meaningful mark on Portugal’s innovation community. </p><p>See you in September<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“Well begun is half done.”</p><p>Aristotle  </p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><strong>Founder Institute's Pitch Your Ideas to Investors &amp; Experts</strong>, Online. Got a startup or idea? Join this interactive online event to get live feedback from top investors and experts. To pre-submit your 3min' pitch, </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeXC0Fp2WaZcrMIXeGpdciulbOvBs-ej-JWUf-qm-xg_wXpzw/viewform"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">visit this link</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> and </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/event/pitch-your-ideas-to-investors-experts-online-portugal-fall-2026."><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">apply until Aug 28</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> 10:00 AM.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">Applications for the</span><strong> Fall Batch ’26</strong><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);"> of <strong>Unicorn Factory</strong> </span><strong>Incubation Program</strong><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">, for early-stage startups, are now open. Receive mentorship tailored to your project’s needs, participate in training sessions, access a network of over 190 mentors, and connect with 150 investors and corporate partners. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/jaISlWytDAr?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>Apply by September 6 here</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);">The 11th edition of </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://boqvbrp.clicks.mlsend.com/ty/c/eyJ2Ijoie1wiYVwiOjE3ODkxMjUsXCJsXCI6MTk1Nzk2MzA0NDQyNDI2NjE1LFwiclwiOjE5NTc5NjMxODU4MDM3NzQ3Mn0iLCJzIjoiNzc5OTQ0OTRlMTc0Y2E4MyJ9"><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"><strong><u>Road 2 Web Summit</u></strong></span></a><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"> by <strong>Startup Portugal</strong> is open. Up to </span>125 Portuguese startups<span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"> get an intensive bootcamp in Porto and Lisbon, a discount on their Web Summit package, and a shot at the Galp prizes. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://boqvbrp.clicks.mlsend.com/ty/c/eyJ2Ijoie1wiYVwiOjE3ODkxMjUsXCJsXCI6MTk1Nzk2MzA0NDQ5NzY2NjQ4LFwiclwiOjE5NTc5NjMxODU4MDM3NzQ3Mn0iLCJzIjoiMjE4ZWM5MzBjMzVkNjYzMyJ9"><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"><strong><u>Apply here</u></strong></span></a><strong>.</strong></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">The</span><strong>&nbsp;Santander X Awards</strong><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">, are looking for university projects and startups with the potential to grow. Participants gain access to prizes, mentoring, training, and visibility. Applications are open until Sep 11 for </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/14lQgQZKatn?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>startups</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">&nbsp;and&nbsp;</span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/dhQ1KvMD2Uu?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>university students</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">&nbsp;here.&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><strong>Instituto Pedro Nunes</strong> is selecting 12 Startups for Websummit 26. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://forms.gle/ U1ykD5JT4146WecVA "><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Apply here until Sep 15</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">.</span></p></li><li><p><strong>BSC AI Factory Incubation Programme </strong>in Porto supports startups and SMEs in the development of AI products and projects. Running at UPTEC from 5 October 2026 to 30 March 2027, the programme combines free coworking with specialist support, workshops, networking opportunities and connections to the wider European BSC AI Factory ecosystem. Selected companies can also receive support in identifying the technical, software and computing resources most appropriate to their projects. A<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://form.typeform.com/to/tgWhzCRf?typeform-source=bsc-aifactory.eu">pplications open until Sep 15</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Gathering Design Sprint</strong> is a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.boardingpass.co/gathering-design">4-week virtual sprint</a> teaching founders the craft of designing gatherings people remember, and want to come back to. The next Sprint launches September 14th <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.boardingpass.co/gathering-design">Enroll here</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Access to funding</strong> is a critical factor for startups looking to scale. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://OpportunityHub.eu">OpportunityHub.eu</a> brings together funding opportunities across European countries into a single platform.</p></li><li><p>For all AI builders, 20×20, <strong>RedBridge</strong>’s first PechaKucha-style night. The format is simple and a little unforgiving: 20 slides, 20 seconds each. The deck advances whether you’re ready or not. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ekbau.r.sp1-brevo.net/mk/cl/f/sh/SMK1E8tHeFuBlatR8GYFbzpYxvmC/QK1btIHZjYss">Apply to present, next Sep 17</a></p></li><li><p>Is expanding to Portugal your next move? Discover how with Launch in Lisbon! That is exactly what Launch in Lisbon is designed to make easier. The <strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa</strong> program supports international entrepreneurs and companies looking to launch, establish, or expand their operations in Portugal and across Europe. <span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">The program is available in both in-person and virtual formats, although virtual participation provides limited access to the full program. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/V3DPGTNcGrQ?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>Early Bird and virtual tickets are already available here</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">.</span></p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/">Applications open</a> for the <strong>Founder Institute</strong> next cohort, starting in October</p></li><li><p><strong>PORTUGAL - EUDIS Hackathon 2026 Autumn</strong>, registration for the EUDIS Hackathon 2026 Autumn is now live! We are thrilled that you are ready to innovate and build with us. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tally.so/r/yPAkyp">Please complete the registration form</a> to submit your application.</p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><strong>Insurtech LucidHorizon </strong>launched MimicTask.</p></li><li><p>Startup Leiria will take the following Startups to Startup Summit in Florianopolis:  <strong>Enline</strong>; <strong>Coalex.ai</strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://coalex.ai">; </a><strong>Deeploy</strong>; <strong>sheerME</strong> ; and <strong>Good Casting</strong>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Startup Portimão</strong> celebrates it's 10th anniversary.</p></li><li><p><strong>GreenDash</strong> won best project award for 'Empreendedorismo Ambiental, Sustentabilidade e Transição Energética' powered by 𝗟𝘂𝘀𝗼𝗽𝗼𝗻𝘁𝗲!</p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚</p><p>🎧<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/3iYsbVDLFpbuhNZW5cdld9?si=QLchRXolSNCZk3LtmuPo-g">Conversas empreendedoras</a> com José Epifânio da França</p><p>🎧<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/3KzmNxE18bpsABijF6Ej5Q?si=lzbp4FfUR0GZwrzYhtFUyQ">Hospital da Luz 10 MINUTOS DE INOVAÇÃO</a>, falamos com Bernardo Tavares, CTO da Granter, e com Rita Ramos, a gestora deste projeto na equipa de investigação do Hospital da Luz Learning Health.</p><p>🎬<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/EfJbbxust_c?si=Nn3fQTHb4pESLVd9">why no roi in ai</a>? with Matteo Cassese </p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Are we back? Not yet | Week 31</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/are-we-back-not-yet-week-31</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/are-we-back-not-yet-week-31</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 22:14:11 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>Hello everyone, Hope you’re having a great summer; whether you unplugged completely, travelled, or finally caught up on some long‑overdue sleep. I’m making a brief August appearance because there are a few events and calls worth your attention. Even in the heat, the ecosystem is showing early signs…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3>Hello everyone,</h3><p>Hope you’re having a great summer; whether you unplugged completely, travelled, or finally caught up on some long‑overdue sleep. I’m making a brief August appearance because there are a few events and calls worth your attention. Even in the heat, the ecosystem is showing early signs of gearing up for a strong September.</p><p>If you’re still looking for what to read before the break ends, take the summer suggestions from João Silva, Gabriela Faria, and Rui Quinta; <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/posts/summer-readings-week-29">here</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/posts/as-august-approaches-week-30">here</a>.</p><p>Take a look at the 'Highlights of the Week' with the next deadlines not to be missed. </p><p>See you in September<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“What good is the warmth of summer, without the cold of winter to give it sweetness.”</p><p>John Steinbeck</p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p>Last call for <strong>Tourism Advance</strong> applications. Powered by Fábrica de Startups and supported by Turismo de Portugal, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.tourismadvance.pt/">Tourism Advance</a> is an open innovation programme that connects startups with hospitality companies seeking innovative solutions to address real business challenges. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://www.tourismadvance.pt"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Applications close 23 Aug</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><strong>Founder Institute's Pitch Your Ideas to Investors &amp; Experts</strong>, Online. Got a startup or idea? Join this interactive online event to get live feedback from top investors and experts. To pre-submit your 3min' pitch, </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeXC0Fp2WaZcrMIXeGpdciulbOvBs-ej-JWUf-qm-xg_wXpzw/viewform"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">visit this link</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> and </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/event/pitch-your-ideas-to-investors-experts-online-portugal-fall-2026."><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">apply until Aug 28</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> 10:00 AM.</span></p></li><li><p>Fall Batch ’26 of the <strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa Incubation Program</strong> is looking for early-stage startups. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/10l5DecMUzX?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>Apply until Sep 6</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);">The 11th edition of </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://boqvbrp.clicks.mlsend.com/ty/c/eyJ2Ijoie1wiYVwiOjE3ODkxMjUsXCJsXCI6MTk1Nzk2MzA0NDQyNDI2NjE1LFwiclwiOjE5NTc5NjMxODU4MDM3NzQ3Mn0iLCJzIjoiNzc5OTQ0OTRlMTc0Y2E4MyJ9"><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"><strong><u>Road 2 Web Summit</u></strong></span></a><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"> by <strong>Startup Portugal</strong> is open. Up to </span>125 Portuguese startups<span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"> get an intensive bootcamp in Porto and Lisbon, a discount on their Web Summit package, and a shot at the Galp prizes. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://boqvbrp.clicks.mlsend.com/ty/c/eyJ2Ijoie1wiYVwiOjE3ODkxMjUsXCJsXCI6MTk1Nzk2MzA0NDQ5NzY2NjQ4LFwiclwiOjE5NTc5NjMxODU4MDM3NzQ3Mn0iLCJzIjoiMjE4ZWM5MzBjMzVkNjYzMyJ9"><span style="color: rgb(81, 88, 86);"><strong><u>Apply here</u></strong></span></a><strong>.</strong></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">The</span><strong>&nbsp;Santander X Awards</strong><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">, are looking for university projects and startups with the potential to grow. Participants gain access to prizes, mentoring, training, and visibility. Applications are open until Sep 11 for </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/14lQgQZKatn?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>startups</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">&nbsp;and&nbsp;</span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/dhQ1KvMD2Uu?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>university students</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">&nbsp;here.&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><strong>Instituto Pedro Nunes</strong> is selecting 12 Startups for Websummit 26. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://forms.gle/ U1ykD5JT4146WecVA "><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Apply here until Sep 15</span></a><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">.</span></p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://351startups.com/portugal-community-fund/">apply for the</a> <strong>Lisboa’s Community Fund</strong>. The community fund is a shared basket of money and resources that local communities can draw on to carry out their activities or organize events. Administered by 351 Startups, the Community Fund will allow several smaller communities in Portugal to develop and become more active.</p></li><li><p><strong>Gathering Design Sprint</strong> is a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.boardingpass.co/gathering-design">4-week virtual sprint</a> teaching founders the craft of designing gatherings people remember, and want to come back to. The next Sprint launches September 14th <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.boardingpass.co/gathering-design">Enroll here</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Access to funding</strong> is a critical factor for startups looking to scale. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://OpportunityHub.eu">OpportunityHub.eu</a> brings together funding opportunities across European countries into a single platform.</p></li><li><p>For all AI builders, 20×20, <strong>RedBridge</strong>’s first PechaKucha-style night. The format is simple and a little unforgiving: 20 slides, 20 seconds each. The deck advances whether you’re ready or not. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ekbau.r.sp1-brevo.net/mk/cl/f/sh/SMK1E8tHeFuBlatR8GYFbzpYxvmC/QK1btIHZjYss">Apply to present, next Sep 17</a></p></li><li><p>Is expanding to Portugal your next move? Discover how with Launch in Lisbon! That is exactly what Launch in Lisbon is designed to make easier. The <strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa</strong> program supports international entrepreneurs and companies looking to launch, establish, or expand their operations in Portugal and across Europe. <span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">The program is available in both in-person and virtual formats, although virtual participation provides limited access to the full program. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://us.list-manage.com/V3DPGTNcGrQ?e=2abddbe8a8&amp;c2id=259d014ea392169934a44d27a84120f5"><u>Early Bird and virtual tickets are already available here</u></a><span style="color: rgb(32, 32, 32);">.</span></p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/">Applications open</a> for the <strong>Founder Institute</strong> next cohort, starting in October</p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><strong>Tekever </strong>kicks off 500M funding round for a 5.5B evaluation</p></li><li><p> <strong>Neuraspace</strong> raised 15,6M</p></li><li><p><strong>OPNOVA</strong> won Startup Spotlight na Black Hat</p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sapo.pt/autores/carlos-resende">Ecossistema portugues</a> by Carlos Resende</p><p>🎧Max Hodak explains how the company buys things and hires people, and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.ycrootaccess.com/p/max-hodak-there-are-no-blanket-rules">why those systems determine how fast it can move</a>.</p><p>🎧<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/55rFW5WnJI8IL9CFIqr2kY?si=9tII_l2IT_mhr1Rxps2WtQ">How to Design</a> in the Agent Era</p><p>🎬Your startup will take everything you give to it. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/F42HcNDHgi8?si=gIsFC3h9ZjBUHuyW">Make it count</a> | Yan Simard<br><span style="color: rgb(15, 15, 15);"><strong> </strong></span></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>As August Approaches | Week 30</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/as-august-approaches-week-30</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/as-august-approaches-week-30</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 15:51:28 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>And the ecosystem keeps reading. There’s a moment, right before summer fully arrives, when the ecosystem enters a softer gear. This week follows that same cadence. Less noise, more clarity. And because reading is one of the few forms of rest that also expands us, we continue our summer ritual:…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3>And the ecosystem keeps reading.</h3><p>There’s a moment, right before summer fully arrives, when the ecosystem enters a softer gear. This week follows that same cadence. Less noise, more clarity. And because reading is one of the few forms of rest that also expands us, we continue our summer ritual: asking people we admire to share the books they believe are worth carrying into the break; to the beach, the countryside, or that café where no one knows us.</p><p>The result remains what <strong>Adamastor</strong> loves most: diverse, thoughtful, and refreshingly unaligned. The ecosystem grows when it reads outside its own bubble.</p><p><span><strong>Rui Quinta — <em>I Am a Strange Loop</em>, Douglas Hofstadter</strong>  <br>A brilliant and strange exploration of consciousness, identity, and the construction of the self. Hofstadter blends logic, mathematics, and humanity with rare sensitivity. A book about empathy, about what we absorb from others and what we never fully become.</span></p><p><span><strong>Gabriela Faria — <em>Born a Crime</em>, Trevor Noah</strong>  <br>Trevor Noah’s improbable, painful, and hilarious story of growing up “illegal” under apartheid. For Gabriela, born in South Africa, the book resonates deeply but its humanity and humour are universal.</span></p><p><span><strong>João Silva — <em>Magnifica Humanitas</em>, Pope Leo XIV</strong>  <br>A timely reflection on AI, human dignity, and what must remain specifically human. Regardless of faith, it offers scale and depth in a moment of technological acceleration.</span></p><p><span><strong>João Silva — <em>O Louco de Deus no Fim do Mundo</em>, Javier Cercas</strong>  <br>Still on his reading list, but Cercas is always a reliable companion for anyone who wants literature that thinks while it entertains.</span></p><p><span><strong>Carlos Resende — <em>O Riso de Deus</em>, António Alçada Baptista</strong>  <br>A book that doesn’t teach you how to build a company, it teaches you how to live. Doubt as a healthy force, serenity as strength, and laughter (even divine laughter) as intelligence.</span></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“Risk more than others think is safe. Dream more than others think is practical.”</p><p>Howard Schultz</p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p><strong>WebSummit</strong> 26 announced <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://websummit.com/speakers/">the first speakers</a> Among are names like Michele Catasta, President &amp; Head of AI, Replit; Marcus Segal, Partner, Andreessen Horowitz; and Jen Wong, COO, Reddit.</p></li><li><p><strong>Scaling Up</strong> is <strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa</strong>'s flagship program for post-seed scaleups ready to grow, raise Series A/B, or expand internationally. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.f6s.com/scalingupbyunicornfactorylisboa/apply">Applications open until July 31.</a></p></li><li><p><strong>Proof-of-Concept Co-Financing Instrument. EIT Food's</strong> Co-Financing Instrument aids agrifood startups by de-risking pilot projects and promoting innovation and collaboration with industry leaders. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eitfood.eu/open-calls/proof-of-concept-co-financing-instrument-2">Apply until</a> Jul 31</p></li><li><p><strong>Mobility &amp; Tourism Innovations Tirol</strong> is a Europe-wide innovation initiative looking for ready-to-implement solutions that will shape the future of tourism mobility in Tirol and the Austrian Alps. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://f7ce1.r.sp1-brevo.net/mk/cl/f/sh/6rqJfgq8dIUQXqxfW5O5jSMp8fY/63VGbvH38Y8Y">Apply until</a> Jul 31</p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">Applications for the </span><strong>2026 Prémios PME Pitch</strong><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);"> are now open. If you have an innovative solution and the ambition to scale it, this is your moment to put it in front of the right people. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://lp.pmemagazine.com/l/3BHw0dABF1112/">5.000eur + visibility are worth it, apply here</a><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">.</span></p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://351startups.com/portugal-community-fund/">apply for the</a> <strong>Lisboa’s Community Fund</strong>. The community fund is a shared basket of money and resources that local communities can draw on to carry out their activities or organize events. Administered by 351 Startups, the Community Fund will allow several smaller communities in Portugal to develop and become more active.</p></li><li><p><strong>Gathering Design Sprint</strong> is a 4-week virtual sprint teaching founders the craft of designing gatherings people remember, and want to come back to. The next Sprint launches September 14th <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.boardingpass.co/gathering-design">Enroll here</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Overcome the Impostor Phenomenon</strong>. Claim your space in Tech. Discover your Potential. Shape your identity in tech. The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://TechID.ai">TechID.ai</a> Journey is a 100% social and completely free practical laboratory, designed to accelerate employability for more women in technology. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://techid.ponts.network/">Secure your spot</a>.</p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/">Applications open</a> for the <strong>Founder Institute</strong> next cohort, starting in October</p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><strong>Code for All </strong>listed at TIME World's Top EdTech Companies of 2026</p></li><li><p><strong>Cascade </strong>raised +3M with Índico Capital Partners, Andreessen Horowitz Speedrun and Ada Ventures</p></li><li><p><strong>Lampsy</strong> and <strong>Manie</strong> among the Top 50 of the VDS Startup Competition 2026</p><p></p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sapo.pt/autores/carlos-resende">Ecossistema portugues</a> by Carlos Resende</p><p>📚ESNA Compendium Volume V: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.esnalliance.eu/reports">IP &amp; Tech Transfer</a></p><p>📚Top <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://time.com/article/2026/07/22/worlds-top-edtech-companies-2026/">Ed Tech companies</a> </p><p>📚Top 50 of the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://vds.tech/news/top-50-startups-vds-2026/">VDS Startup Competition</a> 2026</p><p>🎧Nina's notes <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/show/4iwD64Mwp16Bq8u5EHeQLv">podcast</a></p><p>🎧Are You VC-able? <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.buzzsprout.com/2224511/episodes/17859844">Hard Truths About Startup Funding</a></p><p>🎬<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_ZQBXi_Elgw">Inovação por Pacientes: A fonte inexplorada de ideias revolucionárias</a>  (Patient Innovation: The untapped source of breakthrough ideas) with Giordano Koch and Pedro Oliveira<br><span style="color: rgb(15, 15, 15);"><strong> </strong></span></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Summer readings | Week 29</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/summer-readings-week-29</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/summer-readings-week-29</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 15:25:03 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>The weeks before summer break have a particular rhythm. The ecosystem slows down just enough for us to notice the things we usually miss: the conversations that linger, the ideas that finally breathe, the founders who admit, without guilt, that they need a pause. Next editions follows that cadence.…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>The weeks before summer break have a particular rhythm. The ecosystem slows down just enough for us to notice the things we usually miss: the conversations that linger, the ideas that finally breathe, the founders who admit, without guilt, that they need a pause.</p><p>Next editions follows that cadence. Less noise, more clarity. And because summer is the one moment when reading becomes a form of recovery, I invited a few people I admire to share the books they believe are worth carrying into the break; worth taking to the beach, the countryside, or that café where no one knows us.</p><p>The result is exactly what I hoped for: diverse, thoughtful, and refreshingly unaligned. The ecosystem grows when it reads outside its own bubble.</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/gabriela-faria-6275878b/"><strong>Gabriela Faria</strong></a><strong> Founder at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/lisbonprojectassociation/"><strong>Lisbon Project</strong></a><strong> — <em>Necessary Endings</em>, Henry Cloud</strong> A clear-eyed guide to difficult decisions: people, projects, and relationships that must end for growth to happen. As Gabriela puts it, <em>“what got us here won’t get us there.”</em></p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rquinta/"><span><strong>Rui Quinta</strong></span></a><span><strong> Co-Founder at  </strong></span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/withcompany/"><span><strong>With Company</strong></span></a><span><strong> — <em>Designerly Ways of Knowing</em>, Nigel Cross</strong> <br>A foundational work for anyone who wants to understand design not just as practice, but as a way of knowing and acting in the world. For Rui, it also carries a personal note: Nigel Cross himself was in the audience when he first shared this idea.</span></p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/joaospvz/"><strong>João Silva</strong></a><strong> Head of Data &amp; Tech at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/startupportugal/"><strong>StartUp Portugal</strong></a><strong> — <em>Lamento de uma América em Ruínas</em>, J. D. Vance</strong>  A raw portrait of the Rust Belt’s working-class families and the wounds that shape worldviews, votes, and resentments. For João, it’s essential reading for anyone trying to understand how narratives form, and why that matters for technology and AI.</p><p>And I included one of my own; <strong><em>Principles: Life and Work, Ray Dalio</em></strong> A book that teaches the discipline of clarity. For anyone building something ( startup, team, life) it’s a reminder that good judgment is rarely accidental and almost always the result of deliberate thinking.</p><p>We’ll be here next week, with some more of our guests’ suggestions. </p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><strong>“Great founders move fast, make decisions, and don't wait for permission.”</strong></p><p><strong>Sam Altman</strong></p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p>Call for Founders! <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://STUDIOS.PT"><strong>STUDIOS.PT</strong></a><strong> - Portuguese Venture Studio Association</strong> is launching the program "Build With…" It's a matchmaking initiative between founders and venture studios to actually building together. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://studios.pt/buildwith/">Applications open until July 24.</a></p></li><li><p><strong>ETH Global</strong> Come build our decentralized future in Lisbon. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ethglobal.com/auth?use_redirect=/events/lisbon2026/apply?ref=H734NIIBRQ">Apply to attend next July 24</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>WebSummit</strong> 26 announced <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://websummit.com/speakers/">the first speakers</a> Among are names like Michele Catasta, President &amp; Head of AI, Replit; Marcus Segal, Partner, Andreessen Horowitz; and Jen Wong, COO, Reddit.</p></li><li><p><strong>Scaling Up</strong> is Unicorn Factory Lisboa's flagship program for post-seed scaleups ready to grow, raise Series A/B, or expand internationally. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.f6s.com/scalingupbyunicornfactorylisboa/apply">Applications open until July 31.</a></p></li><li><p><strong>Tourism Advance</strong> by Fábrica de Startups &amp; Turismo de Portugal, this open innovation programme connects startups with hospitality companies seeking innovative solutions to address real business challenges. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.tourismadvance.pt/">Find out more here.</a></p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.techstars.com/techstars-eit-urban-mobility-founder-catalyst">Techstars x EIT Urban Mobility Founder Catalyst</a>. Applications open until Aug 26.</p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/safety/go/?url=https%3A%2F%2Faltalab%2Eai%2Fapply&amp;urlhash=C2zP&amp;mt=61tdFu8yQ6X_wGPVRGM3LJ_pw219tjAyToc_b-PyCn59-9iiyoeDM_lt_ts8-I52gxZantYKXeagPB-cjzYEbyKwwEaU_qbYsJj6ebGwWuV4c_VVfIpLWtVX&amp;isSdui=true">AltaLab is not a typical accelerator</a>. Selected teams get direct, hands-on support from the AltaLab and AltaIR Capital team and the strongest have a path to funding of up to $50K or $500K, depending on their stage and progress. Starts Sep 07.</p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><strong>Cozecare</strong> received an Honourable Mention in the Sustainability and Social Impact category at the Prémio Nacional de Inovação 2026; <strong>Augusto Costa Franco</strong> of Sigma Easy Charge, was the public’s top‑voted winner of the Innovation Champion Trophy, while the Jury selected <strong>Nuno Sebastiao</strong>, Feedzai for the Personality Award.</p></li><li><p>Leiria City Council will invest €7,500 to integrate the solutions of <strong>Guide Sofia</strong>, <strong>Leiria Concierge</strong>, and <strong>Work from Leiria</strong> into its tourist routes.</p></li><li><p> Hephaesnus raised 400k.</p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sapo.pt/artigo/empreender-cansa-o-custo-emocional-de-construir-uma-startup-6a553f3ee2e253d69e8d0cac">Empreender cansa: o custo emocional de construir uma startup</a> by Carlos Resende</p><p>📚Após a queda da Unbabel, a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://dinheirovivo.dn.pt/economia/aps-a-queda-da-unbabel-a-ia-nacional-resiste-e-prepara-150-milhes-em-exportaes">IA nacional resiste</a> e prepara 150 milhões em exportações</p><p>📚European <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://data.europa.eu/data/datasets">data sets</a></p><p>📚Why You <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://weareoutcome.co/blog/why-you-shouldnt-have-an-innovation-portfolio-according-to-hbr/">Shouldn’t Have An Innovation Portfolio</a> (according to HBR)</p><p>🎧<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/6XvJy9EYbZUGiA5JOY6hWh">AI For Real</a>: Is audio the next AI interface w/ Angelo Giacco (ElevenLabs)</p><p>🎧The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/3pDRSdBa33D4B8HMfWWT3g">Most Expensive Money</a> You'll Ever Raise w/ Wallen founder of business travel platform Engine </p><p>🎬<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/I_RVjSFfy1s?si=TVtgJK0RmD4np1jI">Three Money Stories You Need To Tell</a> by Rich Mironov author of "Money Stories", at Productized Conference 2026</p><p>🎬<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/j0GEt4d-2Ic?si=-0iX1H5Q4kKmbTNL">A Regra Estoica Que Salva Qualquer Empreendedor De Enlouquecer</a> c/ André Dionísio, ByTheLaw</p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Entrepreneurial DNA | Week 28</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/entrepreneurial-dna-week-28</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/entrepreneurial-dna-week-28</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 20:52:20 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>What makes someone a true entrepreneur? Is it resilience, creativity, risk tolerance or a bit of everything, deeply wired into who they are? This week marks the final stretch of the Founder Institute batch. It’s always a fascinating moment. Before the program begins, many founders aren’t sure if…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>What makes someone a true entrepreneur? Is it resilience, creativity, risk tolerance or a bit of everything, deeply wired into who they are?</p><p>This week marks the final stretch of the Founder Institute batch. It’s always a fascinating moment. Before the program begins, many founders aren’t sure if they “have what it takes”. And then, somewhere between the pressure, the feedback, the pivots and the uncomfortable honesty, they start to see it or at least get a first glimpse of their entrepreneurial DNA.</p><p>That's why I want to explore the idea of "Entrepreneurial DNA" not as a buzzword, but as a serious question every founder should ask themselves. One tool I really appreciate is the Entrepreneur DNA Assessment from the Founder Institute, designed to evaluate core personality traits statistically linked to startup success. It focuses on things like fluid intelligence, openness, bravery, and even emotional stability.</p><p>Why does this matter? Because being a founder isn’t just about having a great idea. It’s about handling uncertainty, persisting through failure, and leading with clarity when the path is anything but clear. These traits aren't always visible on a CV but they often determine who thrives and who burns out.</p><p>So this week, I challenge you to reflect:</p><ul><li><p>Do you know your strengths and blind spots as a founder?</p></li><li><p>Have you ever taken a personality-based startup assessment?</p></li><li><p>Are you building a team that complements your DNA?</p></li></ul><p>Whether you're just getting started or deep in the grind, understanding the psychology of entrepreneurship is a huge unlock.</p><p>Looking forward to hearing what you discover.</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><strong>“The biggest risk is not taking any risk.” </strong></p><p><strong>Mark Zuckerberg</strong></p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.canopy.community/">Canopy Community</a> launches "<strong>Startup Summer</strong>". A flexible six-week programme helping first-time founders turn ideas into reality. A global programme designed for aspiring entrepreneurs balancing work, family and everyday life. Program commences July 20. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.canopy.community/offers/Ba2xyBGt/checkout">Applications are open</a>.</p></li><li><p>Call for Founders! <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://STUDIOS.PT"><strong>STUDIOS.PT</strong></a><strong> - Portuguese Venture Studio Association</strong> is launching the program "Build With…" It's a matchmaking initiative between founders and venture studios to actually building together. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://studios.pt/buildwith/">Applications open until July 24.</a></p></li><li><p><strong>Applied AI Hackathon</strong>: Law firm C-suite execs are flying in from the US specifically for this event to judge the demos, alongside Portuguese startup founders and AI influencers. ​The perks: ​$2,000 prize pool; ​Free drinks + food at the Ritz-Carlton venue; ​Transportation from Lisbon to Sintra covered; ​Stand-out performers get fast-tracked interviews at Swans (typically a &lt;0.5% funnel); ​A portfolio project you pitch live to US execs (for your CV). <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/gmyuby6v?utm_source=carlos-resende">Applications open until July 17</a>.</p></li><li><p>Applications for <strong>Portugal at SF Tech Week 2026</strong> close July 15. If you're a Portuguese founder past validation and thinking seriously about the US market — this is the most structured, connected path to get there. 5 to 10 spots. Fully funded (travel and transportation extra). <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sftechweek.redbridgelisbon.com/">A selection committee of investors and operators with direct Silicon Valley experience reviewing every application</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>ETH Global</strong> Come build our decentralized future in Lisbon. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ethglobal.com/auth?use_redirect=/events/lisbon2026/apply?ref=H734NIIBRQ">Apply to attend next July 24</a>.</p></li><li><p>Applications for the <strong>2026 Prémios PME Pitch</strong> are now open. If you have an innovative solution and the ambition to scale it, this is your moment to put it in front of the right people. Finalists get to present at the 2026 PME Magazine - Portugal.Mundo.Empresas Forum, alongside entrepreneurs, investors, partners and business leaders. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://lp.pmemagazine.com/l/3BHw0dABF1112/">5.000eur + visibility are worth it, apply here</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>WebSummit</strong> 26 announced <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://websummit.com/speakers/">the first speakers</a> Among are names like Michele Catasta, President &amp; Head of AI, Replit; Marcus Segal, Partner, Andreessen Horowitz; and Jen Wong, COO, Reddit </p></li><li><p><strong>Scaling Up</strong> is Unicorn Factory Lisboa's flagship program for post-seed scaleups ready to grow, raise Series A/B, or expand internationally. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.f6s.com/scalingupbyunicornfactorylisboa/apply">Applications open until July 31</a></p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><strong>ESNA</strong> officially launched <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://OpportunityHub.eu">OpportunityHub.eu.</a></p></li><li><p><strong>OWL Places</strong> won the Católica Santander Award.</p></li><li><p><strong>Xarp</strong> winner of the Fashion Innovation Call Pitch Competition by Portugal Fashion, with a project developing AI-powered extended reality solutions for retail. </p></li><li><p><strong>TEKEVER</strong> acquired <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://cloudsweep.ai">cloudsweep.ai.</a></p></li><li><p><strong>Eng8</strong>, <strong>DeepNeurotic</strong>, <strong>Future Voltaics</strong>, and <strong>ZeroPact</strong> awarded at Prio Jump Start.</p></li><li><p><strong>PhycoFerm</strong> (Food, Health/Medical) with funding from NXW - Nutrition from Water.</p><p></p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sapo.pt/artigo/empreender-cansa-o-custo-emocional-de-construir-uma-startup-6a553f3ee2e253d69e8d0cac">Empreender cansa: o custo emocional de construir uma startup</a> by Carlos Resende</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/code-cheap-part-taste-expensive-one-rui-barroca-n1mhe/">The code was the cheap part. Taste was the expensive one</a>. by Rui Barroca</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://flicktalks.substack.com/p/the-interlude-aisle-one-board-evolved">The Interlude Aisle: One Board, Evolved</a> by Ary Prieto and Simão Manuel (Attach)</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://shiftdiaries.substack.com/p/ai-will-assist-the-humanities-stem">AI will assist the humanities</a>. STEM will assist AI.</p><p>📚EU Inc: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://alliedforstartups.org/wp-content/uploads/EU-Inc_-Cant-Touch-This-Red-Lines.pdf">Can’t Touch This - Red Lines</a></p><p>🎧What's Mext: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/4LJCnVu2RyGndPmNo3XkJO?si=5ntoGO4XS4iErhbb5AaFgA">How do ecosystems accelerate innovation and create real impact?</a> with Gil Azevedo </p><p>🎧Diane Brady and Kristin Stoller<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/5dqm2lj6fi2TLmaaunYuia"> recap the year’s defining themes on Leadership Next - from CEO wellness and “leaders as athletes"</a></p><p>🎬<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a722F3yPwWk">Captar investimento e lidar com investidores</a> com Virgilio Bento (Sword) e Rodrigo Fernandes (Augusta Labs)</p><p>🎬Founder Tales <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/p2n_O0WCwWI?si=MDs8tAZCeIj8fiZy">com Vicente Garção</a> (Lampsy)</p><p>🎬Productized: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xtS7pSMEknU">O Fim da Velocidade: Estratégia de Produto Quando a Rapidez é uma Commodity</a> with Krasi Bozhinkova</p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Heat Wave | Week 27</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/heat-wave-week-27</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/heat-wave-week-27</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 17:58:02 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>When Summer Stops Being Just Summer Across Europe, temperatures are climbing again, and it’s not only the weather charts that are spiking; it’s operational costs, productivity dips, and the general strain on teams. Extreme heat has quietly become a structural factor in how companies operate. Recent…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3>When Summer Stops Being Just Summer</h3><p>Across Europe, temperatures are climbing again, and it’s not only the weather charts that are spiking; it’s operational costs, productivity dips, and the general strain on teams. Extreme heat has quietly become a structural factor in how companies operate. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/07/04/quente-demais-para-trabalhar-ondas-de-calor-baixam-produtividade/">Recent studies</a> continue to underline the trend: days above 30 °C consistently reduce daily revenue and operating profit, and prolonged heat spells shave off annual productivity in ways that compound over time.</p><p>For startups, the impact is sharper. Smaller teams, tighter resources, improvised offices, distributed operations, every extra degree adds friction. Momentum fades, decision‑making slows, and execution suffers. And there’s that familiar paradox: many of the founders most exposed to the problem are the ones building solutions for it.</p><p>But this is where summer stops being just a risk and becomes a market signal. Demand for climate‑monitoring tools, smart infrastructure, energy efficiency systems, resilient agriculture, and adaptive work environments is rising faster than supply. Heat isn’t only a warning, it’s a roadmap. Founders building at the intersection of technology and climate adaptation are finding real traction.</p><p>Portugal is quietly positioning itself in this space. Our climate‑tech scene is more diverse, more technical, and more ambitious: renewable energy, storage, EV infrastructure, circularity, biotech, precision agriculture, ocean tech. Companies like Windcredible, Bandora, MicroHarvest, Wisecrop, Powerdot, Cleanwatts, Raiz Vertical, Inductiva, Seedsight, AddVolt, Manie, humiverso, Kencko, Oceano Fresco, Wisecrop, YData and PFX Biotech show that we’re not just reacting.</p><p>And as the climate heats up, the calendar does too. July arrives with a strong lineup of events, talks, gatherings, and chances to breathe the ecosystem; before heading off to a beach, a shady garden, or a café with reliable A/C and a cold drink. Summer is no longer just a season; it’s a stress test for teams, an accelerator for innovation, and, for those reading the signals, a clear opportunity to build where the world needs it most.</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><strong>"In the midst of winter, I found there was, within me, an invincible summer."</strong> </p><p><strong>Albert Camus</strong></p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p><strong>WebSummit</strong> 26 announced <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://websummit.com/speakers/">the first speakers</a> Among are names like Michele Catasta, President &amp; Head of AI, Replit; Marcus Segal, Partner, Andreessen Horowitz; and Jen Wong, COO, Reddit </p></li><li><p><strong>Co-working Day for Designers + Mentoring</strong> by LisboaUX, this Friday at Casa do Impacto</p></li><li><p><strong>Portugal Tech Week</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://351startups.com/become-volunteer/">is looking for new volunteers</a> to help prepare the biggest edition of the event yet.</p></li><li><p>Finding relevant startup programs, grants, pilot opportunities, events can be time-consuming.  Not anymore, <strong>Build Up Labs</strong> built the<strong> </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startuptools.builduplabs.com/founder-opportunities/"><strong>Founder Opportunities</strong> search tool</a>. It brings together open programs, funding opportunities, networking events, new perks, and visibility opportunities curated by us and our AI agents for our founders community and the wider startup ecosystem in Portugal.</p></li><li><p>A new platform for Europe's startup ecosystem. <strong>ESNA</strong> launched  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://OpportunityHub.eu">OpportunityHub.eu</a>, a digital gateway connecting talent, founders and investors with opportunities across Europe.</p></li><li><p><strong>Tech Foundry Portugal</strong> -<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupportugal.com/programs/tech-foundry-portugal-deep-tech-edition/">new deadline</a>- July 10.</p></li><li><p><strong>Tourism Advance</strong> is an open innovation program that connects startups with companies in the hospitality sector seeking solutions to address real business challenges. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.tourismadvance.pt/">Applications open</a> until Aug 23.</p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://upin.up.pt/pt-pt/content/bip-proof-20252026-candidaturas-abertas">Applications for BIP PROOF are now open</a>. The program supporting proof‑of‑concept projects across the University of Porto’s research and innovation ecosystem will award €10,000 to each selected project. Applications are open until Aug 3rd.</p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><strong>BRAINR</strong> has secured a 1.5M investment from Portugal Ventures, extending its record-breaking 11M seed round.</p></li><li><p><strong>Sound Particles</strong>, and <strong>Nutrivalley</strong> raised  +1.5M</p></li><li><p><strong>Bizay</strong> raised 48M to boost US operations</p></li><li><p><strong>OZU</strong> won the People’s Choice Award at the Digital Built Accelerator</p></li><li><p>The winning Startups of the Startup Braga Acceleration Program: The Life is a Pitch Award went to <strong>FutureTemp</strong>; The IP Award went to <strong>NEXI TECHNOLOGIES</strong>; The Beyond Borders Award went to <strong>ASO agent</strong>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Care2Pay</strong> and <strong>Navictus</strong>, selected as the winners of the Unicorn Factory Spring Batch '26.</p></li><li><p>Triggers (Casa do Impacto) finalists: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://L.ai"><strong>L.ai</strong></a><strong> - Holistic Waste Management</strong> (Francisco Pais de Sousa, João Sàágua, João Coelho e Nuno Ventura); <strong>HydroAI</strong> (João Pimenta, João Fernandes, Eduardo Carvalho e Sérgio Capela); and <strong>Ai Action - AiTecServ</strong> (Jaime Santos, MSc). </p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sapo.pt/artigo/o-lado-invisivel-do-ecossistema-quem-faz-o-trabalho-que-ninguem-ve-6a42c32ce8c4505cbeb59c4c">O lado invisível do ecossistema: quem faz o trabalho que ninguém</a> vê by Carlos Resende</p><p>📚“<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://eco.sapo.pt/entrevista/o-mundo-e-muito-mais-competitivo-fazer-uma-coisa-so-ok-ja-nao-chega/">O mundo é muito mais competitivo. Fazer uma coisa só ok já não chega</a>” com Cristina Fonseca</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/from-knowledge-value-what-still-needs-vbsce/">From Knowledge to Value</a>: what still needs to be fixed in Portugal’s innovation ecosystem by Silvia Almeida</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupgenome.com/ecosystems/porto">📚Porto ecosystem by the numbers</a> by Startup Genome</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://searchfundinstitute.substack.com/p/58-what-2026-stanford-study-says">58%: What 2026 Stanford Study Says About the State of Search Funds</a> by Newton Campos</p><p>📚Claude x Khosla Ventures: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.productmarketfit.tech/p/claude-x-khosla-ventures-the-pitch">The Pitch Deck Agent</a></p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://x.com/chesny/status/2068396516016824803">How AI works</a> by Chesny</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/svkxQ7pdk4o?si=suTia2ZFK2FgNDj_">Como medir o impacto da inovação?</a> | Diogo Vieira da Silva (Porto Business School) | Tech Refresh</p><p>🎬<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/is2lgRB3lzI?si=IBQ7uhve9eVSG6EC">Inside Founder's Mind</a> #1 - MIGUEL ALVES RIBEIRO</p><p>🎬Stanford Luck Researcher: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/EvEsWpiT8WQ?si=8DD1jN6p_8MuI_zw">How to Manifest the Life You Want</a></p><p>🎬<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/c3iJUoMzt5I?si=XIlOnW2Ir1R7AwJQ">How Coach scaled from a single store into a global icon</a> with Lew Frankfort</p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The 351 Effect | Week 26</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/the-351-effect-week-26</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/the-351-effect-week-26</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 29 Jun 2026 14:57:38 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>The 351 Portuguese Startup Association has become one of the most consequential forces in Portugal’s entrepreneurial landscape. What began as a grassroots digital community has evolved into something far more structural: the social infrastructure that gives density, continuity, and territorial…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>The <strong>351 Portuguese Startup Association</strong> has become one of the most consequential forces in Portugal’s entrepreneurial landscape. What began as a grassroots digital community has evolved into something far more structural: the social infrastructure that gives density, continuity, and territorial reach to the country’s startup ecosystem. Its impact is not theoretical; it is visible, measurable, and increasingly impossible to ignore.</p><p>Take the<em> </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://portugaltechweek.com/"><em>Portugal Tech Week</em></a>. No other organisation, public or private, had ever managed to activate the country at this scale. More than 20 cities involved, around 300 events powered by local partners, and over 30,000 people engaged. It wasn’t a conference. It wasn’t a festival. It was a national mobilisation of entrepreneurial energy and it proved that innovation in Portugal is not confined to Lisbon and Porto. It lives in Braga, Aveiro, Évora, Madeira, the Açores, and everywhere in between, waiting for someone to connect the dots.</p><p>That “someone” has been the <strong>351</strong>.</p><p>And the work goes deeper. The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://351startups.com/techstars-community-leader-academy-2025/"><em>Community Leaders Academy</em></a>, developed with Techstars, is quietly training and validating the next generation of regional ecosystem builders; the people who create communities where none existed, who keep talent rooted in the territory, and who give founders outside the traditional axis a real chance to grow. This is capacity‑building. It is the slow, patient work that makes an ecosystem viable.</p><p><strong>351</strong> is not just a meeting point for founders. It is the mechanism that allows new communities to emerge, that helps early projects survive the fragile first months, and that gives regions the tools to build their own entrepreneurial future. In a country that too many times confuses innovation with slogans and startups with events, the 351 has been a reminder that ecosystems are not built on stages; they are built on the ground, every day, by people doing work that rarely makes headlines.</p><p>As the association enters a new institutional chapter, with its first formal electoral process, one thing becomes clear: Portugal’s startup ecosystem is maturing. Volunteer enthusiasm was the fuel to begin; structure, continuity, and leadership are the engine required to sustain impact. And the 351 is already proving it can operate at the level of Europe’s most influential startup associations, with a uniquely Portuguese model that is more distributed, more community‑driven, and, frankly, more human.</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><strong>“The biggest lesson I’ve learned is that startup founders grow faster together.”</strong> <em>Stewart Noakes, co‑founder of Canopy Community</em></p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p>THE IMPACT CIRCLE 2026 is a matchmaking event bringing together ~500 curated leaders and over 15 corporations, connecting promising startups with companies shaping the industries of the future. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.theimpactcircle.eu/">Startups can apply until 1 June</a></p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://liquidinnovation.co/smart-city-of-rock/">Smart Rock Tank</a> by <strong>Rock In Rio</strong> and <strong>Unicorn Factory</strong> this Wednesday</p></li><li><p><strong>Co-working Day for Designers + Mentoring</strong> by LisboaUX, this Friday at Casa do Impacto</p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">Know a teenager with big ideas? </span><strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa</strong><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);"> is running the </span><strong>Innovation Summer School,&nbsp;</strong><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">a 2-week hands-on bootcamp in Lisbon and Porto where high schoolers (14–18) team up to build real startups, tackle corporate challenges, and pitch to experts. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.innovationsummerschool.com/"><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">Deadline for applications; Lisbon - June 26 / Porto</span></a><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);"> - July 8. &nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p>Finding relevant startup programs, grants, pilot opportunities, events can be time-consuming.  Not anymore, <strong>Build Up Labs</strong> built the<strong> </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startuptools.builduplabs.com/founder-opportunities/"><strong>Founder Opportunities</strong> search tool</a>. It brings together open programs, funding opportunities, networking events, new perks, and visibility opportunities curated by us and our AI agents for our founders community and the wider startup ecosystem in Portugal.</p></li><li><p><strong>Tourism Advance</strong> is an open innovation program that connects startups with companies in the hospitality sector seeking solutions to address real business challenges. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.tourismadvance.pt/">Applications open</a> until Aug 23</p><p></p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><strong>Cozecare, DermVision, </strong>and <strong>NeuroDev</strong> were the winners of HealthCup — Capital Semente 2026 by UBIMedical Incubator</p></li><li><p><strong>SafeAlleleSCA</strong> wins the Tecnimede Open Innovation Competition</p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚Shipping Solo with AI: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/shipping-solo-ai-o-que-20-anos-de-produto-me-sobre-com-rui-barroca-hpf9e/">o que 20 anos de produto me ensinaram sobre trabalhar com inteligência artificial</a> por Rui Barroca</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://pmemagazine.sapo.pt/tenho-20-anos-e-ja-nao-quero-crescer/">Tenho 20 anos e já não quero crescer</a> por Rita Tacão Graça</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://media.licdn.com/dms/document/media/v2/D4E1FAQHVoPfNpj-QHg/feedshare-document-sanitized-pdf/B4EZ77Ni9GHoA8-/0/1782331094340?e=1782982800&amp;v=beta&amp;t=jMaXMuoZX_mDP1PDqZ9wW-1DzQTjZGxucqOJwYHPB0o">EUROPEAN STARTUP &amp; SCALEUP SCOREBOARD</a> Report for Portugal 2026</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.productcircle.co/state-of-ai-2026">State of AI in Product 2026</a> by Product Circle</p><p>📚YCombinator <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.ycombinator.com/rfs">Request for Startups</a></p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/3Q08BTHdteR4WVffZDJ4UJ?si=1sFh2QNUSaqGUlpl2MaHgw">Learn AI is a bad advice</a> by Greg Isenberg </p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/5B2b3B6coCVY0POAEjY5Ur?si=1QODwZ6WTdG6kSt-kCZN4A">Q&amp;A on fundraising</a> in this lecture with Marc Andreessen, Founder of Netscape and Andreessen Horowitz, Ron Conway, Founder of SV Angel, and Parker Conrad, Founder of Zenefits.</p><p>🎬<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/lsBNA3-Kh58?si=Dxfs4saxDSqiLBvk">ConversAI</a> com Rui Barroca</p><p>🎬How Portugal Is <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/3SFQ6MFpBe8?si=DZ0wDGd7cw2Zqksy">Using AI to Transform Public Administration</a></p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>São João, Startups &amp; Talent | Week 25</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/sao-joao-startups-talent-week-25</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/sao-joao-startups-talent-week-25</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 22 Jun 2026 08:24:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>June arrives and Portugal shifts into that unmistakable rhythm of the Popular Saints: Santo António, São Pedro and, above all, São João. These aren’t just festivities; they’re full‑body experiences. And if you’re in Porto, you know there’s no description that does São João justice. You have to feel…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>June arrives and Portugal shifts into that unmistakable rhythm of the Popular Saints: Santo António, São Pedro and, above all, São João. These aren’t just festivities; they’re full‑body experiences. And if you’re in Porto, you know there’s no description that does São João justice. You have to feel it; the noise, the smoke, the music, the hammers, the chaos, the joy.</p><p>In Porto, São João isn’t a night. It’s the night.</p><p>The city becomes a living organism: streets overflowing with people, 'martelinhos' and sardines on every corner, improvised stages, fireworks that shake the river, and that collective sense of “we’re all in this together”. Curiously, or not, that same energy is what fuels Porto’s startup ecosystem.</p><p>A city that knows how to celebrate also know how to build. Collaboration isn’t a buzzword here; it’s muscle memory. Resilience isn’t a pitch slide; it’s cultural DNA. Creativity isn’t a workshop; it’s how the city breathes.</p><p>With the support of the Porto City Hall, the ecosystem has been growing consistently. Not in sudden hype cycles, but in the steady, deliberate way that actually lasts. Talent, investment, international ambition; all rising.</p><p>Anchored by players like Founders Founders, UPTEC, Scale Up Porto, Porto Digital, Porto Business School, ANJE and amplified by events like SIM Conference, Porto region has secured its place on the European map.</p><ul><li><p>+700 Startups and Scaleups (ScaleUp Porto Ecosystem Report, 2025)</p></li><li><p>+17.000 employers (ScaleUp Porto Ecosystem Report, 2025)</p></li><li><p>+€8.5B in ecosystem value (GSER Startup Genome, 2026)</p></li><li><p>Top 60 Emerging Ecosystems globally (GSER Startup Genome, 2026)</p></li></ul><p>Not bad for a city that still insists on grilling sardines in the middle of the street.</p><p>Porto isn’t just keeping up, it’s setting the pace.</p><p>And doing it without losing itself. That’s the part I admire most. The city grows, evolves, attracts, compete, but never abandons its identity. São João is the perfect reminder of that: tradition and transformation, side by side.</p><p>And just like weaving through the São João crowds, Porto’s founders know how to hustle, pivot, and find their own path forward;  sometimes through unlikely shortcuts, other times through pure creative stubbornness.</p><p>So whether you’re dancing under fireworks or pitching your next big idea, remember: in Porto, innovation doesn’t replace tradition; it grows from it.</p><p>Always with that deep sense of belonging: to your neighborhood, your roots, and to a city that looks outward without ever forgetting who it is. 💙</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><em>“Innovation is part of Porto’s identity, and the SIM Conference shows how our ecosystem is stronger and more collaborative than ever."</em></p><p><em>Pedro Duarte (Porto's Mayor) </em></p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Goparity | Impact finance</strong> is moving into equity crowdfunding, launching funding rounds between €300K and €1M in Portugal.</p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/je46teui">Trans-Atlantic Angel Conference (TAAC) #9 Final Demo Day</a>, happening online on Thursday 25 at 4:00 PM CEST.</p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/0sjy3bn4">Hire Your AI Team in Minutes</a> | With Abdul Khan from <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Spinnable.ai">Spinnable.ai</a> this Thursday at BuildUp Labs.</p></li><li><p><strong>Santander X</strong> Do you want to take your startup or scaleup to the global stage of innovation? Applications open until June 30.</p></li><li><p>THE IMPACT CIRCLE 2026 is a matchmaking event bringing together ~500 curated leaders and over 15 corporations, connecting promising startups with companies shaping the industries of the future. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.theimpactcircle.eu/">Startups can apply until 1 June</a></p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">Know a teenager with big ideas? </span><strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa</strong><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);"> is running the </span><strong>Innovation Summer School,&nbsp;</strong><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">a 2-week hands-on bootcamp in Lisbon and Porto where high schoolers (14–18) team up to build real startups, tackle corporate challenges, and pitch to experts. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.innovationsummerschool.com/"><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">Deadline for applications; Lisbon - June 26 / Porto</span></a><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);"> - July 8. &nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><strong>Porto </strong>Ranks Among Top 60 Emerging Ecosystems Globally with 693% Ecosystem Value Growth in the 2026 Global Startup Ecosystem Report</p></li><li><p><strong>Lampsy</strong>, <strong>blue.auth</strong>, <strong>zeropact</strong>, <strong>Gazelle</strong>, <strong>GetVocal, MyCancer, metatissue, RT Beam Tech, Rootkey, DIGin, OctoHealth</strong> were the finalists of Startup World Cup Portugal. <strong>Lampsy</strong> will now represent Portugal in Silicon Valley, where it will compete against winners from more than 70 countries for the 1 million euros investment prize.</p></li><li><p><strong>ZeroPact</strong> won Caixa Capital award.</p></li><li><p><strong>Matterpieces</strong> (Construction Impact Award), <strong>Typeble</strong> (Digital Innovation Award), and <strong>OZU</strong> (People’s Choice Award), are the winners of Digital Built Demo Day organized by Técnico Venture Lab.</p></li><li><p><strong>UpSpeech</strong> (People's Choice Award); <strong>VaultHaus</strong> (Digital Award); <strong>MYCancer</strong> (Impact Award), are the winners of HealthQ UP Demo Day</p></li><li><p><strong>MindMatch</strong> won PITX by Startup Leiria</p></li><li><p><strong>Jorge Pimenta</strong> as the new Vice President of EBN.</p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚PIONEERS - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1l9zkU8JUoqZMzRckYukX7SnQKcSOm4oa/view">O Retrato da Mulher Portuguesa na Tecnologia</a></p><p>📚 Is <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/ai-going-take-my-job-asking-friend-named-joe-susana-dinis-correia-o9ryf/">AI Going to Take My Job</a>? (Asking for a Friend Named Joe) by Susana Dinis Correia</p><p>📚 Thomas: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.ycombinator.com/launches/QwO-thomas-the-first-yc-backed-ai-founder">the first YC-backed AI founder</a></p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eit.europa.eu/news-events/news/gender-smart-innovation-can-strengthen-europes-economy-and-competitiveness">EIT Community Supernovas handbook</a> on gender-smart innovation</p><p>📚A New Era of <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.midjourney.com/medical/blogpost">Midjourney</a> </p><p>📚MAZE: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://docsend.com/view/aivzcub8ekn2s9p3">a year of impact</a></p><p> 📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupgenome.com/report/the-global-startup-ecosystem-report-2026/introduction">Global Startup Ecosystem Report 2026</a> (#GSER2026) by Startup Genome</p><p>🎧  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/6eNbKitoZFsk6XeMFfDn4W">IA por IAs</a>: Pare de copiar prompts</p><p>🎥 “<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/ei_mOZxF70c?si=OkrQRyzilI4Kukp_">Quando os Digital Twins Resolvem</a>”</p><p>🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/ZiqHiosxOiY?si=oNUfnTw4MC2bRkAW">Bitalk</a> com Ricardo Morgado, cofundador e CEO da LoopOS</p><p>🎥 Lyft was drowning in data and losing customers. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7473388017806762005/">CEO David Risher fixed it by getting in the car</a></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Resilience | Week 24</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/resilience-week-24</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/resilience-week-24</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 15 Jun 2026 10:48:06 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>Resilience. We usually define it as the ability to recover quickly from difficulties. A neat dictionary sentence for something that, in real life, is anything but neat. This week, I kept thinking about the founders we meet across the ecosystem; different industries, different stages, different…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span>Resilience. We usually define it as the ability to recover quickly from difficulties. A neat dictionary sentence for something that, in real life, is anything but neat.</span></p><p><span>This week, I kept thinking about the founders we meet across the ecosystem; different industries, different stages, different personalities, yet all connected by the same thread: a stubborn capacity to absorb shocks, adapt, and keep building.</span></p><p><span>We often talk about vision, talent, timing, capital, networks. All important. But when you listen carefully to founders who have survived long enough to create something meaningful, you notice that the real story is always the same: they were hit, they fell, they recalibrated, and they continued.</span></p><p><span>Resilience is not glamour. It’s not a TED talk. It’s not a motivational poster.<br>It’s the quiet discipline of showing up again the next morning.</span></p><p><span>And here’s the part we sometimes forget: resilience is learnable.<br>Some people seem to have it naturally, yes. But most founders build it the same way they build their companies — through repetition, mistakes, and the uncomfortable process of becoming someone capable of handling more than they could last year.</span></p><p><span>I’ve come to believe that resilience is the single strongest predictor of startup success. Not the size of the market. Not the sophistication of the product. Not even the brilliance of the team. Every startup, from the smallest to the most ambitious, goes through cycles of doubt, scarcity, and unexpected turbulence. What separates those who endure from those who fade is the founder’s ability to stay in the game long enough for the strategy to work.</span></p><p><span>And the truth is that our ecosystem is full of these quieter examples; founders who don’t make headlines but who keep pushing, adjusting, and learning. </span></p><p><span>They are the backbone of any entrepreneurial country.</span></p><p><span>So as we enter another week, here’s a simple reminder for all of us building, mentoring, or supporting founders: <strong>Resilience isn’t about being unbreakable. It’s about being rebuildable.</strong></span></p><p><span>And that, more than anything else, is what keeps ecosystems alive.</span></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><em>“You may have to fight a battle more than once to win it.”</em></p><p><em>Margaret Thatcher</em></p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p><strong>PRODUCTIZED CONFERENCE </strong>| 18-19 June (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://www.productized.co">www.productized.co</a>) returns to Lisbon for two days focused on product strategy, AI, and the future of building great products. Get your <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ti.to/productized/conf2026/discount/STARTUPDIGEST15">ticket with 15% exclusive discount here.</a></p></li><li><p>'<strong>Parecia uma boa ideia</strong>' an Open Mic with a stand-up vibe, where people share real stories: decisions, adventures, lessons learned, and moments that didn't go exactly as planned. This Friday at Rose &amp; Stone Viseu</p></li><li><p><strong>Santander X</strong> Do you want to take your startup or scaleup to the global stage of innovation? Applications open until June 30.</p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">Know a teenager with big ideas? </span><strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa</strong><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);"> is running the </span><strong>Innovation Summer School,&nbsp;</strong><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">a 2-week hands-on bootcamp in Lisbon and Porto where high schoolers (14–18) team up to build real startups, tackle corporate challenges, and pitch to experts. </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.innovationsummerschool.com/"><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">Deadline for applications; Lisbon - June 26 / Porto</span></a><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);"> - July 8. &nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sftechweek.redbridgelisbon.com/#program">Portugal at SF Tech Week 2026</a>: applications are open until Jul 15</p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.iapmei.pt/PRODUTOS-E-SERVICOS/Empreendedorismo-Inovacao/Empreendedorismo-(1)/StartUP-Voucher-2025-2026.aspx">StartUP Voucher Innovate</a>: Applications for the <strong>StartUP Voucher Innovate</strong>, an initiative promoted by IAPMEI aimed at empowering young people to create their own jobs in technology-based fields, are open until August 25th.</p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://portugaltechweek.com/portugal-tech-week-palace/">Portugal Tech Week Palace</a> are officially opening submissions for: Sessions; Partners; Curators; Ambassadors; and, Volunteers</p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><strong>Portugal Tech Week</strong> was selected as a finalist in the “Digital Upskilling” category at the European Digital Skills Awards 2026 (EDSA26)</p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);">Innovation Hubs from </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="_6be99de5 d30a0239" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/insper-edu/"><span style="color: rgb(10, 102, 194);"><strong>Insper Instituto de Ensino e Pesquisa</strong></span></a><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);"> and Nova SBE ... signed a partnership  </span></p></li><li><p><strong>SCEMAI </strong>and<strong> Savearth </strong>selected for Startup Welcome Package in Germany</p></li><li><p><strong>Builtrix</strong>, <strong>Emissium</strong>, <strong>Empresta AI</strong> e <strong>GreenDash</strong> selected for Sage Impact Entrepreneurship Programme</p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);"><strong>Elétrico Pitch</strong>, by </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="_6be99de5 d30a0239" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/remote.com/"><span style="color: rgb(10, 102, 194);"><strong>Remote</strong></span></a><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);"> , is now confirmed for Portugal Tech Week 2026 and is accepting applications.</span></p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sapo.pt/artigo/o-empreendedorismo-jovem-em-portugal-desafios-e-oportunidades-6a1dc626434934ab0422a278">O empreendedorismo jovem em Portugal</a> by Carlos Resende</p><p>📚Pode existir uma <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://expresso.pt/opiniao/2026-06-11-pode-existir-uma-rede-de-inovacao-iberica--d92f56af">rede de inovação ibérica</a>? by Gil Azevedo</p><p>📚1.ª edição do <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ani.pt/publicada-1-a-edicao-do-european-startup-and-scaleup-scoreboard/">European Startup and Scaleup Scoreboard</a> by European Comission</p><p>📚“Portugal ainda está<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://jornaleconomico.sapo.pt/noticias/thijs-povel-portugal-ainda-esta-muito-atras-dos-seus-pares-em-termos-de-capital-de-risco/"> muito atrás dos seus pares no capital de risco</a>” with Thijs Povel</p><p>📚Are ecosystem leaders <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupgenome.beehiiv.com/p/are-ecosystem-leaders-wasting-money-on-accelerators">wasting money on accelerators</a>?</p><p>📚NVIDIA's CEO handed Stanford students <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.the-ai-corner.com/p/jensen-huang-stanford-cs153-playbook-2026">the playbook for the next 10 years</a> By Ruben Dominguez</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.anthropic.com/institute/recursive-self-improvement">When AI builds itself</a> by anthropic</p><p>📚Sifted 100: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sifted.eu/intelligence/reports/sifted-100-southern-europe-2026">Southern Europe Leaderboard 2026</a></p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/669550d38372f33552d2516e/6a172558bd2947234379749f_a8684052fd49a64374c9a9d3e4e5ab59_Prioritizing%20the%20risks%20from%20Artificial%20Intelligence.pdf">Prioritization of Risks from Artificial Intelligence</a> - A Delphi Study of 272 International Experts</p><p>🎧 Michael Seibel on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1hHMwLxN6EM&amp;t=270s">Lean MVP</a></p><p>🎥 </p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Green Pass is an Opportunity | Week 23</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/green-pass-is-an-opportunity-week-23</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/green-pass-is-an-opportunity-week-23</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 08:47:55 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>This week, the Government launched the Green Rail Pass inside the gov.pt app. A small feature, yes, but also a moment when a public digital service feels… well, like a service. Useful, simple, and where citizens already are. It’s a reminder of something we often forget: digital innovation in the…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>This week, the Government launched the Green Rail Pass inside the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://gov.pt">gov.pt</a> app.</p><p>A small feature, yes, but also a moment when a public digital service feels… well, like a service. Useful, simple, and where citizens already are.</p><p>It’s a reminder of something we often forget: digital innovation in the State is not about new portals or new slogans. It’s about removing friction from people’s lives. One tap instead of three forms. A pass instead of a process. A product instead of a PDF.</p><p>But there’s a deeper point here.</p><p>Portugal has a <strong>Startup ecosystem</strong> capable of building world‑class digital products; fast, user‑centric, measurable. Yet the State looks like feeling tied into a straitjacket as if it must build everything alone. Slowly. Expensively. With the usual choreography of procurement, delays, and committees.</p><p>The Green Pass, and a few other recent launches, shows what’s possible and it also shows what’s missing.</p><p>If the State truly wants to accelerate digital public services, it needs to treat the ecosystem as a partner, not an second thought. That means:</p><ul><li><p>opening APIs instead of closing systems.</p></li><li><p>running pilots with startups instead of multi‑year tenders.</p></li><li><p>share and publishing real data.</p></li><li><p>inviting product teams into the room, not only consultants.</p></li><li><p>building with the country, not just for the country.</p></li></ul><p>Portugal has the talent, the Startups, and the ambition to help modernise the State.</p><p>What we lack is a mechanism, and the political appetite to make collaboration the norm.</p><p>The Green Pass is a good step, but the real innovation will come when the Gov/State stops reinventing the wheel and starts co‑creating with the people who already know how to build it.</p><p>And a final note: <strong>Adamastor</strong> has a new layout. Lighter, faster, and (we hope) more useful, just like the digital services we keep talking about. Thank you for all the feedback you’ve shared over the past days. Keep it coming; <strong>Adamastor</strong> grows the same way ecosystems do: through iteration, collaboration, and a community that cares enough to improve it.</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><span><em>“Digital transformation is not about technology. It is about people" </em></span></p><p><em>Ursula von der Leyen</em><span><em>.</em></span></p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p><strong>startup 23 accelerator</strong> 2nd edition DEMO DAY, June 11 at Fintech House.</p></li><li><p><strong>STCP The Mobility Hackathon 2026</strong> is looking for cutting-edge startups and innovators ready to shape the future of mobility. Apply until June 11</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Last days! Applications <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupprize.eu/">open until June 13</a> for the <strong>European Startup Prize for Mobility</strong>.</p></li><li><p>If you're a Bachelor student passionate about innovation, sustainability, and the future of urban mobility, this is your chance to join an international programme designed to turn real-world challenges into impactful solutions: 𝗜𝗻𝗻𝗼𝘃𝟰𝗠𝗼𝗯𝗶𝗹𝗶𝘁𝘆 𝗦𝘂𝗺𝗺𝗲𝗿 𝗦𝗰𝗵𝗼𝗼𝗹 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟲 𝗡𝗲𝘄 𝗮𝗽𝗽𝗹𝗶𝗰𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗱𝗲𝗮𝗱𝗹𝗶𝗻𝗲: June 15.</p></li><li><p><strong>PRODUCTIZED CONFERENCE </strong>| 18-19 June (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://www.productized.co">www.productized.co</a>) returns to Lisbon for two days focused on product strategy, AI, and the future of building great products. Get your <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ti.to/productized/conf2026/discount/STARTUPDIGEST15">ticket with 15% exclusive discount here.</a></p></li><li><p> <strong>Lab2Market@Tecnico</strong> has new date: June 24 15h00 @TIC </p></li><li><p><strong>Santander X</strong> Do you want to take your startup or scaleup to the global stage of innovation? Applications open until June 30.</p></li><li><p><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">Know a teenager with big ideas? </span><strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa</strong><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);"> is running the </span><strong>Innovation Summer School,&nbsp;</strong><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">a 2-week hands-on bootcamp in Lisbon and Porto where high schoolers (14–18) team up to build real startups, tackle corporate challenges, and pitch to experts. Check available dates and apply </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://innovationsummerschool.com/">here</a><span style="color: rgb(34, 34, 34);">.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);"><strong>Porto</strong> is one of the fastest-rising tech ecosystems in the world. According to </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Dealroom.co"><span><strong>Dealroom.co</strong></span></a><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);">'s Global Tech Ecosystem Index 2026</span><strong> </strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Naide Vieira</strong> (Iplexmed) distinguished with the EIT Women Leadership award</p></li><li><p><strong>Humanos</strong> won the Mastercard For Fintechs 2026 competition</p></li><li><p><strong>Augusta Labs</strong> raised 5M and reached 50M valuation</p></li><li><p><strong>CATÓLICA-LISBON</strong> and <strong>Fundação Santander Portugal</strong> launched the I<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt/news/catolica-lisbon-and-fundacao-santander-portugal-launch-eu10000-award-recognize-innovation">nnovation for Sustainability Award</a> – Climate Resilience</p></li><li><p><strong>BRAINR, Biocol Labs, Bloq it, Ascend, sheerME, Lyzer, Coverflex, knokcare, Akurateco</strong>;  listed at Sifted 100: Southern Europe Leaderboard (100 fastest-growing startups and scaleups by revenue growth over the past three financial years).</p></li><li><p>Investors Portugal Awards: ESG Award – <strong>GoParity</strong>; Investment of the Year – <strong>Tekever</strong></p><p>; Business Angel of the Year – <strong>Nuno Sebastião</strong>; Early Stage Investor of the Year - <strong>LC Ventures</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>VetBeforePet</strong> won Omplo National Pitch Competition in Viseu</p></li><li><p><strong>Closure</strong> has won 2nd place at Techstars Global Pitch Competition. They were selected after winning Techstars Startup Weekend Women Loulé in March</p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.pwc.pt/pt/sala-imprensa/artigos-opiniao/2026/escalar-sem-reinventar-roda-caminho-eficiente-startups-portugal.html">Escalar sem reinventar a roda</a>: o caminho mais eficiente para startups em Portugal por Eduardo Barroso e Norton Amato</p><p>📚É o <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.forbespt.com/e-o-talento-portugues-que-posiciona-o-pais-como-hub-estrategico-em-tecnologia/#google_vignette">talento português que posiciona o país como hub estratégico em tecnologia</a> por Predrag Poposki </p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://app.dealroom.co/tech-ecosystem-index">The Global Tech Ecosystem Index 2026</a> by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Dealroom.co">Dealroom.co</a> </p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://thv.vc/insights/early-stage-investment-navigation">Not every company needs Venture Capital and that's fine</a> by Pedro Coutinho</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.fastcompany.com/90927453/acquired-number-1-tech-podcast-sensation">The making of ‘Acquired</a>,’ the No. 1 tech podcast sensation</p><p>📚State of play of the implementation of the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://research-and-innovation.ec.europa.eu/document/download/b7bfa53a-da21-4b2e-be25-677285033e21_en">EU Startup and Scale strategy</a> </p><p>🎧 Tim Ferriss <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/6sfpC8qRGFA?si=Wluu0Zrp1py3A3Gj">on taking risks</a> </p><p>🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/live/lGDn_gt5_8I?t=2284s">Grants, VCs, and the future of markets</a> with Bernardo Seixas from Granter and Leanne (Si Ying) Zhang from Bank for International Settlements</p><p>🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zFHzTy7XLbM">How to Build a Remarkable Brand in the Age of AI</a> with Seth Godin</p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Santos and Entrepreneurship | Week 22</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/santos-and-entrepreneurship-week-22</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/santos-and-entrepreneurship-week-22</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jun 2026 10:25:02 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>What Young Entrepreneurship Is Really Telling Us About Portugal? That&apos;s a question I put myself over the last weeks as I’ve been moving between university competitions — NOVA, NOVA SBE, Católica — and the pattern is unmistakable: there is talent, energy, and a genuine will to build. What’s missing…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>What Young Entrepreneurship Is Really Telling Us About Portugal? That's a question I put myself over the last weeks as I’ve been moving between university competitions — NOVA, NOVA SBE, Católica — and the pattern is unmistakable: there is talent, energy, and a genuine will to build. What’s missing is not ambition; it’s the path.</p><p>The young ecosystem is alive than ever. Junior Enterprises, incubators, university programs, and events like Junitec's Unicorn Day show a generation that isn’t waiting for permission. They are already creating.</p><p>But between an idea and a real company there is still a gap many don’t know how to cross. And it’s not a funding problem anymore. That perception is outdated. Today there is capital, there are business angels, there are venture studios, there are public funding, there are a novelty of options. What’s missing, often, is guidance; knowing where to start, how to validate, how to decide.</p><p>The good news is that mentorship is finally gaining critical mass. Founders with years of scars and wins are starting to give back. It’s a natural and healthy evolution of the ecosystem.</p><p>What remains heavy is our cultural relationship with risk. We still educate young people to avoid mistakes, when entrepreneurship lives from the opposite: try, fail, adjust, try again. Here, the ecosystem can play a transformative role that few other areas in Portuguese society can match. </p><p>And then there’s education. Universities are getting closer to the ecosystem (and that’s positive) but the pre‑university system is still far from the real world. Not a minor detail: the State is responsible for three quarters of all secondary students.</p><p>The strategic challenge is now unavoidable: Portugal needs to choose where to bet and how to invest. Think, reflect, design, execute. Four verbs we historically struggle with, but without them we won’t turn young talent into real impact.</p><p>Final note to the Santos Populares and traditional Arraiais that are arriving all over the country. Starting in June happens the traditional and very famous “Santos Populares”. The streets are decorated and packed with people grilling and eating sardines and bifanas, dancing, and drinking. It’s a wonderful time to enjoy the best of the Portuguese popular traditions.</p><ul><li><p>Applications <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupprize.eu/">open until June 13</a> for the <strong>European Startup Prize for Mobility</strong>.</p></li><li><p><strong>startup 23 accelerator</strong> 2nd edition DEMO DAY, June 11 at Fintech House.</p></li><li><p><strong>PIRATE Night </strong>on June 24th <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.piratesummit.com/pirate-night/">applications open</a> for free booth + two tickets.</p></li><li><p><strong>PRODUCTIZED CONFERENCE </strong>| 18-19 June (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://www.productized.co">www.productized.co</a>) returns to Lisbon for two days focused on product strategy, AI, and the future of building great products. Get your <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ti.to/productized/conf2026/discount/STARTUPDIGEST15">ticket with 15% exclusive discount here.</a></p></li><li><p><strong>Santander X</strong> Do you want to take your startup or scaleup to the global stage of innovation? Applications open until June 30.</p></li></ul><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><strong>"We always overestimate the change that will occur in the next two years and underestimate the change that will occur in the next ten. Don't let yourself be lulled into inaction."</strong> — <em>Bill Gates</em></p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Junitec Unicord Day</strong> at Lispolis this Tuesday.</p></li><li><p><strong>The Startup Capital Summit</strong> is one of the main Startup Conferences in Portugal and will take place in Coimbra this Wednesday <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.startupcapitalsummit.com/en/registrations-and-applications/">Tickets available.</a></p></li><li><p><strong>Community Leaders Gathering</strong> - Algarve Edition this Thursday in Olhão.</p></li><li><p><strong>Google for Startups AI Agents Challenge</strong> - Submissions open until June 6.</p></li></ul><h2>Congrats </h2><ul><li><p><strong>Lampsy Health</strong>, <strong>Badge</strong> and <strong>Trash4Goods</strong> are the winners of Startup Grind Lisbon Pitch Awards</p></li><li><p><strong>Mena.ai</strong> won Start Rise Challenge </p></li></ul><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://campaign.landing.jobs/tttr-2026">Tech Talent Trends Report 2026</a> by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Landing.Jobs">Landing.Jobs </a>&amp; Damia</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/psychologically-habitable-future-catolica-lisbon-school-of-business-h8rre/">The “psychologically habitable” future</a> by Frederico Fezas-Vital</p><p>📚Engineering Managers: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.ieee-tems.org/ieee-tems-leadership-briefs/emotional-infrastructure-of-tech/">The Emotional Infrastructure of Tech</a> by Aishwarya Babu</p><p>📚EIC Tech Report 2026 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://eic.ec.europa.eu/news/eic-tech-report-2026-identifies-25-emerging-deep-tech-signals-support-europes-strategic-autonomy-and-2026-03-30_en">identifies 25 emerging deep tech signals</a> </p><p>📚The Country <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/portugal-2026-country-seeking-turn-research-power-patrick-coelho-jqlse/">Seeking to Turn Research Into Technological Power</a> by Patrick Coelho</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/1sseqdYHW5qBVB1gnzKuVD?si=PTjIHI2SRRe-6krUB2Psbg">3 Dados de Conversa</a>: as diferenças entre realidade virtual (VR), realidade aumentada (AR) e realidade mista (MR) e análise ao impacto destas tecnologias com Lénia Mestrinho e Maria Ribeiro Soares</p><p>🎥  Talk from a YC partner that built monzo, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/yrebryk_yc-general-partner-broke-down-in-13-minutes-ugcPost-7463613444932648960-H7mR/">about how we should be using AI properly</a></p><p>🎥  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/eHJnEHyyN1Y?si=Yc8UgDKXw8en55KL">6 Tips on Being a Successful Entrepreneur</a> by John Mullins </p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Founder vs. Reality Fit  | Week 21</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/founder-vs-reality-fit-week-21</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/founder-vs-reality-fit-week-21</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 25 May 2026 16:25:01 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>There are meetings that follow the agenda, and there are meetings that reveal far more than what was planned. I’m fortunate to have more than a few of the second kind. I sat down with two founders to review the usual: what they are building, product, positioning, the next set of decisions that…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>There are meetings that follow the agenda, and there are meetings that reveal far more than what was planned. I’m fortunate to have more than a few of the second kind.</p><p>I sat down with two founders to review the usual: what they are building, product, positioning, the next set of decisions that always feel more urgent than they really are. We went through the motions the roadmap, the constraints, the opportunities. And then, almost as an aside, one of them mentioned he had written a series of papers on the underlying concepts that give structure to the product he's building.</p><p>I read them later, and one of those essays hit directly on a theme I’ve been returning to for some time: the decisions founders avoid because they feel expensive, when in reality the cost lies in postponing them.</p><p>The essay was “The Decision That Costs You Nothing.”  </p><p>And the timing couldn’t have been better.</p><p>What struck me wasn’t just the argument; that misalignment, whether with investors, clients, or partners, builds up quietly until it becomes structural. It was the recognition that founders often already know the truth long before they act on it. The intellectual foundation is there. The clarity is there. The writing is there. But the decision, the one that actually changes the trajectory, is postponed.</p><p>We talk a lot about product-market fit, but far less about founder-reality fit.</p><p>About the courage to walk away from what looks like progress but isn’t. About the discipline to stop feeding relationships, assumptions, or strategies that will never pay back the energy they consume.</p><p>Over the years I saw that same pattern the essay describes: the knowledge exists, the reasoning is solid, the signals are visible, but the structural decision hasn’t been made yet.</p><p>And that’s the point worth bringing to the Adamastor community this week: founders rarely lack insight; they lack permission to act on the insight they already have.</p><p>Sometimes that permission comes from a mentor, sometimes from a crisis, and sometimes — as it happened to me this week — it comes from reading the right sentence at the right moment, written by someone who, I've got a felling that already realise how relevant it would become to their own product.</p><p>The decision that costs you nothing is always the one you’ve been postponing.</p><p>And the sooner you make it, the sooner the real work can begin.</p><p><em>The work mentioned is "The Decision That Costs You Nothing" by Ahmad Noureddine and you can find it on the 'Read' section.</em></p><p>💡 <strong>The Startup Capital Summit</strong> is one of the main Startup Conferences in Portugal and will take place June 3rd. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.startupcapitalsummit.com/en/registrations-and-applications/">Tickets available.</a></p><p>💡 <strong>PIRATE Night </strong>on June 24th <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.piratesummit.com/pirate-night/">applications open</a> for free booth + two tickets.</p><p>💡 <strong>Productized</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://productized.co/">is in June this year</a> (not October)</p><p>💡 <strong>Santander X</strong> Do you want to take your startup or scaleup to the global stage of innovation? Applications open until June 30.</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><strong>"</strong>We do not see things as they are, we see them as we are.” </p><p>Anaïs Nin</p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 <strong>Startup Grind Lisbon Pitch Awards 2026</strong>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://sglx.pt/PitchNight">this</a> Tuesday.</p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/7tc1lyus">Masterclass: Entrepreneurship Through Acquisition &amp; Search Funds with Professor Newton Campos</a> @Nova SBE on May 27.</p><p>🔷 Lispolis - <strong>Startups Deep Tech em Saúde</strong>, and Startup Portugal: <strong>Above &amp; Beyond</strong>, this Thursday.</p><p>🔷 <strong>Startup Capital Summit</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.startupcapitalsummit.com/">returns to Coimbra</a> on June 3rd.</p><p>🔷 <strong>Google for Startups AI Agents Challenge</strong> - Submissions open until June 6.</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏 <strong>AXIOS CARE</strong> won Empreender com Impacto - Pitch Competition by  InCubo Alto Minho.</p><p>👏 <strong>Savearth</strong> has raised €400,000.</p><p>👏 <strong>NOVA Starters Academy</strong> winners: NSafe (overall winner);  MEMVO (Audience Award); Daysy (Best MArket Validation).</p><p>👏 <strong>VeriCasa</strong> was awarded Best Startup in the GOAL programme at the Plug and Play Summer Summit in Silicon Valley</p><p>👏 <strong>Get2C</strong> and <strong>Periplus</strong> awarded at SME EnterPRIZE competition</p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sapo.pt/artigo/portugal-nao-tem-falta-de-startups-6a0b64a8d2558eb23228c33d">Portugal não tem falta de startups</a> por Carlos Resende </p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/portugals-strategic-play-ai-capturing-value-where-most-santa-clara-gpdke/">Portugal's Strategic Play in AI</a>: Capturing Value Where It Matters Most by Pedro Santa Clara</p><p>📚 5 Insights da SIM Conference 2026: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.dig-in.pt/mediablog/5-insights-da-sim-conference-2026/">O papel dos Dados e da Expertise da DIG-IN</a> no Futuro do Ecossistema</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ahmad.pt/essays/the-decision-that-costs-you-nothing">The Decision That Costs You Nothing</a> by Ahmad Noureddine</p><p>📚 Who I Am — Inês Odila:<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.notion.so/coverflex/Who-I-Am-In-s-Odila-Writing-Style-Agent-Profile-35acae5c2169810089eef2d94de8a851"> Writing Style &amp; Agent Profile</a></p><p>📚 ESNA Compendium Volume I: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://backoffice.esnalliance.eu/multimedia/esna/building-a-competitive-europe-vol.i-regulatory-barriers.pdf">Regulatory Barriers</a></p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/3PmvHE203RjmNBJ0PCVQL9">Are we living longer</a>: Céline Abecassis-Moedas and Rui Quinta we dive into the longevity revolution</p><p>🎥  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/BP0WXizt6vU?si=V0BsP5SB1csBemHJ">Improving padel skills with data</a> | Andre Croft de Moura from CourtMaster w/ Luis Gutman</p><p>🎥  CDK | André Oliveira (PixelMatters): <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/vT9R9npaPhU?si=7T8ugH7HCO58dRDh">Design, talento e os segredos de quem constrói do zero</a></p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Growing up | Week 20</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/growing-up-week-20</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/growing-up-week-20</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 18 May 2026 18:49:03 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>I returned from Porto with tired legs and a head buzzing in that familiar way these gatherings tend to provoke (and the party along Dragao, Ribeira and Aliados dried my batteries). The third edition of SIM Conference once again filled the Alfândega with energy, ambition and a density of…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>I returned from Porto with tired legs and a head buzzing in that familiar way these gatherings tend to provoke (and the party along Dragao, Ribeira and Aliados dried my batteries). The third edition of <strong>SIM Conference</strong> once again filled the Alfândega with energy, ambition and a density of conversations that you don’t often find concentrated in one place. And, as always, the city did its part, reminding us that entrepreneurship may be global, but its rituals are still very local.</p><p>But now that the badges are in a drawer and the rhythm of the week has reclaimed its usual shape, it’s worth pausing to look at what actually happened, not the LinkedIn version, but the real one.</p><p>According to Startup Portugal, this year brought together more than 4,000 people, around 400 startups, and close to 200 investors, with roughly one in five coming from outside the country. Numbers matter, of course. They tell us that Portugal can now convene a room that would have been unthinkable a decade ago. But what stayed with me wasn’t the scale, it was the density. People who raise capital and people who allocate it, actually meeting with intent. Not by accident, not by proximity, but by design.</p><p>That is still rare in Portugal. And it is still precious.</p><p><strong>SIM</strong> has grown into something that sits in an interesting space: part marketplace, part checkpoint, part mirror. It shows us what we are becoming, but also what we are still not.</p><p>This year, more founders spoke about revenue than rounds. More investors asked about retention than about pitch decks. More conversations were about operations, hiring, and the unglamorous mechanics of building something that lasts. It’s a sign of maturity: the ecosystem is learning that the story is not the company. The company is the company.</p><p>And then there was the room, the one that matters. The one where people who build, people who fund, and people who support the ecosystem sat together with a level of seriousness that wasn’t always there in previous editions. Less noise, more signal. Less theatre, more intent.</p><p>As a side note, I was a very interested spectator of the Ecosystem Table during <strong>SIM</strong>, a conversation that deserves its own space, and that I’ll write about in the future. It was one of those moments where you feel the ecosystem thinking collectively, not competitively.</p><p><strong>SIM Conference 2026</strong> didn’t just showcase an ecosystem. It revealed one that is growing up. Not in size, that part is easy, but in posture; and that should make us optimistic. </p><p>A final note to acknowledge Startup Portugal. This is not a sympathy gesture toward an organisation that consistently receives me with warmth, but a recognition of a team that delivered and deserves to be credited for it.</p><p>💡 <strong>The Startup Capital Summit</strong> is one of the main Startup Conferences in Portugal and will take place June 3rd. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.startupcapitalsummit.com/en/registrations-and-applications/">Tickets available.</a></p><p>💡 <strong>PIRATE Night </strong>on June 24th <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.piratesummit.com/pirate-night/">applications open</a> for free booth + two tickets.</p><p>💡 <strong>Santander X</strong> Do you want to take your startup or scaleup to the global stage of innovation? Applications open until June 30.</p><p>💡 <strong>Portugal Tech Week</strong> returns from November 6 to 15, 2026, and at the heart of it, PTW Palace returns as one of the spaces where the week comes alive. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://portugaltechweek.com/sponsor/">And they are looking for sponsors.</a></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><strong>"</strong>If someone offers you an amazing opportunity and you are not sure you can do it, say yes – then learn how to do it later!"</p><p><strong>Richard Branson</strong></p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/nfnlqmzo">NOVA Starters Academy DEMO Day</a>, this Wednesday.</p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eventbrite.pt/e/sunset-fado-experience-at-ando-living-rooftop-wine-and-petiscos-included-tickets-1987353986271">Sunset Fado Experience at Ando Living Rooftop</a> w/ Fiona.</p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.meetup.com/productized/events/314655558/">Productized Talks at Sixt</a> this Thursday.</p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.meetup.com/351-the-portuguese-startup-association/events/314660185/">Startup Grind Lisbon Pitch Awards</a> next Tuesday.</p><p>🔷 Applications for the 7th edition of <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupprize.eu/">European Startup Prize for Mobility</a> are open.</p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/7tc1lyus">Masterclass: Entrepreneurship Through Acquisition &amp; Search Funds with Professor Newton Campos</a> @Nova SBE next May 27.</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏   <strong>GuideSofia</strong>, 𝐂𝐨𝐧𝐧𝐞𝐜𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 and <strong>Lola Stories</strong> the winners of Nova Startup Club - Pitch Competition </p><p>👏   <strong>merytu</strong> raised 1.5M</p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://mcusercontent.com/e5764e5179c91b6f2b534bf34/files/b0155cbe-a61a-fd38-6c89-f3cd691496aa/Impact_report_2025_compressed_1_.pdf">GOPARITY 2025 Impact Report</a></p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sloanreview.mit.edu/article/philosophy-eats-ai/">Philosophy Eats AI</a></p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/7dhOTmUAdcppyFyrqjWy1o">The Founder Mindset</a> w/ Reza Satchu and Reese Witherspoon (Hello Sunshine)</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/3vtuq52a66G0FbPKXeDqAW?si=wT0qmJ0nQN-mQzk_sOg4dg">DOJO AI: Personal Branding - How to Systematize LinkedIn</a> w/ Maria Ledentsova</p><p>🎥  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1j4qXZBiwI8">iMotorbike $10M Journey</a> w/ Gil Carmo, Founder &amp; CEO of iMotorbike</p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>SIM! | Week 19</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/sim-week-19</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/sim-week-19</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 10 May 2026 16:28:10 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>When Ronaldo jumps, the stadium holds its breath. When he lands with that unmistakable “ Sim! ”, the energy shifts, a spark, a surge, a collective lift. That same pulse is about to hit Porto again. SIM Conference returns this week , and once more the city becomes a meeting point for founders,…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>When Ronaldo jumps, the stadium holds its breath. When he lands with that unmistakable “<strong>Sim!</strong>”, the energy shifts, a spark, a surge, a collective lift.</p><p>That same pulse is about to hit Porto again.</p><p><strong>SIM Conference</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://simconf.com/">returns this week</a>, and once more the city becomes a meeting point for founders, investors, operators, and the people who keep this ecosystem moving forward. The last two editions left me genuinely energized; this year, I’m heading back with even more curiosity about what Portugal is building next.</p><p>I’ll be at SIM, fully in the mix, as always and moderating the panel '<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/6nv5kmtb?tk=8KLxFX">Building Community in Portugal</a>' on Friday at 15h20.</p><p>If you’re around, reach out. Let’s connect, catch up, compare notes, or simply say hello. These moments matter, and they’re always better shared.</p><p>And it’s not just Porto. Over the next days, there’s a wave of ecosystem events happening across the country; from meetups to pitch sessions to community gatherings, and everything in between. If you want to keep track of what’s coming, the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events">Adamastor Agenda</a> has it all mapped out.</p><p>From “Sim!” to SIM Conference, <strong>see you in Porto</strong>. </p><p>💡 <strong>May 14–15 | Sim Conference at Alfândega do Porto</strong> Get Adamastor discount:  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/sim-conference-2026">30% off with SDG30.</a></p><p>💡 <strong>PIRATE Night </strong>on June 24th <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.piratesummit.com/pirate-night/">applications open</a> for free booth + two tickets.</p><p>💡 <strong>Portugal Tech Week</strong> returns from November 6 to 15, 2026, and at the heart of it, PTW Palace returns as one of the spaces where the week comes alive. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://portugaltechweek.com/sponsor/">And they are looking for sponsors.</a></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><strong>"The glorification of entrepreneurship as an end in itself may actually be hurting our economy... Most true entrepreneurs are not business owners, and conversely, many business owners lack the personality traits that define an entrepreneur."</strong></p><p><strong>Paul O'Brien </strong></p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.up.pt/eventos/event/conferencia-vc-pe-risco-oportunidade-mundo-mudanca">Conferência VC &amp; PE</a> | Risco e Oportunidade num mundo em mudança @FEP.</p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/7si3sepb">Reimagining Women’s Health</a>: The Next Frontier | FemTech Portugal x Sword.</p><p>🔷 Applications for the 7th edition of <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupprize.eu/">European Startup Prize for Mobility</a> are open. </p><p>🔷  <strong>Web Summit 2026</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://websummit.com/">announced the first speakers</a>: Larry Li (Founder, Amino Capital); Jen Wong (COO, Reddit); and Richard Socher (CEO, Recursive). </p><p>🔷  <strong>Santander X</strong> Do you want to take your startup or scaleup to the global stage of innovation? <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://app.santanderx.com/calls/the-quantum-ai-leap">Applications open until June 30</a>.</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏   <strong>VARTHEO </strong>has been selected for the Campus Founders Accelerator Program.</p><p>👏   Startups taking part of Web Summit Vancouver 2026:  <strong>CyberX - The Ethical Hacking Services; Enline; Nitrogen Sensing Solutions; Jammin; AtivoLabs; Aivis; DAISEE</strong>; and <strong>VisionHammer</strong>.</p><p>👏   <strong>Savearth</strong> raised 400k.</p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 João Moita and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.joaomoita.com/">How he helps product teams stay relevant in the age of AI</a>.</p><p>ESNA - Europe Startup Nations Alliance: What can you learn from <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://scoreboard.esnalliance.eu/">Startup Nations Standard Scoreboard</a>? </p><p>📚 DUBAI FUTURE FOUNDATION: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.dubaifuture.ae/the-global-50-special-report/#:~:text=HIGHLIGHTED%20OPPORTUNITIES">A Special Report on future opportunities Empowering Youth and Future Generations</a>.</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.hsbcinnovationbanking.com/gb/en/resources/venture-capital-term-sheet-guide-2026">Venture Capital Term Sheet Guide</a> 2026 by Glen Waters.</p><p>🎧 First joint podcast in 10 years: Sam Altman and Greg Brockman finally talked - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.the-ai-corner.com/p/sam-altman-greg-brockman-core-memory-podcast-10-things-2026">10 things matter</a>.</p><p>🎥  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/2QO8sV7AiUY?si=gVxWTE_1YjWDwaBK">Disrupt with Purpose and Create a Story Worth Sharing</a> by Lubna Forzley-Badr.</p><p>🎥  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.hsbcinnovationbanking.com/gb/en/resources/inside-term-sheet-negotiations">Inside term sheet negotiations</a>: in conversation with Dan Bowyer and Emily Wood.</p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Truth Hurts, But Silence Hurts More | Week 18</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/truth-hurts-but-silence-hurts-more-week-18</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/truth-hurts-but-silence-hurts-more-week-18</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 05 May 2026 08:19:14 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>This week’s Adamastor was inspired by a post from Udemy’s co‑founder; one of the most successful startups to emerge from the Founder Institute , and by a sharp comment from Fernando Fraga: politeness in mentorship is rarely about protecting the founder; it’s about protecting the mentor’s network.…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>This week’s Adamastor was inspired by a post from Udemy’s co‑founder; one of the most successful startups to emerge from the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/">Founder Institute</a>, and by a sharp comment from Fernando Fraga: politeness in mentorship is rarely about protecting the founder; it’s about protecting the mentor’s network.</p><p><strong>And he’s right</strong>.</p><p>Telling a founder their idea is broken means risking the relationship, the introductions, the future deal flow. Vague encouragement is reputationally safer than honest critique. In Portugal, this instinct is even stronger, because we have a cultural reflex to avoid the harsh truth in the name of being “polite”. We soften the edges, we dilute the feedback until it becomes harmless and useless, and in doing so, we often fail the people we’re trying to help.</p><p>I’ve spent some time with acceleration and mentorship programs, here and abroad, and the most useful conversations I ever had with founders were the uncomfortable ones: telling one his go‑to‑market was built on untested assumptions; telling another his cap table would collapse before seed; telling a third that the co‑founder dynamic wouldn’t survive future rounds ...</p><p>Some adapted, some didn’t. The ones who could hear it built the companies. Most of the ones who couldn’t… didn’t.</p><p>The rarest mentors aren’t the smartest, they’re the ones willing to spend relational capital to tell a founder what they actually need to hear. The ones who choose truth over convenience. At the end of the day, polite feedback is just abandonment disguised as respect.</p><p>What This <strong>Means for the Maturity of Our Ecosystem</strong></p><p>The way we give, or avoid giving, feedback says a lot about the maturity of an ecosystem. Young ecosystems protect themselves through politeness: everyone is supportive, everyone is friendly, everyone avoids friction. It looks healthy, but it isn’t. It’s simply the behaviour of a system still too fragile to handle truth.</p><p>As an ecosystem matures, honesty stops being seen as aggression and starts being seen as service. The quality of conversations rises. Decisions accelerate. Founders stop looking for validation and start looking for clarity. And mentors stop measuring their words to protect their “network capital” and start using it to create real impact.</p><p><strong>Portuga</strong>l is exactly at that inflection point. Density has increased, talent is stronger, cycles are faster and that demands a culture of truth. Not brutal truth, but useful truth. The kind of truth that prevents a founder from losing two years chasing a hypothesis that never had legs. The kind of truth that saves capital, time, and emotional energy. The kind of truth that builds companies, not presentations.</p><p>If we want a stronger, more international, more competitive ecosystem, we need to abandon the idea that being polite means saying what the other person wants to hear. Maturity begins when we understand that the greatest act of respect is telling someone something that might change the trajectory of their company, even if it’s uncomfortable.</p><p>In the end, it’s simple: an ecosystem grows when its conversations grow.  </p><p>And conversations only grow when we stop confusing politeness with respect.</p><p><strong>This week </strong>also marks <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sapo.pt/artigo/o-que-falta-dizer-sobre-o-empreendedorismo-em-portugal-69f1320a8f0d8a54e7baabea">the beginning of my collaboration with SAPO.pt</a>, where I’ll be writing, every two week, a column on the Portuguese entrepreneurial ecosystem. The goal is simple: help the country understand what is actually happening beneath the surface, the talent we have, the companies being built, the value being created, and the cultural shift already underway. I’ve always believed that if Portugal truly grasps the scale and potential of this ecosystem, everyone benefits: founders, investors, institutions, and the country itself. It’s a new challenge, one I’m taking on with enthusiasm, and I hope to count on your support as we open this space to a wider audience.</p><p>And I just realised we’re now just one week away from <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://simconf.com/">SIM Conference in Porto</a>, one of the high moments of the ecosystem calendar. Two days where the energy, the density, and the ambition of the Portuguese tech scene are all in the same room. If you’re building, investing, mentoring, or simply paying attention to what’s emerging here, you should be there. <strong>I’ll be there</strong>, fully immersed as always, and I hope to cross paths with many of you. These encounters matter, they remind us that this ecosystem moves forward when we show up.</p><p>💡 <strong>Tech Hiring Conference</strong> 2026 May 07 by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Landing.Jobs">Landing.Jobs</a> &amp; Damia Group, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/tech-hiring-community-conference-2026">tickets on sale</a></p><p>💡 <strong>START Rise Challenge</strong>, powered by Start Campus is a national platform for bold AI founders to gain visibility, sharpen their ideas, and move closer to real-world pilots. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startrisechallenge.com/#hero">Explore the program and apply until May 07</a></p><p>💡 <strong>May 14–15 | Alfândega do Porto</strong> Where it all connects: we’re heading to @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://simconf.com/">simconference</a> Two days to meet founders, investors, innovation teams, and ecosystem builders. Curated formats that make conversations more relevant and follow-ups easier.  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/sim-conference-2026">30% off with SDG30</a></p><p>💡 <strong>PIRATE Night </strong>on June 24th <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.piratesummit.com/pirate-night/">applications open</a> for free booth + two tickets</p><p>💡 <strong>Portugal Tech Week</strong> returns from November 6 to 15, 2026, and at the heart of it, PTW Palace returns as one of the spaces where the week comes alive.</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“We tend to overestimate the effect of a technology in the short run and underestimate the effect in the long run”</p><p><em>Kevin Kelly (futurist)</em> </p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 <strong>Startup HR Pitch &amp; Round Table | APG + 351 </strong>this Wednesday</p><p>🔷 <strong>Startup Summer Experience 2026</strong> – Startup applications for the summer internship program promoted by Nova SBE Haddad Entrepreneurship Institute are open until May 11. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://forms.office.com/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=4zEpxDNn5kGNQsSLozS7pIBjyWuFdtRAnsHDTolW5nJUQzNZUTQ5TUVYMVBQSkQxU1VQWEVXOTlNMi4u&amp;route=shorturl">Access the best Nova SBE talent for a 5-week internship program</a>.</p><p>🔷 Applications for the 7th edition of <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupprize.eu/">European Startup Prize for Mobility</a> are open </p><p>🔷 <strong>START Lisbon</strong> Career Fair, will take place on 11 May 2026 at Unicorn Factory Lisbon.</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏   <strong>Remote</strong> announced the acquisition of Bravas </p><p>👏   <strong>Sword Health</strong> has been granted a new core U.S. patent for its AI Care Model</p><p>👏   <strong>Nova SBE Haddad Entrepreneurship</strong> celebrates it's 4th Anniversary</p><p>👏   <strong>PFx Biotech</strong> featured in the Official 2025 FoodTech 500 by Forward Fooding</p><p>👏   the winners of The Ventures Portugal 2026: Best Traction — <strong>Cozecare</strong>; Best Product — <strong>Simplifyer</strong>; Best AI Model — <strong>Forecast Factor</strong>; Best Team — <strong>PFx Biotech</strong>  </p><p>👏   <strong>PluggableAI</strong> and <strong>Lampsy Health</strong> the winners of Premios Empreende XXI  </p><p>👏   <strong>merytu</strong> raised 1.5M</p><p>👏   <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://SaudeAI.PT">SaudeAI.PT</a> part of the National AI for Healthcare Initiative was officially launched </p><p>👏    startups representing Portugal’s innovation ecosystem at Startup Grund US: <strong>Granter</strong>, <strong>VeriCasa</strong>, <strong>Air Apps</strong>, <strong>Twine</strong>, <strong>Coalex</strong>, <strong>Mantis-ai</strong>, <strong>Starweaver</strong>, <strong>UpSpeech</strong>, and <strong>NutriPetPlan</strong></p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sapo.pt/artigo/o-que-falta-dizer-sobre-o-empreendedorismo-em-portugal-69f1320a8f0d8a54e7baabea">O que falta dizer sobre o empreendedorismo em Portugal</a> por Carlos Resende</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://portugaltechweek.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/PTW2025_Report.pdf">Portugal Tech Week</a> 2025 report</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.immersivstudios.com/en/blog/vr/nova-sbe-vr">Teaching Budgeting Through VR</a>: An Immersive Classroom for Nova SBE by Immersive Studios</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.ciiic.nl/en/news/xr-x-ai-technologie-als-gereedschap-verhaal-als-kompas">XR x AI</a>: technology as a tool, story as a compass</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://link.springer.com/epdf/10.1186/s12913-025-13571-2?sharing_token=aduOlVHoiUbE5svlp6YpDm_BpE1tBhCbnbw3BuzI2RMQzQA88HGslUIQxiAaU_hHEkTHxIfieqQjYqXJvqlAZKZivMXV-P7ZvlqxKs3ZU2GSJKDwcR3hL7z0paYUYQ4BVmqZQWaAbTImSZmWf-NIKFuI0nmmZjFNp2Npw2pr9Kg%3D">Preparing tomorrow’s health entrepreneurs</a>: a collaborative multi-stakeholder approach to identifying core competencies and training needs of future professionals</p><p>🎧 James Everingham, CEO of Guild AI, joins The Deep View Conversations to talk about <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/1qX23mIkuxLtB5JjYRh1ib?si=5bMvGe1qQrGFCn7K4B-ZZQ">building a safety layer for AI agents</a></p><p>🎥  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/BjJ2RpHPQps?si=gZE19hrfVfOfY_Dy">Stop Using AI Like a Secretary, It's Your Chief Operating Officer</a> w/ Matteo Cassese</p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Ecosystem is buzzing | Week 17</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/ecosystem-is-buzzing-week-17</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/ecosystem-is-buzzing-week-17</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 27 Apr 2026 11:10:41 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>The ecosystem is buzzing again, and the next days offer one of those rare snapshots where everything overlaps: international networks landing, local communities multiplying events, and universities finally trying to reinvent their role in the talent pipeline. It’s the kind of week that reveals both…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>The ecosystem is buzzing again, and the next days offer one of those rare snapshots where everything overlaps: international networks landing, local communities multiplying events, and universities finally trying to reinvent their role in the talent pipeline. It’s the kind of week that reveals both the ambition and the contradictions of our ecosystem. A city that wants to play globally, but still behaves, at times, like a very charming village.</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.alumni.cam.ac.uk/events/camentrepreneurs-portugal-launch">CAMentrepreneurs Portugal</a> (Cambridge University) arrives with its mix of intellectual curiosity and global confidence — and yes, I’ll be there. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://lisbonconnectionweek.com/">Lisbon Connection Week</a> pulls founders, community builders and creatives into the same orbit, adding density to a city that thrives on serendipity but still struggles with coordination. Nova SBE hosts its <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/90sw5j5z">Pitch Competition</a> — I’ll be there too — one of the rare moments where the ecosystem stops performing and actually evaluates ideas. And <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.the-ventures.com/">The Ventures Global Startup Award</a> steps into the week as well — I’ll be there — adding another layer to this increasingly complex choreography of events, communities and ambitions; <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.redbull.com/pt-pt/events/red-bull-basement-portugal-2026">The Red Bull Basement</a> at Tecnico Innovation Center; and the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/tech-hiring-community-conference-2026">Tech Hiring Community Conference</a> by Landing Jobs rounds out the week, reminding us that talent remains the ecosystem’s most persistent bottleneck and its greatest opportunity.</p><p>If you want to understand where Portugal stands today, this is not a bad week to observe.</p><p>Because while all of this unfolds in Lisbon, other signals appear across the country: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/njycskga">Startup HR Pitch</a> &amp; Round Table | APG + 351 connecting startups and corporates; Startup Grind keeping the founder community alive and moving; <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/ewuuweaf?locale=pt">Omplo's Viseu</a> reminding us that innovation is not a Lisbon‑only phenomenon; the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startrisechallenge.com/#hero">START Rise Challenge</a> giving bold AI founders a national platform to gain visibility, sharpen their ideas and move closer to real‑world pilots; and, at the pinnacle, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://simconf.com/">SIM Conference</a> in Porto, a gathering that increasingly positions itself as the North’s answer to Lisbon’s gravitational pull.</p><p>It’s a busy calendar, yes. But more importantly, it’s a sign of something deeper: an ecosystem learning to operate at higher frequency. More events, more density, more collisions. And beneath the surface, a slow but meaningful shift; universities stepping into the talent pipeline with a different posture, more open to the world, more aware of their role in shaping ambition. Not the headline this week, but an important undercurrent.</p><p>For years, our academic institutions lived in a comfortable paradox: excellent islands surrounded by an innovation ecosystem that grew mostly outside them. Talent was produced inside, ambition was developed outside. The bridge between the two was fragile, informal, and often accidental. But the world has changed, and the competition for talent is global. The best students are mobile. And ecosystems that thrive are those where universities are not just suppliers of diplomas, but active engines of innovation.</p><p>By watching the events aligned for the coming weeks, you can almost see the outline of what Portugal could become: a country where talent is not something we hope for, but something we cultivate; where ambition is not imported, but produced; where events are not just noise, but signals of a system gaining maturity.</p><p>Lisbon is well supplied with events. What we need now is more substance, and substance begins where performance ends, in the uncomfortable spaces where ideas are tested, questioned and forced to grow.</p><p>These weeks give us a glimpse of that possibility.</p><p>Now we just need the discipline to turn it into reality.</p><p>💡 <strong>Productized Conference</strong> (June 18 &amp; 19) Two days for product people figuring out how to build, decide, and ship in an AI-shaped industry. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://productized.co/tickets">Early bird tickets close this Thursday </a></p><p>💡 Applications for the 6th edition of the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/pt/sobre-nos/projetos-para-um-futuro-melhor/social-equity-initiative/leapfrog/candidaturas-6%C2%AA-edicao">Nova SBE Social Leapfrog program</a> are open until May 3rd</p><p>💡 <strong>Data Makers Fest</strong> A international festival <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.datamakersfest.com/">for all data practitioners and dedicated to practical data work</a>; less theory, more execution, happening from 4 to 6 May in Porto. We have <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tickets.datamakersfest.com/purchase">a discount code for our readers</a> STARTUP-DIGEST-10</p><p>💡 <strong>Tech Hiring Conference</strong> 2026 May 07 by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Landing.Jobs">Landing.Jobs</a> &amp; Damia Group, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/tech-hiring-community-conference-2026">tickets on sale</a></p><p>💡 <strong>START Rise Challenge</strong>, powered by Start Campus is a national platform for bold AI founders to gain visibility, sharpen their ideas, and move closer to real-world pilots. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startrisechallenge.com/#hero">Explore the program and apply until May 07</a></p><p>💡 <strong>May 14–15 | Alfândega do Porto</strong> Where it all connects: we’re heading to @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://simconf.com/">simconference</a> Two days to meet founders, investors, innovation teams, and ecosystem builders. Curated formats that make conversations more relevant and follow-ups easier.  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/sim-conference-2026">30% off with SDG30</a></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“who you hire is the company you build"</p><p>Vinod Khosla </p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 <span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);"><strong>The Ventures Portugal</strong> 2026, </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.the-ventures.com/portugal-2026"><span style="color: rgb(30, 33, 52);">Final and Awards ceremony</span></a><span style="color: rgb(30, 33, 52);"> this Thursday</span></p><p>🔷 Applications for the 7th edition of <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupprize.eu/">European Startup Prize for Mobility</a> are open </p><p>🔷 <strong>omplo Viseu</strong> National Pitch Competition​ - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/ewuuweaf">Startups can apply here</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>Above &amp; Beyond Hangout</strong> | SIM Conference: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/li66wxqm">Make It Count</a> this Wednesday</p><p>🔷 <strong>START Lisbon</strong> Career Fair, will take place on 11 May 2026 at Unicorn Factory Lisbon.</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏   <strong>Tomas Moreno</strong> (Head of Innovation Ecosystem at EDP) named among the Top 50 senior corporate innovation leaders in Europe. </p><p>👏   <strong>Antonio Miguel</strong> (Maze Impact) speaker at Impact Europe</p><p>👏   Startups selected to be present at Rock In Rio - Smart City of Rock: <strong>Getvocalai, Infinite Foundry, Sensaway, Planta smart homes, Trash4goods, Windcredible, Goparkly, Alia, Meetball, Indulge Me, Katchit, Yooddle, </strong>and<strong> VRGlass</strong></p><p>👏   <strong>Miha Jagodic</strong> and <strong>João Lopes</strong> (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Bloq.it">Bloq.it</a>) featured on Forbes 30 Under 30 Europe Class of 2026 </p><p>👏   <strong>Unicage</strong>, <strong>CoalexAI</strong>, and <strong>Lympid </strong>had been selected for the Visa Innovation Program Europe 2026 Spain &amp; Portugal Edition</p><p>👏   <strong>Upspeach</strong> won Startups by the Sea pitch competition</p><p> 👏   <strong>Sybilion</strong> announced a 3.6M seed round</p><p>👏   <strong>Matching Founders</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://matchingfounders.cc/startup-ideas">launched a new chapter</a> in San Francisco</p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 O ativo mais subestimado de Portugal é a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://executivedigest.sapo.pt/o-ativo-mais-subestimado-de-portugal-e-a-capacidade-de-combinar-tecnologia-de-topo-com-grandes-projetos-de-investimento-admite-fernando-fraga/?utm_source=dlvr.it&amp;utm_medium=linkedin">capacidade de combinar tecnologia de topo com grandes projetos de investimento</a> com Fernando Fraga</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://observador.pt/opiniao/teatro-da-inovacao-a-ilusao-que-sai-cara/">Teatro da inovação</a>: a ilusão que sai cara por Tomás Moreno</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://publications.jrc.ec.europa.eu/repository/handle/JRC146239">Is Europe losing its startups</a>? by European Commission</p><p>📚 Jarna Hyvönen, Volare: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eu.vc/p/jarna-hyv-nen-volare-why-climate-hardware-startups-need-a-new-funding-playbook">Why Climate Hardware Startups Need a New Funding Playbook</a></p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://medium.com/@efantinatti/philosophy-eats-ai-how-critical-thinking-can-help-us-survive-and-thrive-with-artificial-95f444cdf026">Thinking can help Us survive and thrive</a> with Artificial Intelligence by E. Fantinatti</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://insights.euclid.vc/p/no-country-for-old-founders">No Country for Old Founders</a>: Why domain expertise is becoming more important in Vertical AI, not less</p><p>🎧 Andreas Munk speaks with Sasha Vidiborskiy, Atomico: How to Think About Deep Tech Investing</p><p>🎥  The Neuron: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/S8qYC3i_g9E?si=lE1Li9pCEbHsBMLR">AI Hallucinations Are Overloading Healthcare</a> </p><p>🎥  André Dionísio &amp; Totas Rodrigues on<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4rKekXCvE_Y"> Building ByTheLaw to Revolutionize Legal Knowledge</a> | TLOAF</p><p>🎥  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/cSWvm7nu1rI?si=iBG-svBQ2z_Ykns1">The End of Work: Vinod Khosla's Bold AI Prediction</a> | Titans and Disruptors</p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Where Research Meets Reality | Week 16</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/where-research-meets-reality-week-16</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/where-research-meets-reality-week-16</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 20 Apr 2026 08:21:44 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>and Why Portugal Can’t Ignore It Somewhere along the way, we convinced ourselves that research and execution pull in opposite directions. That one belongs to universities and the other to startups; that research slows you down and the market speeds you up. As if science were a luxury and execution…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3>and Why Portugal Can’t Ignore It</h3><p>Somewhere along the way, we convinced ourselves that research and execution pull in opposite directions. That one belongs to universities and the other to startups; that research slows you down and the market speeds you up. As if science were a luxury and execution the only thing that matters. It’s a false choice and one that costs Portugal more than we admit.</p><p>This week I read Pedro Bizarro’s reflection on reaching one hundred patents. A Portuguese company, born from academic research, shaping a global industry with scientific depth and commercial clarity. It’s a reminder that innovation doesn’t come from choosing between research and business. It comes from refusing to separate them.</p><p>In Portugal, we still treat academia and startups like two neighbours who nod politely but never really talk. Universities optimise for publications; startups optimise for survival. One moves slowly, the other too fast. And somewhere in the middle, we lose the opportunity to build things that last. But then comes a very Portuguese truth: We don’t lack talent; we lack translation. Translation between discovery and application. Between theory and product. Between what is possible and what is actually useful.</p><p>Feedzai built that bridge early. Not because it was fashionable, but because it was necessary. They proved that deep research is not the enemy of speed, it’s the foundation of defensibility. And they did it from Portugal, which should make us think twice before repeating the old line that “we’re too small”.</p><p>I look at Braga effort to become a deep‑tech engine; at Coimbra, which keeps producing scientific talent any country would fight for; at Porto, blending engineering with industry in a way that feels almost inevitable; and at Lisbon, bringing density, ambition and the world knocking at the door. Even Madeira and Faro are starting to find their own angles.</p><p>The ingredients are here. What’s missing is alignment.</p><ul><li><p>Researchers who see the market as a path to relevance, not a threat.</p></li><li><p>Founders who understand that scientific depth is not a delay, but a moat.</p></li><li><p>Companies willing to invest before the return is obvious.</p></li><li><p>Universities that open the door without fear of losing territory.</p></li><li><p>Policies that reward impact, not just output.</p></li></ul><p>Countries that lead in innovation aren’t the ones with the most research or the most startups. They’re the ones that manage to connect the two.</p><p>I feel that Portugal is close, closer than we think. But bridges don’t build themselves and ecosystems don’t mature by accident. If we want to compete globally, we need to stop treating research and business as separate worlds. They are two halves of the same engine. And when they run together, they move a country forward.</p><p>Let me close this week's Adamastor with great news for Portugal’s startup ecosystem. The winning team from <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://swloule.com/">Startup Weekend Women Loulé</a> “Closure.” has been selected among the 10 global finalists of the Techstars pitch competition. Out of 38 cities worldwide, “Closure.” will represent Loulé and Portugal in the final online pitch.</p><p>What started as one weekend of ideas, courage, and execution is now reaching the global stage. A proud moment for everyone helping grow the startup ecosystem across Portugal reminding us that we can build from anywhere.</p><p>💡 <strong>Data Makers Fest</strong> A international festival <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.datamakersfest.com/">for all data practitioners and dedicated to practical data work</a>; less theory, more execution, happening from 4 to 6 May in Porto. We have <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tickets.datamakersfest.com/purchase">a discount code for our readers</a> STARTUP-DIGEST-10</p><p>💡 <strong>Tech Hiring Conference</strong> 2026 May 07 by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Landing.Jobs">Landing.Jobs</a> &amp; Damia Group, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/tech-hiring-community-conference-2026">tickets on sale</a></p><p>💡 <strong>May 14–15 | Alfândega do Porto</strong> Where it all connects: we’re heading to @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://simconf.com/">simconference</a> Two days to meet founders, investors, innovation teams, and ecosystem builders. Curated formats that make conversations more relevant and follow-ups easier.  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/sim-conference-2026">30% off with SDG30</a></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“Vision without execution is hallucination"</p><p>Thomas Edison</p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 The <strong>inNOVAetors Academy</strong> IS BACK and presents a 6-week intensive designed for action-takers that prioritize execution over discussion. No experience needed—just the drive to turn ideas into impact. Applications open until Apr 20</p><p>🔷 How to Master Your Pitch at <strong>Nova SBE</strong> this Thursday</p><p>🔷 <strong>Digital Built Accelerator</strong> Built for the innovators of construction. Prioritizing Construtech, Contech  and  New Materials. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.digitalbuiltaccelerator.pt/">Applications open</a> until Apr 24</p><p>🔷 <strong>Subvisual</strong>'s Starbase in Coimbra this Friday </p><p>🔷 <strong>The Future Innovators Hackathon</strong>: A Road to START Hack. Build bold MVPs in 24 hours, in person with mentors and entrepreneurs from the Unicorn Factory ecosystem. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://future-innovators-hackathon.devpost.com/">Apply Apr 25</a></p><p>🔷 Applications for the 7th edition of <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupprize.eu/">European Startup Prize for Mobility</a> are open </p><p>🔷 <strong>LisboaUX</strong>: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://medium.com/@malikpiara/lisboaux-introducing-ai-job-pages-af0284cd72c0">launch new AI Job Pages </a></p><p>🔷 <strong>omplo Viseu</strong> National Pitch Competition​ - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/ewuuweaf">Startups can apply here</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>START Lisbon</strong> Career Fair, will take place on 11 May 2026 at Unicorn Factory Lisbon.</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏   <strong>GovHorizon</strong> raised 292k</p><p>👏   <strong>Instaleap </strong>has been acquired by Instacart</p><p>👏    <strong>FLASHGuard Project</strong> , <strong>Dermamatica</strong> and <strong>clea</strong> the top 3 startups at MIT 100k</p><p>👏   launch of ​<strong>Center for Entrepreneurship, Growth &amp; Competitiveness</strong> at Porto Business School </p><p>👏   <strong>Granter </strong><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);">going to the global finale of The Pitch by Deel </span></p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.feedzai.com/blog/100-patents-innovation-fraud-detection/">100-Patent Milestone</a>: Why R&amp;D and Innovation are Feedzai’s Secret Weapon by Pedro Bizarro </p><p>📚 Europe's Startup Ecosystem: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/europes-startup-ecosystem-data-opportunity-a-clear-support-zysze/">A Data Opportunity</a>-A clear support for policymakers</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://thv.vc/insights/gtm-scaling-us">SCALING INTO THE U.S</a>.: Culture, Pace, and Psychology by Maria Burpee</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://bbycroft.net/llm">Visualization and walkthrough</a> of the algorithm that backs ChatGPT </p><p>📚 Anthropic trava modelo de IA <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://pt.euronews.com/next/2026/04/08/anthropic-trava-modelo-de-ia-mythos-preview-por-risco-excessivo-para-o-publico">Mythos Preview</a> por risco excessivo para o público</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ricardo-vargas.com/podcasts/anthropic-mythos-when-ai-creates-risks-we-cannot-predict/">Anthropic Mythos</a>: When AI Creates Risks We Cannot Predict</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.founderspodcast.com/episodes/412-how-roger-federer-works">Founders</a>: How Roger Federer Works</p><p>🎥 Negócios sem trela: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/i3E4v1D0YnQ?si=-yBY-ADkk7foGw6Y">Como Ser Uma Mulher Empreendedora em Portugal</a>?</p><p>🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/GyiqK7Ifq7Q?si=poI58cnRawNlgMXF">What AI can't do</a>, and why you can by Svetlana Makarova</p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>In Times Like These, Builders Matter Even More | Week 15</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/in-times-like-these-builders-matter-even-more-week-15</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/in-times-like-these-builders-matter-even-more-week-15</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 13 Apr 2026 22:36:59 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>The world feels unstable again. Conflicts rise, tensions spread, and uncertainty has become part of our daily vocabulary. From Ukraine to the Middle East, from political shocks to economic volatility, it often seems like we are living in a permanent state of disruption. And yet, throughout history,…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>The world feels unstable again. Conflicts rise, tensions spread, and uncertainty has become part of our daily vocabulary. From Ukraine to the Middle East, from political shocks to economic volatility, it often seems like we are living in a permanent state of disruption.</p><p>And yet, throughout history, it is in moments like these that people step forward to build. Not because the world is calm, but precisely because it isn’t.</p><p>Entrepreneurs have always been part of that group. They look at problems the way others look at opportunities, not with naive optimism, but with a stubborn belief that something better can be created. It’s almost a reflex: when they see a challenge, they start imagining solutions. Yesterday, during a Founders Communication Workshop, I saw a clear example of this. Manon’s pitch reminded me exactly of what I’m writing here: the instinct to build, even when the world feels uncertain.</p><p>This is the part of entrepreneurship we sometimes forget. Behind the pitch decks, the metrics, the fundraising cycles, there is a simple truth: building a company is, at its core, an act of service. It is choosing to respond to the world’s problems with action instead of resignation.</p><p>Entrepreneurs will not solve everything alone. No one can. But without them, many of the solutions we need would never leave the paper, the lab, or the imagination.</p><p>And this is why communities like ours matter. Because behind every founder trying to make a difference, there must be a network that supports, challenges, and believes in them, especially in times like these.</p><p>💡 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/core">Portugal Spring 2026 Program</a> is accepting applications</p><p>💡 <strong>Data Makers Fest</strong> A international festival <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.datamakersfest.com/">for all data practitioners and dedicated to practical data work</a>; less theory, more execution, happening from 4 to 6 May in Porto. We have <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tickets.datamakersfest.com/purchase">a discount code for our readers</a> STARTUP-DIGEST-10</p><p>💡 <strong>Tech Hiring Conference</strong> 2026 May 07 by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Landing.Jobs">Landing.Jobs</a> &amp; Damia Group, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/tech-hiring-community-conference-2026">tickets on sale</a></p><p>💡 <strong>May 14–15 | Alfândega do Porto</strong> Where it all connects: we’re heading to @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://simconf.com/">simconference</a> Two days to meet founders, investors, innovation teams, and ecosystem builders. Curated formats that make conversations more relevant and follow-ups easier.  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/sim-conference-2026">30% off with SDG30</a></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“Entrepreneurship is jumping off a cliff and assembling the plane on the way down.”</p><p>Reid Hoffman</p></blockquote><p></p><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷  The Pitch Competition, in collaboration with the <strong>Nova Startup Club</strong> is accepting <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://forms.office.com/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=4zEpxDNn5kGNQsSLozS7pPhwOfy3yaRIvHOfWATJhOdUM1lLRURGN1dHSzFRRzJDSlRaSFhaT0MxUy4u&amp;utm_source=luma&amp;route=shorturl">applications</a> until tomorrow</p><p>🔷  <strong>The Ventures Award</strong> identifies high-potential startups and connects them with a network of leaders from 119 VC funds and business angels, collectively managing over $11 billion in assets. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.the-ventures.com/portugal-2026">Apply until Apr 16</a></p><p>🔷 The <strong>inNOVAetors Academy</strong> IS BACK and presents a 6-week intensive designed for action-takers that prioritize execution over discussion. No experience needed—just the drive to turn ideas into impact. Applications open until Apr 20</p><p>🔷 <strong>Digital Built Accelerator</strong> Built for the innovators of construction. Prioritizing Construtech, Contech  and  New Materials. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.digitalbuiltaccelerator.pt/">Applications open</a> until Apr 24</p><p>🔷 <strong>The Future Innovators Hackathon</strong>: A Road to START Hack. Build bold MVPs in 24 hours, in person with mentors and entrepreneurs from the Unicorn Factory ecosystem. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://future-innovators-hackathon.devpost.com/">Apply Apr 25</a></p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏   <strong>Porto Tech Hub Academy</strong> was launched </p><p>👏   <strong>UFL Spring Batch</strong> ‘26 is here with 46 new startups </p><p>👏   <strong>Porto Tech Hub Academy</strong> launched</p><p>👏   <strong>SEA4FEED</strong>, <strong>SEA2RegenAg</strong>, and <strong>BIOSEA+</strong>, are among the global finalists in the Innovation Awards Roullier </p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 Lisbon’s <strong>Bondstone</strong> launches VC arm and unveils <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eu-startups.com/2026/04/lisbons-bondstone-launches-vc-arm-and-unveils-e50-million-deeptech-fund/">€50 million DeepTech fund</a></p><p>📚 10 keys to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.cuatrecasas.com/en/portugal/corporate/art/10-keys-venture-capital-transactions-portugal-1">venture capital transactions in Portugal</a> by Cuatrecasas</p><p>📚 Sycophantic <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.aec8352">AI decreases prosocial intentions and promotes dependence</a></p><p>🎧 Ferrari ship just 14,000 cars per year (Toyota sells that many every 10 hours), yet over a billion people know what a Ferrari is. It's the highest ratio of brand awareness to actual customers of any company in history. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.acquired.fm/episodes/ferrari">Acquired studied</a> one of the most paradoxical companies.</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tr.ee/k7gwltzyOS">Luso Lab</a>, o podcast que divulga o talento português além-fronteiras; convidado: Ricardo Marvão</p><p>🎥 O <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/ICyX7Fsaj70?si=qy3wcYImOVfDsah6">Papel dos Business Angels e das Incubadoras no Ecossistema Empreendedor</a> com Ivanoel Rodrigues</p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Knowledge in Motion  | Week 14</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/knowledge-in-motion-week-14</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/knowledge-in-motion-week-14</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 06 Apr 2026 07:57:29 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>When Knowledge Leaves the University Walls, Everyone Wins For years we’ve repeated the same sentence in Portugal: “knowledge must leave the universities and reach the companies.” It sounds obvious, but when you listen closely to the people who live this bridge every day, you realise the work is…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3><strong>When Knowledge Leaves the University Walls, Everyone Wins</strong></h3><p>For years we’ve repeated the same sentence in Portugal: “knowledge must leave the universities and reach the companies.” It sounds obvious, but when you listen closely to the people who live this bridge every day, you realise the work is only now beginning to take shape.</p><p>Two recent events that took place made me write this week editorial. The BMI Students Pitch, where I participated as a jury and the episode of Negócio com Impacto, recorded at Católica Lisbon, where this thematics was brought to life with a simple but powerful message: knowledge does not move by itself. As João Cotter Salvado said "<em>Academics often produce knowledge for other academics. That’s not enough to reach the people inside companies.</em>”</p><h3>The heart of the challenge and the opportunity</h3><p>The academy is moving, no doubt about it. There’s intention, there are programs like <em>Forward</em>, and there’s a growing push from reitorias to bring innovation closer to students. But the incentives still don’t fully match. Universities produce knowledge at a very high level, while many companies, especially smaller ones, struggle to absorb it. Without real proximity, shared language, and hybrid profiles, the bridge remains fragile.</p><p>Even so, something important is happening: more co‑creation, more multidisciplinary work, and more people capable of translating academic depth into practical value. That’s where the future is being built.</p><p>We can already see this in our ecosystem, the connection between academia and the market is visible; have to mention <em>APG - Startup HR Pitch</em>, as one good example. Ideas born in classrooms become prototypes, then startups, then companies ready to scale. Students meet founders, founders meet researchers, and companies meet talent. And when we look at the strongest European hubs, the pattern is obvious: the best incubators live inside universities. Portugal is moving in that direction and Braga, Porto, Coimbra and Lisbon are clearly leading.</p><p>But the market still moves slower than the talent. Granter’s story shows this perfectly: a clear problem, a strong solution, cutting‑edge technology and still months of bureaucracy just to work with large companies. The talent is here, the technology is here, the will is here; but the path is still too long. If we want Portugal to compete globally, this needs to accelerate. </p><p>Another important shift is happening in who becomes a founder. Innovation is no longer something reserved for business students, and that’s a strength. More than half of the founders supported by Unicorn Factory come from medicine, engineering, biotechnology, humanities. Innovation emerges when deep expertise meets real‑world problems. What we need now is more multidisciplinary teams and more space to test ideas early.</p><p>And yes, we still struggle with failure. In Portugal, success is celebrated, but failure is quietly avoided. Yet innovation depends on experimentation, and experimentation depends on accepting that some things won’t work. With AI lowering the cost of testing, there’s no reason to wait for perfection before going to market.</p><p>This is where <strong>Adamastor</strong> steps in. Our role is to reinforce the bridge, to make our contribution that knowledge doesn’t stay trapped inside universities, and that companies know how to absorb and apply it. We make our part on connecting research with execution, talent with opportunity, ideas with the people who can help them grow. Giving voice and being side by side with founders, students, researchers, corporates, and ecosystem leaders to turn knowledge into movement. Into impact. Into companies that matter.</p><h3><strong>The future is clear: knowledge applied, talent in motion, impact at scale</strong></h3><p>What I witnessed these last days at Catolica, confirms what many of us already feel: Portugal has everything it needs to build a world‑class innovation ecosystem. But it will only happen if we accelerate the connection between academia and the market.</p><ul><li><p>Universities must open their doors</p></li><li><p>Companies must open their minds</p></li><li><p>Ecosystem players must open the paths</p></li></ul><p>And players like <strong>Adamastor</strong> must keep building the bridges.</p><p>Because when knowledge leaves the university walls, everyone wins: the founders, the companies, the students, the country.</p><p></p><p>💡 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/core">Portugal Spring 2026 Program</a> is accepting applications</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://money-talks.pt/"><strong>Money Talks</strong></a> the biggest financial literacy event in the country, takes place on <strong>April 11 &amp; 12</strong>. Tickets are now on sale use<span style="color: rgb(224, 0, 0);"> </span>promocode: ADAMASTOR</p><p>💡 <strong>Tech Hiring Conference</strong> 2026 May 07 by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Landing.Jobs">Landing.Jobs</a> &amp; Damia Group, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/tech-hiring-community-conference-2026">tickets on sale</a></p><p>💡 <strong>Data Makers Fest</strong> A international festival <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.datamakersfest.com/">for all data practitioners and dedicated to practical data work</a>; less theory, more execution, happening from 4 to 6 May in Porto. We have <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tickets.datamakersfest.com/purchase">a discount code for our readers</a> STARTUP-DIGEST-10</p><p>💡 <strong>May 14–15 | Alfândega do Porto</strong> Where it all connects: we’re heading to @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://simconf.com/">simconference</a> Two days to meet founders, investors, innovation teams, and ecosystem builders. Curated formats that make conversations more relevant and follow-ups easier.  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/sim-conference-2026">30% off with SDG30</a></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“<strong>Knowledge has to be improved, challenged, and increased constantly, or it vanishes”</strong> </p><p><em>Peter F. Drucker</em></p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 <strong>Bitalk Roundtable Live</strong> @ Unicorn Factory, today </p><p>🔷 Fundraising &amp; Investing Strategies @<strong>Nova SBE, </strong>Welcome the Spring Batch '26 @<strong>Carmo Rooftop</strong>, and Scaling from 0 to the first 1000 customers with Tim Ward @<strong>Sitio Rossio</strong>, all this Thursday </p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.innovationsummerschool.com/">Applications are now open</a> for <strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa’s Innovation Summer School</strong>, a summer camp for young people ages 14 to 18 designed to foster a spirit of innovation and entrepreneurship</p><p>🔷 <strong>Money Talks</strong> next weekend @<strong>Aula Magna</strong></p><p>🔷&nbsp;<strong>UPTEC</strong>&nbsp;is&nbsp;looking&nbsp;for&nbsp;𝟑&nbsp;𝐬𝐭𝐚𝐫𝐭𝐮𝐩𝐬,&nbsp;𝐒𝐌𝐄𝐬,&nbsp;𝐨𝐫&nbsp;𝐢𝐧𝐧𝐨𝐯𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧&nbsp;𝐜𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐞𝐫𝐬&nbsp;to&nbsp;develop&nbsp;technological&nbsp;pilots&nbsp;within&nbsp;the&nbsp;scope&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;Interreg&nbsp;Atlantico&nbsp;SaferSEA&nbsp;project.&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScz2So1NBXD36Ad5fNtR_mTq4axYSwBFGdeIMLw2WtbuphhRw/viewform"><u>Apply&nbsp;until</u></a>&nbsp;Apr&nbsp;08</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏  <strong>Remote</strong> was Named One of the Most Innovative Companies in 2026</p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 De meses para minutos: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://news.microsoft.com/source/emea/features/de-meses-para-minutos-como-a-fashable-esta-a-construir-o-futuro-da-moda-com-ia/?lang=pt-pt">como a Fashable está a construir o futuro da moda com IA</a></p><p>📚 “A <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://pmemagazine.sapo.pt/a-inovacao-nao-deve-estar-reservada-aos-grandes-centros-ou-as-grandes-empresas-simplifyer/">inovação não deve estar reservada aos grandes centros ou às grandes empresas</a>” com Isabel Carapeta (Simplifyer)</p><p>📚 RNi – Portugal Incubators | <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupportugal.com/rni-portugal-incubators/network-members/">Full list of Network Members</a></p><p>📚 Sam Altman May Control Our Future — <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2026/04/13/sam-altman-may-control-our-future-can-he-be-trusted">Can He Be Trusted</a>? By Ronan Farrow and Andrew Marantz</p><p>📚 The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.fastcompany.com/91497248/human-resources-most-innovative-companies-2026">most innovative human resources companies</a> of 2026 by Fast Company</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/ai-future-work-filipa-larangeira-mwfae/">AI &amp; The Future of Work</a>, a conversation with Vasco Pedro by Filipa Larangeira</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/4RQt5I7QNoMm4PAdVJCdUH?si=6ekov3AeQG6AemNKM8-Ipw">UPTEC Out Of Office</a>: Ana Ferreira, fundadora e CEO da b_create partilha os desafios de construir e escalar um projeto próprio</p><p>🎧Na conversa com Walter Duarte, Nuno Fernandes, CEO da DIG-IN, fala sobre o seu percurso pessoal e profissional<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/6txbDwu9cEFG623ppjYkaS?si=aE-3LRHJQhyRQl9ApYs9dg"> e sobre como  a Zomato se transformou em dig-in</a> e como, hoje, a estratégia de inovação lhes permitiu  posicionarem-se com uma empresa de dados 360.</p><p>🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f0Ef8mfy-Zs">Negócios com Impacto</a> na Católica Lisbon School of Business and Economics</p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Easter time🐰 | Week 13</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/easter-time-week-13</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/easter-time-week-13</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 30 Mar 2026 08:06:13 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>Entrepreneurs are wired for possibility. Most are risk‑takers, adventurers, passionate builders who wake up every day ready to chase an opportunity. And even though almost all of them carry a few painful failures in their journey, they still show up again and again, to face challenges head‑on.…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Entrepreneurs are wired for possibility. Most are risk‑takers, adventurers, passionate builders who wake up every day ready to chase an opportunity. And even though almost all of them carry a few painful failures in their journey, they still show up again and again, to face challenges head‑on. Failure shapes them; it’s part of the craft.</p><p>As a Christian and a very imperfect one, I sometimes wonder whether Jesus could be seen as a kind of “spiritual entrepreneur”. Someone with vision, courage, strategic clarity, and a willingness to take risks for something bigger than Himself. Whether or not one shares that view, the parallel is interesting: purpose, resilience, and service are at the heart of both paths, the same foundations that quietly sustain every entrepreneurial journey.</p><p><span>Before closing, I want to make a rare exception. I don’t usually highlight individuals in our ecosystem — fortunately, there are many who deserve recognition — but I can’t let this moment pass without acknowledging João Rosado, who is leaving Unicorn Factory. João has consistently worked on behalf of the community with dedication, clarity, and generosity, including in projects where I’ve had the privilege to collaborate with him. His contribution has mattered, and it will continue to echo. All the best, João!!</span></p><p><span>As we enter this Easter break, a moment when many pause, rest, or simply breathe a little deeper, I hope it brings you renewed energy, new aspirations, and a sense of hope for what you’re building.</span></p><p>Wishing you all a peaceful and inspiring Easter time🐰🍛</p><p>💡 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/core">Portugal Spring 2026 Program</a> is accepting applications</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://money-talks.pt/"><strong>Money Talks</strong></a> the biggest financial literacy event in the country, takes place on <strong>April 11 &amp; 12</strong>. Tickets are now on sale use<span style="color: rgb(224, 0, 0);"> </span>promocode: ADAMASTOR</p><p>💡 <strong>Tech Hiring Conference</strong> 2026 May 07 by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Landing.Jobs">Landing.Jobs</a> &amp; Damia Group, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/tech-hiring-community-conference-2026">tickets on sale</a></p><p>💡 <strong>Data Makers Fest</strong> A international festival <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.datamakersfest.com/">for all data practitioners and dedicated to practical data work</a>; less theory, more execution, happening from 4 to 6 May in Porto. We have <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tickets.datamakersfest.com/purchase">a discount code for our readers</a> STARTUP-DIGEST-10</p><p>💡 <strong>May 14–15 | Alfândega do Porto</strong> Where it all connects: we’re heading to @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://simconf.com/">simconference</a> Two days to meet founders, investors, innovation teams, and ecosystem builders. Curated formats that make conversations more relevant and follow-ups easier.  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/sim-conference-2026">30% off with SDG30</a></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“If you don't know where you are going, any road will take you there"</p><p><strong>Lewis Carroll </strong></p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 A <strong>Curated Dinner for Designers &amp; Researchers</strong> by LisboaUX, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/7zu0pvgd">tonight</a>!</p><p>🔷 <strong>Bitalk Roundtable</strong> - Live @ Unicorn Factory next Apr 07. The theme of this Roundtable Live is: Scaling Up in a Trump World. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eventbrite.pt/e/bilhetes-bitalk-roundtable-live-unicorn-factory-1985275789328">Secure your place !</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>Webinar Lean Academy: Da Calamidade à continuidade dos negócios</strong> next Apr 07 at Torres Vedras and Aveiro. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.lean.org.pt/opensessions">Limited spots</a>! </p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.innovationsummerschool.com/">Applications are now open</a> for <strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa’s Innovation Summer School</strong>, a summer camp for young people ages 14 to 18 designed to foster a spirit of innovation and entrepreneurship</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏  <strong>Builtrix</strong>, <strong>Emissium</strong>, <strong>Empresta AI</strong>, and <strong>GreenDash</strong> selected for Sage Impact Entrepreneurship Programme</p><p>👏  <strong>Axios Care</strong>, <strong>Benno AI</strong>, <strong>Cozecare</strong>, <strong>Dermaleaf Cosmetics</strong>, <strong>FermentAtelier</strong>, and <strong>SEIVA</strong> selected for SpinUM – Concurso de Ideias de Negócio da Universidade do Minho / TecMinho</p><p>👏 <strong>Sybilion</strong> announced a 3.6M Seed</p><p>👏 <strong>RF Sentinel</strong>,<strong> Navictus</strong>, and <strong>ROOTkey</strong> are the winners of EUDIS Defence Hackathon</p><p>👏 <strong>Above &amp; Beyond Hangout</strong> just celebrated its 50th edition </p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 André Marquet, CEO da Productized: “<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://jornaleconomico.sapo.pt/noticias/andre-marquet-ceo-da-productized-falta-uma-estrategia-nacional-para-a-nova-defesa/">Falta uma estratégia nacional para a ´nova defesa</a>”</p><p>📚 “<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://linktoleaders.com/os-fundadores-de-start-ups-crescem-mais-depressa-juntos-stewart-noakes-canopy-community/">Os fundadores de start-ups crescem mais depressa juntos</a>” com Stewart Noakes</p><p>📚 Coverflex | <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.coverflex.com/pt/ebooks/estado-da-compensacao-2026">State Of Compensation In Portugal 2026</a></p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://whamnow.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/The-WHAM-Report-The-Bussiness-Case-for-Accelerating-Womens-Health-Investment-1.pdf">The WHAM Report</a>: The Business Case for Accelerating Women’s Health Investment</p><p>📚 It’s AI, so I Didn’t Read, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.thealgorithmicbridge.com/p/its-ai-so-i-didnt-read">we have a new hot term: AI;DR</a>  by Alberto Romero</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://humandimension.substack.com/p/the-responsibility-of-academics-in">The Responsibility of Academics in the Age of AI</a> by Antonio Dias de Figueiredo</p><p>🎧 Conversas com CEO <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.jornaldenegocios.pt/podcast/conversas-com-ceo/detalhe/nuno-comando-e-o-convidado-de-conversas-com-ceo">com Nuno Comando</a> (Casa do Impacto)</p><p>🎥 Startup Nations Standards Report 2025: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://vimeo.com/event/5696096">Online Launch Event</a> <span style="color: rgb(35, 49, 59);"><strong> </strong></span></p><p>🎥 Stephan Moraes (Indico Capital): <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/D4SMES7rKh4?si=zfihHfY1HJkWbV5j">Why Not Everybody Should Be an Entrepreneur</a> with Thomas Viguier and Markus Perkumas</p><p>🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.ainauts.space/c/live-webinars/from-zero-to-hero-with-full-stack-claude-bd380316-dbad-47ac-8d0e-f5e403544b6f">From Zero to Hero with Full Stack Claude</a> by Rui Vas</p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>EU INC and the Rebuild Letter | Week 12</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/eu-inc-and-the-rebuild-letter-week-12</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/eu-inc-and-the-rebuild-letter-week-12</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Mar 2026 12:53:52 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>What they matter for Portuguese Startups Two major European milestones landed almost back‑to‑back: the latest advances in the EU INC framework and the publication of the Rebuild Letter . At first glance, they might look like another round of Brussels centric paperwork. They’re not. Both carry real…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><em>What they matter for Portuguese Startups</em></p><p>Two major European milestones landed almost back‑to‑back: the latest advances in the <strong>EU INC</strong> framework and the publication of the <strong>Rebuild Letter</strong>. At first glance, they might look like another round of Brussels centric paperwork. They’re not. Both carry real consequences for the Portuguese startup ecosystem, an ecosystem that has grown quickly, but still depends on European scale, capital, and regulatory coherence to survive, compete and grow.</p><p><strong>EU INC</strong> is the clearest signal yet that Europe finally understands the cost of fragmentation. For Portuguese founders, this matters more than most people realise. Competing from a country of 10 million people only works if Europe behaves like a single market of 450 million, not 27 regulatory islands pretending to be one. A coordinated industrial and innovation strategy means fewer barriers, faster scaling, and access to deeper capital pools. It means a startup born in Lisbon can grow with the same ambition as one born in Berlin or Paris, without being slowed down by bureaucratic friction.</p><p>The <strong>Rebuild Letter</strong> adds the political backbone; as Stuart Cerne <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/posts/165">highlighted in his piece</a> for Adamastor this week, the Letter is more than a political gesture, it’s a call for Europe to reclaim strategic ambition. It calls for a Europe capable of acting with unity and purpose, especially in technology, security, and economic resilience. For Portugal’s startups, this isn’t abstract rhetoric. It means clearer rules for AI, data, and digital markets; stronger incentives for deep‑tech; and a more predictable environment for investors. When Europe rebuilds its strategic capacity, Portuguese innovators gain a platform that amplifies their impact far beyond national borders.</p><p>Both initiatives point to a truth that is both a strength and a weakness: Portugal cannot rely on its domestic market to support globally competitive companies. No startup scales on 10 million consumers. But it can scale on 450 million, if Europe acts as one Europe, not 27 Europes.</p><p>This is why these milestones matter. <strong>EU INC</strong> and the <strong>Rebuild Letter</strong> are not bureaucratic exercises; they are structural opportunities. They can give Portuguese startups what they need most: scale, stability, and strategic alignment. The alternative is simple and bleak; talent and investment drifting to ecosystems that move faster and think bigger.</p><p>Europe is at a crossroads. If it chooses unity, Portugal’s innovators stand to gain more than most. If it hesitates, the smallest players will pay the price first. Europe has the talent, the resources, and the history to lead; what it needs now is the courage to act as one.</p><p>💡 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/core">Portugal Spring 2026 Program</a> is accepting applications</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://money-talks.pt/"><strong>Money Talks</strong></a> the biggest financial literacy event in the country, takes place on <strong>April 11 &amp; 12</strong>. Tickets are now on sale use<span style="color: rgb(224, 0, 0);"> </span>promocode: ADAMASTOR</p><p>💡 <strong>Tech Hiring Conference</strong> 2026 May 07 by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Landing.Jobs">Landing.Jobs</a> &amp; Damia Group, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/tech-hiring-community-conference-2026">tickets on sale</a></p><p>💡 <strong>May 14–15 | Alfândega do Porto</strong> Where it all connects: we’re heading to @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://simconf.com/">simconference</a> Two days to meet founders, investors, innovation teams, and ecosystem builders. Curated formats that make conversations more relevant and follow-ups easier.  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://3cket.com/en/event/sim-conference-2026">30% off with SDG30</a></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“<strong>Companies are brought, not sold"</strong></p><p><strong>Gonçalo Fortes</strong></p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 Meet the top startup mentors at the <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/event/meet-the-top-startup-mentors-at-the-founder-institute-portugal-portugal-spring-2026.">this Wednesday</a> The majority of this event will be devoted to answering your questions and giving you feedback on your business.</p><p>🔷 <strong>Acceleration Program 10th Edition</strong> by Startup Braga designed for those who have a technological project in the MVP phase that addresses urban and social challenges in one of the following three areas: Sustainability and Smart Cities; Digital Economy and Smart Cities; and Industry and Construction of the Future. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://accelerationprogram.startupbraga.com/">Apply until Mar 31</a></p><p>🔷 until Mar 31 apply to <strong>MIT Portugal</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://mitportugal.org/activity/iwi-2026/about">Innovation Workshop 2026</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>Meet Up LISPOLIS</strong> returns this Thursday with the theme “<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/meet-up-lispolis-tickets-1985051690041">Health Innovation in Lisbon</a>”</p><p>🔷 <strong>UPTEC</strong> is looking for 𝟑 𝐬𝐭𝐚𝐫𝐭𝐮𝐩𝐬, 𝐒𝐌𝐄𝐬, 𝐨𝐫 𝐢𝐧𝐧𝐨𝐯𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐜𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐞𝐫𝐬 to develop technological pilots within the scope of the Interreg Atlantico SaferSEA project. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScz2So1NBXD36Ad5fNtR_mTq4axYSwBFGdeIMLw2WtbuphhRw/viewform">Apply until</a> Apr 08</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏  <strong>Sybilion</strong> announced a 3.6M Seed</p><p>👏  <strong>VaultHaus</strong> and <strong>CarePlus</strong> are the winners of the Unicorn Factory Lisboa Incubation Program’s Demo Day</p><p>👏  <strong>Portugal Ventures</strong> exits Fever</p><p>👏  <strong>Feedzai </strong>was named to Fast Company's list of the World's Most Innovative Companies</p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 André Dionísio <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.valormagazine.pt/a-nova-geracao-de-pme-digitais/">transformou uma inquietação académica numa startup legaltech</a>, a ByTheLaw</p><p>📚 Portugal, a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/portugal-feitoria-digital-da-am%C3%A9rica-miguel-sousa-soares-mba-isixe/">Feitoria Digital da América</a> por Miguel Sousa Soares</p><p>📚 Flamaid lleva a la ONU <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://forbes.es/forbes-30-under-30/889833/flamaid-onu-granada-seguridad-julieta-ruef/">la tecnología pensada para proteger a las mujeres</a></p><p>📚 Fast Company's list of the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.fastcompany.com/91497102/data-science-most-innovative-companies-2026">World's Most Innovative Companies</a></p><p>📚 Your Startup <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/your-startup-probably-dead-arrival-steve-blank-qfktc/">is Probably Dead On Arrival</a> by Steve Blank</p><p>📚 If You Want to Build Community, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://vivekmurthy.substack.com/p/if-you-want-to-build-community-you">You Have to “Waste Time” with People</a> by Vivek Murthy</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/6S746HarZN9O2fNsgSWpv1?si=VlYPLEE5Rg--JlWx-a2_zw">Startups e Ecossistemas Digitais</a> com Elisa Tarzia e Jorge Remondes </p><p>🎧 '3 Dados de Conversa' – <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/1sseqdYHW5qBVB1gnzKuVD?si=XKLEFoDjSbKWUlxxvot77A">Immersive Technologies, Education &amp; Industry</a> com Maria Ribeiro Soares e Lénia Mestrinho</p><p>🎥 How To <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a1iDb4-NFQA">Find Amazing Startup Ideas Faster</a> with Charlier Ward and Sabba Keynejad</p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Why Europe&apos;s next great companies will be built differently, and why I’m betting on Lisbon</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/why-europes-next-great-companies-will-be-built-differently-and-why-i-m-betting-on-lisbon</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/why-europes-next-great-companies-will-be-built-differently-and-why-i-m-betting-on-lisbon</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Mar 2026 16:26:48 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Stuart Cerne</dc:creator>
      <description>One of the hardest parts of being a founder is the loneliness. You live in a future that does not yet exist, people around you struggle to understand you. Your mum hopes you get a proper job. A lot has been written about what makes Silicon Valley special. Much of it comes down to one thing: being…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span>One of the hardest parts of being a founder is the loneliness.</span></p><p><span>You live in a future that does not yet exist, people around you struggle to understand you. Your mum hopes you get a proper job.</span></p><p><span>A lot has been written about what makes Silicon Valley special. Much of it comes down to one thing: being surrounded by people who understand and cheer for you.</span></p><p><span>But I think the next generation of great companies won't be built by recreating that. They'll be built by founders who are responding to something deeper: a growing exhaustion with platforms that manipulate, systems that extract, and companies that treat growth as permission to do harm.</span></p><p><span>People aren't just craving better products. They're craving companies they can actually trust.</span></p><p><span>That is a different brief. And it calls for a different kind of founder, building in a different kind of place.</span></p><p><span>What I've found in Lisbon, and what I believe is quietly becoming Europe's greatest advantage, is a generation of builders who are ambitious enough to compete globally, and principled enough to refuse the old playbook. Companies rooted in openness, collaboration, and a simple but radical idea: that success should be defined by earning trust, not just capturing attention.</span></p><p><span>And in many ways, it proves that the time for Europe has come.</span></p><h2>Arriving With Nothing But an Idea</h2><p><span>I've been building ventures for more than twenty years across China, Hong Kong, London, New York, and other global hubs. I've seen what works, and what doesn't, in places where billions flow into innovation.</span></p><p><span>Lisbon was different. I didn't come here to launch a startup. I came on holiday: a surf trip during a long sabbatical. I knew no one. No network. No co-founders, investors, or team.</span></p><p><span>When I decided to build again, I had to start from scratch. That's why I want to share this story: to break the self-fulfilling prophecy I'm tired of hearing, that you have to move away to make it.</span></p><p><span>My journey as a startup builder in Lisbon started at Web Summit. I walked into a room full of strangers and did something reckless: I stood up and asked for help turning an idea into reality.</span></p><p><span>What happened next didn't just confirm I was in the right place. It made me realise Lisbon may be one of the best places in the world to build a startup right now.</span></p><h2>A Calculated Bet on Builders</h2><p><span>Here's one anecdote that proves my point: last September, Meetball (the startup I am working on) was still just a prototype, far from ready for public use.</span></p><p><span>I explained the vision to João Nunes Rosado at Unicorn Factory Lisboa. He told me their flagship event, the Entrepreneurship Awards, was coming up. Then he asked a simple question:</span></p><p><span>Would Meetball be ready to test there?</span></p><p><span>It was a huge opportunity. The team went all in, nights and days of relentless work. When the event arrived, the product was rough, but it worked well enough: more than half of the participants engaged, made connections, and gave feedback that shaped the product.</span></p><p><span>João and his team weren't naive. They had reviewed and set minimum requirements before supporting us. It wasn't blind trust, it was a calculated bet on builders. A safe path would have been to wait until the product was "perfect." Instead, they gave us the chance to test and improve. The kind of early support that startups need.</span></p><p><span>Lisbon's ecosystem is full of institutions and people that don't just cheer, they give startups real opportunities to prove themselves.</span></p><h2>The Startup Ecosystem</h2><p><span>Lisbon's startup ecosystem is built by people who value collaboration and actively support one another. Everyone is busy, yet everyone seems to have the time to lend a hand when asked.</span></p><p><span>When we needed office space, VCs like Ground Capital and startups like Wincredible offered theirs. When we needed guidance on setting up a company, Startup Lisboa's One Stop Shop provided practical support. When we needed fresh talent, Nova University Lisbon and Técnico opened doors, bringing energy and experimentation into our team.</span></p><p><span>Communities like the 351 Portuguese Startup Association, Redbridge, Portugal Tech Week, and local chapters of Startup Grind and Techstars act as the connective tissue of the ecosystem. Together, they create something bigger than any single entity, the hallmark of a true startup community.</span></p><h2>The Competitive Advantage of Europe</h2><p><span>People are exhausted by platforms that manipulate them, systems that mislead them, and companies that treat growth as a license to extract.</span></p><p><span>The next wave of great founders aren't idealists. They want to generate real wealth, because they understand that money brings influence, and influence is how you change systems. But they refuse to do it by eroding the thing that actually makes a company last: trust.</span></p><p><span>It turns out the world is hungry for exactly that balance. Companies built by people who deeply care about what they are solving will earn trust by being open about the choices they make.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span>That combination, ambition without compromise, may be Europe's greatest competitive advantage. And investors who understand that are already paying attention.</span></p><p><span>Several forces are converging in Lisbon right now that point to something bigger than one city's success story. Global operators arriving with capital and hard-won experience. Portuguese who built careers abroad and came back with global networks and a desire to contribute. A young generation of local founders who no longer believe they have to leave to build something ambitious.</span></p><p><span>I see it in my own team. The people building with us refuse to compromise their values for short-term gain. But they are building for the world.</span></p><p><span>I believe Europe won't just produce more successful companies. It will produce companies worth believing in. And Lisbon, with its unique mix of global talent, returning diaspora, and homegrown ambition, is where I place that bet.</span></p><h2>The Builder Mindset</h2><p>I could write an essay about what frustrates me about building in Lisbon. Investors can be risk-averse. Bureaucracy is a pain. There is literally an office called "Empresa na Hora" (Company in One Hour) where incorporating a company can still take months.</p><p>Or I can tell you about all the great things that make it super cool to build here! What defines this city is the response to problems.</p><p>I remember venting to João at Startup Portugal about how long it was taking to incorporate our company. He asked one simple question:</p><p>"Give me one practical thing we can improve."</p><p>The energy here is focused on solving challenges. Discussions center on attracting investors, supporting growth, and preparing the ecosystem for the next stage. The 351 Association is a perfect example: founders, investors, and policymakers working together, not waiting for someone else to build it.</p><p>Lisbon also has a unique scale. It feels like a village, you run into the same people at events, cafés, coworking spaces, and meetups. Yet it's big enough to test ideas at city scale. This village-city balance creates fertile ground for experimentation.</p><p>The community ties it all together. People cheer, give feedback, and push you to improve. Belief plus accountability, that is how ecosystems thrive.</p><p>Having built across multiple global ecosystems, I can say there is something special about building in Lisbon.</p><h2>A City Full of Builders</h2><p>Every week is packed with startup events, meetups, talks, demo nights, and gatherings.</p><p>Those conversations form the connective tissue of the ecosystem. If you're a founder in Lisbon, you don't need to cook, there's always someone handing out pizza at a cool event. But the real value is the advice, the network, and the collaborative energy.</p><p>I built my entire team by going to events and sharing my vision. The builders are here.</p><h2>The Bet I'm Still Making</h2><p>I arrived in Lisbon with no contacts, no network, and no plan to start a company.</p><p>One year later, I’m surrounded by collaborators and supporters who genuinely want to see us succeed.&nbsp;</p><p>That didn’t happen because Lisbon is perfect. Every emerging ecosystem has its challenges.</p><p>And to be clear, I don’t believe Lisbon is the only place where great startups can be built. Strong ecosystems exist in many cities around the world. Trying to rank them or declare a single “best place” misses the point.</p><p>What actually matters is something much simpler.</p><p><strong>Ecosystems become great when the people inside them decide to make them great.</strong>&nbsp;When communities focus not just on what is missing, but on how to build what is needed. That is the spirit I have experienced in Lisbon.</p><p>I arrived here knowing no one. One year later I'm building with people who refuse to compromise and refuse to stay small. Lisbon is where that generation is gathering. I know, because I'm building with them.</p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>AI: from buzzword to competitive advantage  | Week 11</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/ai-from-buzzword-to-competitive-advantage-week-11</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/ai-from-buzzword-to-competitive-advantage-week-11</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Mar 2026 08:52:19 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>And what the Portuguese ecosystem really needs to do A few days ago, Building The Future delivered a clear message: the experimentation phase in AI is over. We’ve entered the moment where technology must translate into real competitive advantage and anyone who doesn’t make that transition will…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>And what the Portuguese ecosystem really needs to do</p><p>A few days ago, Building The Future delivered a clear message: the experimentation phase in AI is over. We’ve entered the moment where technology must translate into real competitive advantage and anyone who doesn’t make that transition will simply be left behind.</p><p>But what does this actually mean for the Portuguese entrepreneurial ecosystem?</p><p>It means that having “an AI startup” is no longer enough. You need to prove impact, scale business models, integrate AI into core processes and, above all, build products that solve real problems, not just polished demos for the stage. Competitive advantage doesn’t come from the technology itself, but from the ability to turn it into efficiency, speed, personalization and new business models.</p><p>This point was reinforced by both Bernardo Correia, Secretary of State, and Andrés Ortola, from Microsoft Portugal. Bernardo stressed the urgency for Portugal to accelerate AI adoption strategically, not just tactically; build stronger AI infrastructure, and seize European opportunities or risk being left behind. Ortola, in turn, insisted that digital copilots and generative AI will redefine productivity and competitiveness and that Portuguese companies need to position themselves now, not two years from now.</p><p>One of the most striking moments in Ortola’s talk was a slide dedicated to “Intelligence x Trust.” The equation is simple but decisive: having more powerful models isn’t enough, they must be used responsibly, safely and transparently. For Portuguese startups, this isn’t just an ethical principle; it’s a competitive edge. In a market where trust is scarce, those who manage to combine intelligence with trust from day one will be better positioned to scale, attract international clients and plug into global value chains. Ortola made implicit what many still avoid saying: the AI race won’t be won by technology alone, but by the ability to make it trustworthy, auditable and useful in the real world.</p><p>The Portuguese ecosystem has talent, creativity and a community that knows how to collaborate. What’s sometimes missing is ambition aligned with execution. We need to turn pilots into products, prototypes into businesses and enthusiasm into metrics.</p><p>If there’s one message that came out of this Building The Future, it’s that AI is no longer “the future” it’s the factor that will separate those who lead from those who merely watch. And, of course, Portugal and Europe need to decide quickly what role they want to play in this global race.</p><p>Portuguese startups now have a rare opportunity: to use their agility to do what large companies take years to achieve.</p><p><strong>Adamastor</strong> will, as always, be watching closely those who choose to seize this opportunity and turn technology into impact. Because the future is built, but only by those willing to build it.</p><p>💡 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/core">Portugal Spring 2026 Program</a> is accepting applications</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://money-talks.pt/"><strong>Money Talks</strong></a> the biggest financial literacy event in the country, takes place on April 11 &amp; 12. Tickets are now on sale use<span style="color: rgb(224, 0, 0);"> </span>promocode: ADAMASTOR</p><p>💡 <strong>Lisbon AI Week</strong> will be back in 2026 and has an <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://lisbonaiweek.com/call-for-events">open call for events</a></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“<strong>You can’t have innovation without trust</strong>” </p><p>Satya Nadella</p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/event/startup-founder-forum-with-the-founders-from-courtmaster-and-by-the-law.">Founder Institute</a> Startup Founder Forum, with the founders from <strong>CourtMaster</strong> and <strong>By The Law</strong> this Thursday</p><p>🔷 <strong>Portugal XR Meetup</strong> at Porto Innovation Center this Thursday </p><p>🔷  <strong>FabStartLab</strong> 2nd edition - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.fabstartlab.pt/">applications are open</a> </p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://rocket-booster.com/">Applications are now open</a> for <strong>Rocket Booster</strong>, a program that supports innovative startups in the Tourism sector.</p><p>🔷  applications open for <strong>2026 Shilling VC Summer Fellowship</strong></p><p>🔷  <strong>FabStartLab</strong> - 2.ª Edição is accepting <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://www.fabstartlab.pt/">applications</a> until Apr 06</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏  <strong>iLof</strong> selected for the EPIC-X Acceleration+ Programme among strong European deep-tech startups</p><p>👏  <strong>Leonor Pereira</strong> (<strong>Lampsy</strong>) won 1st place at Woman Summit 2026</p><p>👏  <strong>VaultHaus</strong> among the winners of Winter Demo Day | Lisbon × Valencia</p><p>👏  <strong>Adeci Group</strong>, <strong>BM2Solar</strong>, <strong>BloodFlow,</strong> <strong>Bloop</strong>, <strong>Chain Reactor</strong>, <strong>DOJO AI</strong>, <strong>Jsonify</strong>, <strong>Litehaus</strong>, <strong>Manie</strong>, and <strong>NextBorder</strong> listed 10 of the most promising startups to keep an eye on by EU-Startups</p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 «Braga <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.diariodominho.pt/entrevista/2026-03-13-braga-pode-afirmar-se-como-destino-europeu-de-empreendedorismo-69b41fac5577d">pode afirmar-se como destino europeu de empreendedorismo</a>» com João Fernandes</p><p>📚 “Portugal tem todas as condições para ser <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://linktoleaders.com/portugal-tem-todas-as-condicoes-para-ser-um-farol-da-inovacao-na-europa-gil-azevedo-unicorn-factory-lisboa/">um farol da inovação na Europa</a>” com Gil Azevedo</p><p>📚 Exploring the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.igd.com/commercial-insight/retail-analysis/futures/articles/exploring-the-technology-behind-the-worlds-largest-autonomous-supermarket/72311">technology behind the world’s largest autonomous supermarket</a>,  Vasco Portugal (Sensei) interview with Toby Pickard </p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.alumni.hbs.edu/stories/Pages/story-impact.aspx?num=9666">A Second Life</a>, in Lisbon</p><p>📚 EU–INC campaign warns: Without a pan-European standard, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tech.eu/2026/03/13/eu-inc-campaign-warns-without-a-pan-european-founders-will-keep-choosing-delaware/">founders will keep choosing Delaware</a></p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/0Qp6ju6U9WHi8JfrzIgGs6?si=c-wwsFi7Tsi-u48tBkS7nQ">AI and Mobility</a> com Bruno Jardim</p><p>🎥 Inovadores - Productized: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/WMOn9XHPFN4?si=E0hnv0jkTTei-og6">Bastidores do maior evento de gestão de produto em Portuga</a>l com André Marquet</p><p>🎥 OpenClaw Creator: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/4uzGDAoNOZc?is=oMVMbGXBaNs7Au93">Why 80% Of Apps Will Disappear</a></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>International Women’s Day | Week 10</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/international-women-s-day-week-10</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/international-women-s-day-week-10</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 09 Mar 2026 09:35:53 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>Last Sunday, the world celebrated International Women’s Day , a moment to honour the women who have shaped our past and continue to push our societies toward a fairer and more ambitious future. The date has passed, yes, but the mission doesn’t pause on Monday. Supporting, uplifting and giving…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Last Sunday, the world celebrated <strong>International Women’s Day</strong>, a moment to honour the women who have shaped our past and continue to push our societies toward a fairer and more ambitious future. The date has passed, yes, but the mission doesn’t pause on Monday. Supporting, uplifting and giving visibility to women is something that must happen every single day, especially in entrepreneurship, where recognition is still far from balanced.</p><p>At <strong>Adamastor</strong>, we take this seriously. We see the resilience, the courage and the persistence of women founders who keep building, even when the path is harder than it should be. Your work matters. Your leadership matters. And your impact is felt across the ecosystem, whether or not the spotlight is always there.</p><p>This week, we also celebrate four incredible women from our community; Cintia Mano, Cristina Fonseca, Elisa Tarzia and Joana Pinto, who were named among the 100 most influential women shaping the European startup and venture capital ecosystem in 2026. A well‑deserved recognition and a reminder of the talent that exists right here.</p><p>International Women’s Day may be one day on the calendar, but our commitment is daily. At Adamastor, we stand with women who build, who lead, who challenge the status quo, and who inspire the next generation to do even more.</p><p>Let’s keep championing equality, advocating for change, and empowering one another.</p><p>💡 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/core">Portugal Spring 2026 Program</a> is accepting applications</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://money-talks.pt/"><strong>Money Talks</strong></a> the biggest financial literacy event in the country, takes place on April 11 &amp; 12. Tickets are now on sale use<span style="color: #E00000;"> </span>promocode: ADAMASTOR</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://taikai.network/eudisPortugal/hackathons/2026spring">Applications are open</a> for <strong>EUDIS Defence Hackathon 2026</strong> – Portugal Roadshow </p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“<strong><em>To all women, don’t short yourself. Think big. Take risks"</em></strong></p><p>Christine Lagarde</p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 <strong>Defencetech Meetup Portugal</strong> will take place at Critical Software Lisbon, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/hprdh0vi">Wednesday at 18:00</a>, with the theme ‘Maritime Defence</p><p>🔷 <strong>P-Talks na Feedzai</strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.meetup.com/productized/events/313615677/"><strong> </strong>take place this Thursday</a> with top speakers like Mike Pilawski (ex-Miro) and Feedzai's Head of Research </p><p>🔷 <strong>Founder Institute: Pitch Your Ideas to Portugal's Investors &amp; Experts</strong>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/event/pitch-your-ideas-to-portugal-s-investors-experts-online-portugal-spring-2026.">Online</a> this Wednesday </p><p>🔷 Sword launched <strong>Dawn</strong>. Join the waitlist at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://JoinDawn.com">JoinDawn.com</a></p><p>🔷 “Closure.” with Founders Mima Cibic; ⁠Kamran Thomas Alimagham; ⁠Sophie Dermaux; and ⁠Victoria Robinson were the winning team from the <strong>Startup Weekend Women Loulé</strong> and ⁠now they will prepare to get into the Techstars Weekend Global Online pitch</p><p>🔷 <strong>Demo Day Set.Up IN(dustry)</strong>, today <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.setupguimaraes.com/">in Guimarães</a></p><p>🔷  <strong>FabStartLab</strong> 2nd edition - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.fabstartlab.pt/">applications are open</a> </p><p>🔷 <strong>Startuppers</strong> is your launchpad, fueling ambitions with expert sessions, real cases, and community support. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://351startups.com/startuppers/">The journey kicks off</a> on March 10th with our first session!</p><p>🔷 The networking secret:<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/bilhetes-the-networking-secret-how-communities-can-elevate-your-career-1979855516145"> How communities can elevate your career</a> with Tzufit Herling</p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.fdiintelligence.com/content/a8023cfe-ab4c-4749-984a-bb5d7309f6cd">3 Portuguese projects</a> listed for <strong>Investment Impact Awards 2026</strong>: Operational Small Projects </p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏  <strong>Premios Empreende XXI </strong> finalists: AuroraMed | Immersiv Studios | Invisible CFO | Lampsy Health | SentiVue | Usawa Care | eDynamics Technologies | HUMIVERSO | Medcei | PluggableAI | VaultHaus</p><p>👏  <strong>Altice Labs</strong>; <strong>NOS Inovacao</strong>; e <strong>Sword Health</strong> listed on TOP20 on Barómetro Inventa – Patentes Made in Portugal</p><p>👏  <strong>Cintia Mano</strong>, <strong>Cristina Fonseca</strong>, <strong>Elisa Tarzia</strong>, and <strong>Joana Pinto</strong> were named among the 100 most influential women shaping the European startup and venture capital ecosystem in 2026</p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 2% do capital, o dobro da performance: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tek.sapo.pt/opiniao/artigos/2-do-capital-o-dobro-da-performance-o-paradoxo-das-fundadoras-em-tech">O paradoxo das fundadoras em tech</a></p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/posts/how-i-almost-broke-my-first-company-and-how-i-chose-my-co-founder-differently-the-second-time">How I Almost Broke My First Company</a> And How I Chose My Co-Founder Differently the Second Time by Raza Haider</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://criticalsoftware.com/en/news/critical-software-and-stadler-launch-stadler-digital-labs">Critical Software and Stadler</a> Launch Stadler Digital Labs</p><p>📚 People gathered in Copenhagen to support a simple idea: Europe needs its own social platforms. This is about more than technology; it is about values, trust, and democracy. Take a look at the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://letter.rebuild.net/">Rebuild Letter</a></p><p>📚 Sequoia Capital: The next $1T company won’t sell software. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.theaiopportunities.com/p/sequoia-capital-the-next-1t-company">It will sell the work</a>. by Guillermo Flor</p><p>📚 The Real Numbers: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/real-numbers-what-happens-solo-founders-why-its-than-luis-gon%25C3%25A7alves--0f9xe/">What Happens to Solo Founders</a> (And Why It's Better Than You Think) by Luis Goncalves</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://hbr.org/2026/02/ai-doesnt-reduce-work-it-intensifies-it">AI  Doesn’t Reduce Work</a> It Intensifies It by Aruna Ranganathan and Xingqi Maggie Ye </p><p>🎧 Margarida Barreto '<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/3sDBIoTWaUT1Ppttxu7Ado?si=iq4V2L28QnuY9iO3TxkBOw">Se a criatividade humana não estiver lá</a>, a IA não serve de nada'</p><p>🎥 Dengun: Cria Silicon Valley português no algarve e atrai investidores globais com Miguel Fernandes</p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>How I Almost Broke My First Company And How I Chose My Co-Founder Differently the Second Time</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/how-i-almost-broke-my-first-company-and-how-i-chose-my-co-founder-differently-the-second-time</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/how-i-almost-broke-my-first-company-and-how-i-chose-my-co-founder-differently-the-second-time</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 04 Mar 2026 15:13:38 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Raza Haider</dc:creator>
      <description>I started my first company at 19. First semester of software engineering. Zero money. Zero network. Zero experience. Only obsession. I taught myself everything; design, development, sales, marketing, management, contracts. I would dial 400 leads a day in Karachi, most of them completely cold. I was…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>I started my first company at 19.</p><p>First semester of software engineering.<br>Zero money. Zero network. Zero experience.<br>Only obsession.</p><p>I taught myself everything; design, development, sales, marketing, management, contracts.<br>I would dial 400 leads a day in Karachi, most of them completely cold.<br>I was new. Hungry. Slightly delusional.</p><p>One night, frustrated on the sales floor, I pitched my manager an idea:</p><p>“Let me build a freelancer unit. I’ll bring projects from Upwork. No marketing spend.”</p><p>He said yes.</p><p>Within months, that small experiment became one of the most profitable channels in a 200‑person company. People noticed. Some even approached me to start companies together.</p><p>I said no.</p><p>Until I didn’t.</p><h3>The First Big Mistake</h3><p>A senior colleague — someone who had interviewed me — pitched a partnership.</p><p>“You build it. I’ll stay here for now. Once we’re profitable, I’ll join full‑time.”</p><p>It sounded strategic.<br>I was naive.</p><p>Two years passed. The business grew. He never left his job.</p><p>Then came mistake number two.</p><p>He brought in his brother. Then a friend.</p><p>“Without them we can’t scale.”</p><p>Suddenly we were four partners.</p><p>We eventually hit $1M ARR.</p><p>From the outside, it looked like success.<br>Inside? Chaos.</p><p>Misaligned vision. Poor execution. Premium pricing for mediocre work. Unhappy clients. A culture that didn’t fit.</p><p>And the worst part? I knew we were building something without long‑term alignment.</p><p>In early 2025, I proposed something bold:</p><p>“We should pivot into AI automation.”</p><p>They didn’t see it.</p><p>That’s when I learned a brutal truth:</p><p>Growth doesn’t fix misalignment.<br>It amplifies it.</p><p>So I walked away.</p><h3>Starting Over — Loopless AI</h3><p>I moved to Lisbon on a Digital Nomad Visa.<br>I incorporated <strong>Loopless AI</strong>.<br>I joined Founder Institute Portugal.</p><p>And I made myself a promise:</p><p>Never repeat the co‑founder mistake.</p><p>Because choosing a co‑founder is the highest‑leverage decision in your startup life.<br>It can multiply your vision — or quietly suffocate it.</p><h3>The Co‑Founder Hunt (The Hard Way)</h3><p>I went all in.</p><ul><li><p>Spoke to 15+ mentors</p></li><li><p>Watched 100+ hours of co‑founder advice</p></li><li><p>Signed up for every matching platform</p></li><li><p>Built a spreadsheet of 250+ profiles</p></li><li><p>Interviewed 25+ founders across Europe, the US, and Asia</p></li></ul><p>The best pipeline? YC Co‑Founder Matching.</p><p>But something was always off.</p><p>Skill mismatch.<br>Vision mismatch.<br>Ambition mismatch.</p><p>I wasn’t looking for talent only.<br>I was looking for alignment.</p><h3>The Realization</h3><p>Sometimes you don’t need a new person.<br>You need the right version of someone you already know.</p><p>Back in 2019, as Chairman of IEEE at my university, I met Raheel at a national tech event.<br>He won the national speed programming competition.<br>Brilliant. Calm. Technically exceptional.</p><p>We stayed loosely connected. His last product got acquired.</p><p>When we reconnected during my co‑founder search, something clicked.</p><p>Timing.<br>Maturity.<br>Shared ambition.</p><hr><h3>This Time, We Did It Differently</h3><p>No emotional handshake.<br>No “we’ll figure it out.”</p><p>I proposed a 6‑week sprint.</p><p>Build together.<br>Argue.<br>Stress‑test.<br>Define direction.</p><p>If we survive — we partner.</p><p>We didn’t just survive.</p><p>We built the MVP.<br>Aligned on vision.<br>Debated equity.<br>Defined vesting and cliff.<br>Even discussed what happens if one of us dies.</p><p>I drafted a 10‑page co‑founder agreement covering:</p><ul><li><p>Role accountability</p></li><li><p>Governance</p></li><li><p>Acceleration clauses</p></li><li><p>Buyback rights</p></li><li><p>Deadlock resolution</p></li><li><p>IP assignment</p></li><li><p>Confidentiality</p></li><li><p>Non‑compete</p></li><li><p>Departure scenarios</p></li></ul><p>We converted to a Delaware C‑Corp.</p><p>Then I presented Loopless AI at Founder Institute Demo Day in Lisbon.</p><p>Structure before scale; that changed everything.</p><h3>What We’re Building</h3><p>Loopless AI is not just another AI tool.</p><p>We’re building <strong>the AI Operating System for Real Estate</strong>.</p><p>Human‑coached autonomous AI agents that run the <strong>entire deal lifecycle</strong>.</p><p>Not scripted bots.<br>Not static automations.<br>But coordinated agents across voice and SMS that learn from human coaching.</p><p>Because in real estate:</p><p>When you get a great lead, you can’t afford to mess it up.<br>Execution is everything.</p><p>We signed a formal pilot with a major U.S. wholesaler.<br>We'll launch publicly in the coming months.<br>We’re part of Google Startup Program, NVIDIA Inception, and recipients of the ElevenLabs Startup Grant.</p><p>Now we’re onboarding early operators who want to scale execution without scaling headcount.</p><h3>What I Learned About Co‑Founders</h3><ol><li><p>Talent is common. Alignment is rare.</p></li><li><p>Skills matter. Character matters more.</p></li><li><p>Don’t partner on hope. Partner on proof.</p></li><li><p>Structure early prevents pain later.</p></li><li><p>The right co‑founder reduces anxiety. The wrong one multiplies it.</p></li></ol><p>The first time, I optimized for speed.<br>The second time, for alignment.</p><p>That difference may define the next decade of my life.</p><p>If you’re building something, take your time with this decision.</p><p>It’s not about who can code.<br>It’s about who can endure.</p><p>And if you’re in real estate and want to scale execution without scaling chaos:</p><p>https://looplessai.com/</p><p>We’re just getting started.</p><p><em>by Raza Haider - Founder &amp; CEO, Loopless AI</em></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Quiet Strength of Angels | Week 9</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/the-quiet-strength-of-angels-week-9</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/the-quiet-strength-of-angels-week-9</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 02 Mar 2026 11:24:43 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>There are moments in an ecosystem when you realise something bigger is taking shape, something that goes beyond investment, beyond deal flow, beyond the usual choreography of pitches and term sheets. Angels Way is one of those moments. A community of early‑stage angel investors focused on…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>There are moments in an ecosystem when you realise something bigger is taking shape, something that goes beyond investment, beyond deal flow, beyond the usual choreography of pitches and term sheets. Angels Way is one of those moments. A community of early‑stage angel investors focused on Portuguese startups, built on proximity, collaboration, and a very human alignment with founders. I’m proud to be part of it.</p><p>Even though I couldn’t be present at the recent gathering at Cloudflare’s office in Lisbon, where more than 150 investors met with the founders of the 10 companies Angels Way has already backed, I don’t want to miss the chance to underline the importance of what is being built here. From everything I’ve heard, it was a genuine moment of sharing: experiences, challenges, lessons learned, and visions of the future. But above all, it was a clear demonstration of the strength of a community that is aligned, committed, and active.</p><p>And this is where Angels Way truly stands apart. In a startup world that loves to say “people first” while sometimes behaving in ways that suggest the opposite, Angels Way actually means it. While pitch decks become theatre and founders are pushed into the role of performers, this community chooses a different path, one that feels almost radical in its simplicity. They invest in people, not as a slogan, but as a practice.</p><p>Their philosophy demands something rare: genuine proximity. Early‑stage investing, for Angels Way, is not a transaction; it is a relationship. And relationships require presence, trust, and the humility to walk beside founders rather than above them. Most investors claim to support founders; Angels Way insists on knowing them. Not in the superficial sense of a first meeting, but in the deeper, slower, more human sense, understanding motivations, fears, blind spots, and the values that will ultimately shape the companies they are building. They invest in alignment before they invest in equity.</p><p>This is not about picking winners; it’s about helping build them. Angels Way doesn’t chase hype cycles or fashionable verticals. They look for grounded, ambitious, self‑aware founders, people who understand that resilience is not a trait but a discipline. And in return, they offer something increasingly rare: a community that shows up, listens, and stays.</p><p>In a market obsessed with speed, Angels Way chooses intention. In a landscape driven by FOMO, they choose conviction. And in an industry that often forgets the human beings behind the KPIs, they place those human beings at the centre.</p><p>What is emerging here is more than an investment network. It is the consolidation of the most impactful early‑stage entrepreneurial community in Portugal; built on trust, proximity, and execution. As Luis Guttman wrote, and I fully agree: </p><p><em>The pride is collective. The impact is too.</em></p><p></p><p>💡 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/core">Portugal Spring 2026 Program</a> is accepting applications</p><p>💡 Save the date! <strong>StartupWeekend Women Loulé</strong> will take place next Mar 6, 7 &amp; 8. An inclusive event open to anyone who wants to support and empower women founders and innovators!</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://money-talks.pt/"><strong>Money Talks</strong></a> the biggest financial literacy event in the country, takes place on April 11 &amp; 12. Tickets are now on sale use<span style="color: #E00000;"> </span>promocode: ADAMASTOR</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“If you’re not embarrassed by the first version of your product, you’ve launched too late.” </p><p>Reid Hoffman</p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 <span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);">Fire chat with Portugal’s Top 5 hubs ranked in the Financial Times – Europe’s Leading Start-Up Hubs 2026 at <strong>Catolica Lisbon School of Business &amp; Economics</strong></span></p><p>🔷 <strong>Joao Moita</strong> has launched <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://iwanttobuildthis.com/">https://iwanttobuildthis.com/</a> A vetted community for product people building real things with AI — not just talking about it. Take a look if you have an idea and want to find someone to build it with. </p><p>🔷 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong>: Meet the Startup Ecosystem Porto Edition &amp; <strong>Viseu Tech</strong> Talks this Thursday</p><p>🔷 from march 2 to march 6, <strong>all women are invited to work at SITIO</strong> coworking spaces across Portugal, free for one week!</p><p>🔷 <strong>LX Circular </strong>is an acceleration program dedicated to supporting startups with innovative circular economy solutions. Apply until Mar 08</p><p>🔷 To celebrate International Women's Day on March 8th, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://shebuilds.lovable.app/">Lovable is completely free to use for the day</a>, powered by Anthropic</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏  <strong>Sónia Ferreira</strong> (BestHealth4U); <strong>Ella Frances Cullen</strong> (Minespider); Neide Vieira (IPLEXMED); <strong>Marta Oliveira</strong> (ATMOS Space Cargo) among the 18 women competing for the 𝗘𝘂𝗿𝗼𝗽𝗲𝗮𝗻 𝗣𝗿𝗶𝘇𝗲 𝗳𝗼𝗿 𝗪𝗼𝗺𝗲𝗻 𝗜𝗻𝗻𝗼𝘃𝗮𝘁𝗼𝗿𝘀 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟲</p><p>👏  <strong>BETA BEAT VC Fund</strong> I is officially <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://m36yg.r.ag.d.sendibm3.com/mk/mr/sh/1f8JAEjGcfF85p8NKrvbBUztzt/pVZstYraOPYD">launched</a></p><p>👏  <strong>Lispolis</strong> &amp; <strong>UPTEC</strong> among Top 15 start-up hubs with the best office and lab space score according to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.ft.com/content/ab05487c-72f9-4c1c-9acf-07768693b105">FT</a> </p><p>👏  <strong>Be the Not</strong> &amp; <strong>Rippla</strong> are the winners of the From Start-to-Table Program</p><p>👏  <strong>Usawa Care </strong>was the overall winner of the 10th edition of Cuatrecasas Acelera</p><p>👏  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://cargo.one">cargo.one</a> acquired <strong>Cargofive</strong></p><p>👏  <strong>healthhub</strong> by Unicorn Factory Lisboa Open Day this Wednesday</p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 Como as <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/pt-br/learning/ssl/lava-lamp-encryption/">lâmpadas de lava ajudam na criptografia</a> da internet? por Cloudflare</p><p>📚 SNS com <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sapo.pt/artigo/sns-com-inteligencia-artificial-pode-dar-mais-tempo-aos-medicos-6998834f4c6a066718d368fe">inteligência artificial pode dar mais tempo aos médicos</a> por Tiago Costa (Blodflow)</p><p>📚 How to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupportugal.com/legal-bites-02-how-to-set-up-a-company-in-portugal/">set up a company in Portugal</a> by Startup Portugal</p><p>📚 Is your <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupgenome.beehiiv.com/p/is-your-venture-capital-industry-quietly-leaving-billions-in-economic-value-on-the-table">venture capital industry quietly leaving billions in economic value on the table</a>?</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=5870623">How AI Destroys Institutions</a> by Woodrow Hartzog &amp; Jessica M. Silbey</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://community.inc/article/the-attention-game-is-over">The Attention Game is Over</a>: Trust is the only moat that matters now by Jon Levesque</p><p>📚 Healthspan science <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.mckinsey.com/mhi/our-insights/healthspan-science-may-enable-healthier-lives-for-all#/">may enable healthier lives for all</a></p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://communitycapital.eu/">European Community Capital 2025</a> Report</p><p>📚 FT ranking: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.ft.com/content/ab05487c-72f9-4c1c-9acf-07768693b105">Europe’s leading start-up hubs 2026</a></p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/3RETXDB3C8g35C9ESp3Mp3?si=1a323d2e14184f6b">E se corre bem?</a> com Márcia Pereira (Bandora)</p><p>🎧 DOJO AI: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/6LQGyO9dSeBzS1Lkkg3E6J?si=FXOi14zvRza0uUxypx0dOA&amp;nd=1&amp;dlsi=58a69c69d1834b10">Why 12% agency pricing is 'piracy'</a> with Tom Downer</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/65PqfIPMbXAZTcXMXrshDu?si=l_Dl0E7ZQR223zNiFFCk5A">Não podemos esperar pelo mercado nacional</a> com Pedro Ribeiro Santos, Armilar Venture Partners</p><p>🎥 Decoding AI <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/g35E23iW_Nk?si=V_hc2B0Bj76OjHhF">IA na Saúde</a>: Porque os Médicos Ainda Perdem Horas em Burocracia? com Medgical</p><p>🎥 Sheree Talks - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jKWX-6jADyI">O lado invisível do empreendedorismo</a>: jurídico, inovação e impacto com Bruno Gutman</p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FemTech as a Defining Economic and Social Frontier | Week 8</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/femtech-as-a-defining-economic-and-social-frontier-week-8</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/femtech-as-a-defining-economic-and-social-frontier-week-8</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Feb 2026 10:47:41 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>The presentation of The Vagina Business at Maze Impact HQ cut straight to the point: women’s health is not a side topic, it’s one of the biggest, most overlooked economic opportunities of this decade. And we’re still treating it like an afterthought. Marina’s voice cut through the noise with…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>The presentation of The Vagina Business at <strong>Maze Impact</strong> HQ cut straight to the point: women’s health is not a side topic, it’s one of the biggest, most overlooked economic opportunities of this decade. And we’re still treating it like an afterthought.</p><p>Marina’s voice cut through the noise with clarity and<em> </em>exposes the structural invisibility of women’s bodies in research, product development, and investment. Marina lays out the case clearly:</p><ul><li><p>Women’s health has been systematically deprioritised, leading to chronic underinvestment</p></li><li><p>Around 80% of<strong> FemTech</strong> founders are women, building from lived experience rather than theoretical market gaps</p></li><li><p>Closing women’s health gaps could unlock up to 1 trillion in annual economic impact</p></li><li><p>Every $ invested in women’s health yields $x3 in economic benefits through reduced healthcare costs and higher productivity</p></li></ul><p>The book blends data, storytelling, and a call to action that resonated strongly with the room; a room mostly full of women, but with a few men too, myself included.</p><p>The event created a space where the audience with different backgrounds spoke openly about both the opportunities and the taboos that still shape <strong>FemTech</strong>, some of them pretty much aligned with my vision:</p><ul><li><p><strong>FemTech</strong> is becoming mainstream because the fundamentals are undeniable: massive unmet needs, strong consumer demand, and clear ROI.</p></li><li><p>Taboos still slow innovation, from menstrual health to menopause to sexual wellbeing.</p></li><li><p>Impact and profitability align, FemTech sits at the intersection of social need and economic potential.</p></li><li><p>Representation matters; diverse teams build better products, especially in health.</p></li></ul><p>The discussion made it clear that Innovation Ecosystems must evolve to include the realities of half the population.</p><p>What I take from the room, regarding our Ecosystem:</p><ul><li><p>Women’s health is a growth engine, and there is an urgency of investing in it as a strategic economic lever</p></li><li><p>The demand is real, the technology is ready, and capital is the bottleneck.</p></li><li><p>Talking openly about these topics still makes some people uncomfortable, which is exactly why it matters.</p></li><li><p>The opportunity for Portugal and Europe to lead in <strong>FemTech</strong> innovation.</p></li><li><p>The importance of dismantling taboos that still shape product development and funding decisions.</p></li><li><p>The power of community gatherings to accelerate cultural and market change.</p></li></ul><p>I cannot end without highlighting <strong>Maze Impact</strong>’s role as a convener of conversations that push the boundaries of impact entrepreneurship.</p><p><em>Innovation starts when silence ends. Yesterday at Maze, the silence broke, loudly.</em></p><p></p><p>📍<strong>Região Centro</strong> need your help:</p><ul><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events">Tempestade.SOS</a></p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="mailto:geral@startupleiria.com">geral@startupleiria.com</a></p></li><li><p>Gabinete Reerguer Leiria no Mercado Sant'Ana</p></li><li><p>Cáritas Leiria </p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://www.inpulsar.pt">www.inpulsar.pt</a>   </p></li></ul><p>💡 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/core">Portugal Spring 2026 Program</a> is accepting applications</p><p>💡 Save the date! <strong>StartupWeekend Women Loulé</strong> will take place next Mar 6, 7 &amp; 8. An inclusive event open to anyone who wants to support and empower women founders and innovators!</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://money-talks.pt/"><strong>Money Talks</strong></a> the biggest financial literacy event in the country, takes place on April 11 &amp; 12. Tickets are now on sale use<span style="color: #E00000;"> </span>promocode: ADAMASTOR</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>"Ambition isn't a flaw. It's a driving force"</p><p><strong>Cristina Fonseca</strong></p></blockquote><h2><strong>H</strong>ighlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 Closing Ceremony | <strong>From Start-to-Table</strong> this Tuesday</p><p>🔷 <strong>VDS Valencia</strong> Call for Speakers is <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://vds.tech/call-for-speakers-registration/">now open</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>Canopy Global Demo Night</strong> &amp; <strong>Above and Beyond</strong>: GAMING this Wednesday</p><p>🔷 <strong>Startup Grind</strong> &amp; FoodTec, The Future of Food by <strong>RedBridge</strong> this Thursday</p><p>🔷 <strong>SelectUSA Portugal Series</strong> - De Portugal para os Estados Unidos: Da Oportunidade à Expansão next Monday</p><p>🔷 𝗖𝗮𝗹𝗹 𝗳𝗼𝗿 𝗣𝗮𝗽𝗲𝗿𝘀 | 𝗘𝗖𝗜𝗘 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟲 for the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.academic-conferences.org/conferences/ecie/">𝗠𝗶𝗻𝗶 𝗧𝗿𝗮𝗰𝗸 𝗼𝗻 𝗔𝗰𝗮𝗱𝗲𝗺𝗶𝗰 𝗘𝗻𝘁𝗿𝗲𝗽𝗿𝗲𝗻𝗲𝘂𝗿𝘀𝗵𝗶𝗽 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗘𝗻𝘁𝗿𝗲𝗽𝗿𝗲𝗻𝗲𝘂𝗿𝗶𝗮𝗹 𝗘𝗰𝗼𝘀𝘆𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗺 𝗗𝘆𝗻𝗮𝗺𝗶𝗰𝘀</a> until Wednesday </p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏 <strong>Engineers Hub</strong> a new space dedicated to innovation, technology, and collaboration in Lisbon; Co-created by Unicorn Factory Lisboa and the Ordem dos Engenheiros – Região Sul</p><p>👏 <strong>Rows </strong>will be joining Superhuman</p><p>👏 <strong>SmartRoads</strong> won the Urban Mobility Startup Creation Program, an initiative led by BGI - Sustainable Ventures</p><p>👏 Portuguese hubs mentioned on the Financial Times - Europe’s leading startup hubs 2026: <strong>Unicorn Factory; Lispolis; Fintech House; Startup Braga; Build Up Labs; Startup Leiria; Ericeira Business Factory; Canopy; Casa do Impacto; UPTEC; Startup Madeira; </strong>and<strong> BGI Sustainable Ventures</strong></p><p>👏 <strong>Portugal </strong>ranks #1 globally for Global Mobility &amp; Openness category of the StartupBlink Innovators Business Environment Index (IBEI) 2026</p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚Investors Portugal: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yR9oLkvn1Pb3GYbYNm91W-C8h-QgDOmn/view">Parecer para a COFAP</a> – Comissão de Orçamento, Finanças e Administração Pública</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.publico.pt/2026/02/06/p3/cronica/empatia-nao-inteligencia-emocional-superpoder-2163844">Empatia não é inteligência emocional</a>, mas pode ser o teu superpoder por Filipa Lemos <span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);">Cristina</span></p><p>📚“<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://pmemagazine.sapo.pt/a-inovacao-nao-deve-estar-reservada-aos-grandes-centros-ou-as-grandes-empresas-simplifyer/">A inovação não deve estar reservada aos grandes centros</a> ou às grandes empresas” por Isabel Carapeta (Simplifyer) </p><p>📚How <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/how-body-language-impacts-founders-pitch-kristen-craft-hlwvc/">Body Language Can Impact a Founder's Pitch</a> by Kristen Craft</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://metaduck.com/decipad-lessons-learned/">10 Lessons Learned</a> from Closing Our Startup After 5 Years by Pedro Teixeira</p><p>📚Man accidentally <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.popsci.com/technology/robot-vacuum-army/">gains control of 7,000 robot vacuums</a></p><p>📚Anthropic Education Report: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/AI-fluency-index">The AI Fluency Index</a></p><p>🎧 The Fun They Had - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://podcasts.apple.com/tn/podcast/the-fun-they-had-asimov-predicted-ai-tutors-in-1950s/id1771688480?i=1000750099015">Asimov Predicted AI Tutors in 1950's</a> on Modem Futura</p><p>🎧 Marina Gerner: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://diaryofaclo.podbean.com/e/marinagerner/">FemTech and ‘The Vagina Business’</a> on Diary of Clo</p><p>🎥 Gui Gomes and Joao Alves from <strong>Bleap</strong>: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/IDFhNpygKVw?si=3-Opdk7WTAdFlwAj">Raising $6m to build a fintech completely on the blockchain</a></p><p>🎥 Inovadores: <strong>Bloodflow</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/V-8l_rz4YxA?si=g9iDIipVWO6FQlW9">garante precisão nos relatórios de análises</a></p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Carnaval as a metaphor for entrepreneurship | Week 7</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/carnaval-as-a-metaphor-for-entrepreneurship-week-7</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/carnaval-as-a-metaphor-for-entrepreneurship-week-7</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Feb 2026 12:13:33 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>Carnaval may be Brazil’s global trademark, but we’ve always had our own version. It’s usually a moment to blend in with the locals, feel the culture from the inside, and let yourself be carried by the rhythm. But this year is different. The severe storms that hit the country left scars; physical,…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Carnaval may be Brazil’s global trademark, but we’ve always had our own version. It’s usually a moment to blend in with the locals, feel the culture from the inside, and let yourself be carried by the rhythm. </p><p>But this year is different.</p><p>The severe storms that hit the country left scars; physical, emotional, and economic. Communities that normally spend months preparing for celebration suddenly found themselves rebuilding homes, supporting neighbors, and rethinking what Carnaval even means in a moment like this. And yet, in true Portuguese fashion, people still show up for each other. They adapt. They create. They keep going.</p><p>That resilience is exactly why Carnaval remains such a powerful metaphor for entrepreneurship.</p><p>Every year, even in the best of times, Carnaval is built under pressure. Samba groups and local associations reinvent themselves with tight budgets, shifting plans, and unpredictable challenges. This year, the constraints were heavier, but the spirit didn’t break. That’s the startup mindset in its purest form: innovation born from adversity, creativity sharpened by necessity, and the belief that something meaningful can still emerge from chaos.</p><p>Carnaval is also a collective act. No one shines alone. Designers, musicians, dancers, volunteers, everyone contributes to a shared vision. The same is true for founders. No startup scales without a community: mentors, partners, early adopters, and the team that shows up even when the confetti is replaced by mud and debris. Community isn’t decoration; it’s infrastructure.</p><p>And even in a year like this, boldness still matters. Carnaval rewards those who dare, those who take risks, push boundaries, and bring something unexpected to the avenue. The best entrepreneurial ideas come from that same courage. Playing it safe rarely leads to breakthroughs, in business or in celebration.</p><p>At its core, Carnaval, especially this year, reminds us of passion, resilience, and creativity. These are the values that define entrepreneurship at its best. Whether you’re building a company or helping your neighborhood rebuild, success comes from embracing challenges, trusting your people, and having the courage to stand out.</p><p>Because in both business and in moments of celebration or recovery, the ones who make an impact are the ones who dare to shine, even when the skies have just cleared.</p><p>📍<strong>Região Centro</strong> need your help:</p><ul><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events">Tempestade.SOS</a></p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="mailto:geral@startupleiria.com">geral@startupleiria.com</a></p></li><li><p>Gabinete Reerguer Leiria no Mercado Sant'Ana</p></li><li><p>Cáritas Leiria </p></li><li><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://www.inpulsar.pt">www.inpulsar.pt</a>   </p></li></ul><p>💡 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/core">Portugal Spring 2026 Program</a> is accepting applications</p><p>💡 Save the date! <strong>StartupWeekend Women Loulé</strong> will take place next Mar 6, 7 &amp; 8. An inclusive event open to anyone who wants to support and empower women founders and innovators!</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://money-talks.pt/"><strong>Money Talks</strong></a> the biggest financial literacy event in the country, takes place on April 11 &amp; 12. Tickets are now on sale use<span style="color: #E00000;"> </span>promocode: ADAMASTOR</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf9cBXjPyZF-inWyCP7yP1KhgZWD3I0RJiYOiQdZOzlN8a3Jw/viewform">Pitch Competition</a> – <strong>WOMAN SUMMIT 2026 </strong>is looking for startups founded or co‑founded by women</p><p>📝Tired of feeling disconnected from your country’s governance Lucas Gros created a web app to follow <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://parla-app.eu/">what’s happening in Parliament</a>. Take a look and give feedback</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><strong>“A business has to be involving, it has to be fun, and it has to exercise your creative instincts”</strong> </p><p><em>Richard Branson</em></p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 FemTech 101: An Intro to the <strong>Portuguese Ecosystem Powering Women’s Health Innovation</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events">this Wednesday</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>Coworking Thursdays </strong>this week at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.coworkingthursdays.pt/event-details/viseu-synvert-portugal">Synvert Portugal</a> (Viseu) </p><p>🔷 If you’re building 𝐀𝐈 𝐬𝐨𝐥𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐬 𝐟𝐨𝐫 𝐓𝐫𝐚𝐯𝐞𝐥 &amp; 𝐇𝐨𝐬𝐩𝐢𝐭𝐚𝐥𝐢𝐭𝐲, this is your final opportunity to join a 𝟏𝟐-𝐰𝐞𝐞𝐤 𝐨𝐩𝐞𝐧 𝐢𝐧𝐧𝐨𝐯𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 Check In Tourism 𝐩𝐫𝐨𝐠𝐫𝐚𝐦 connecting startups with leading tourism partners in Portugal. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.checkinopen.pt/">Applications close</a> on Feb 23 </p><p>🔷  <strong>From Start-to-Table </strong>| Closing Ceremony, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events">next Tuesday</a></p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏  <strong>Trash4Goods</strong> won the SIBS Prize</p><p>👏  10 of the most promising Portuguese startups  by EU-Startups: <strong>ADECI Group</strong>, <strong>BM2Solar</strong>, <strong>BloodFlow</strong>, <strong>Bloop</strong>, <strong>Chainreactor</strong>, <strong>DOJO AI</strong>, 👾<strong>Jsonify</strong>, <strong>Litehaus</strong>, <strong>Manie</strong>, and <strong>Next Border</strong></p><p>👏  <strong>Delox</strong> (spin-off from CIÊNCIAS ULisboa) raised 1.6M</p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚Startup Weekend Women chega com <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://thenextbigidea.pt/startup-weekend-women-chega-com-54-horas-para-transformar-ideias-em-startups/">54 horas para transformar ideias em startups</a></p><p>📚How <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://technode.com/2026/02/11/tech-odyssey-series-how-portugal-turns-itself-into-a-startup-accelerator-and-redefines-innovation/">Portugal Turns Itself Into a Startup Accelerator and Redefines Innovation</a></p><p>📚The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/02/15/the-great-computer-science-exodus-and-where-students-are-going-instead/">great computer science exodus</a> (and where students are going) by Connie Loizos</p><p>📚The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://time.com/collections/the-age-of-longevity/7338546/ovaries-unlock-secrets-longevity/">race for measuring age</a> and why it matters by Dominique Mosbergen</p><p>📚Solutions for <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://isulibrary.isunet.edu/doc_num.php?explnum_id=1917">construction of a lunar base</a></p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.jornaldenegocios.pt/podcast/conversas-com-ceo/detalhe/nuno-comando-e-o-convidado-de-conversas-com-ceo">Nuno Comando, director da Casa do Impacto</a>, é o convidado de Conversas com CEO</p><p>🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/gV9qUGOYk1Q?si=p2ft6d0PDim3ShBl">Is AI making us dumb</a>? Breaking down the MIT study</p><p>🎥 “<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C0Z8SRy73Mk">Desmistificando o Investimento Anjo</a>” com Andrea Piazza e Cintia Mano </p><p>🎥 Pedro Ribeiro Santos, Armilar: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eu.vc/p/pedro-ribeiro-santos-armilar-25-years">25 Years of Iberian Tech &amp; The Next Chapter </a></p><p>🎥 Clawdbot <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/tEjg56ZYKJo?si=zGoyOxMCsO78Ildh">Explained in 6 minutes</a> (Beginner's Guide)</p><p>🎥 Decoding AI IA na Saúde: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/g35E23iW_Nk?si=06Bii1AQUmeAyYI3">Porque os Médicos Ainda Perdem Horas em Burocracia</a>? com Medgical</p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>A Hard Week, a Stronger Ecosystem | Week 6</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/a-hard-week-a-stronger-ecosystem-week-6</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/a-hard-week-a-stronger-ecosystem-week-6</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 09 Feb 2026 10:47:36 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>The past week has truly put Portugal to the test. The country faced one of the most severe weather events in recent years, with isolated communities, damaged infrastructure, and thousands of people dealing with material and emotional losses. Moments like these remind us how fragile daily life can…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>The past week has truly put Portugal to the test. The country faced one of the most severe weather events in recent years, with isolated communities, damaged infrastructure, and thousands of people dealing with material and emotional losses. Moments like these remind us how fragile daily life can be, but also how strong our networks become when everything else seems to fail.</p><p>Among those networks, the <strong>Tempestade SOS</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tempestadesos.com/">platform</a> stood out immediately. It quickly became a reference point for requests for help, offers of support, and community coordination. In an emergency scenario, the ability to organise information, connect people, and speed up responses makes all the difference. And this initiative showed once again how technology can serve as a tool for collective resilience.</p><p>This episode also reminds us of something the Portuguese entrepreneurial ecosystem has already proven in other crises: when the country needs it, the tech community steps forward. During the pandemic, the <strong>Tech4Covid19</strong> movement mobilised hundreds of volunteers, startups, and specialists to create solutions in record time; from telemedicine platforms to logistical support systems. It was a clear example of how talent, creativity, and a sense of mission can turn moments of vulnerability into concrete progress.</p><p>Today, facing the devastation caused by the extreme weather, the challenge is different, but the principle remains the same. The entrepreneurial ecosystem can and should play an active role in the recovery of the affected areas. Whether through mapping tools, communication solutions, volunteer platforms, reconstruction technologies, or simply by offering skills and time, there is room for everyone to contribute.</p><p>Rebuilding is not only physical; it is also social, emotional, and deeply community driven. And this is where Portuguese innovation can once again show its value: bringing people closer, accelerating responses, and creating bridges where before there were barriers.</p><p>This week was tough. But it was also a powerful reminder that when the country faces storms — not only the meteorological ones — there is an ecosystem ready to act, to support, and to rebuild. And that is something we can be proud of.</p><p>💡 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/core">Portugal Spring 2026 Program</a> is accepting applications</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://money-talks.pt/"><strong>Money Talks</strong></a> the biggest financial literacy event in the country, takes place on April 11 &amp; 12. Tickets are now on sale use<span style="color: #E00000;"> </span>promocode: ADAMASTOR</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf9cBXjPyZF-inWyCP7yP1KhgZWD3I0RJiYOiQdZOzlN8a3Jw/viewform">Pitch Competition</a> – <strong>WOMAN SUMMIT 2026 </strong>is looking for startups founded or co‑founded by women</p><p>📝 <strong>João Afonso</strong> developed a new platform to help entrepreneurs find cofounders with complementary skills by combining online matching tools with in-person pitch and networking events. Join <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://matchingfounders.cc/startup-ideas">Matching Founders</a> if you haven't, yet and/or help spread the word  </p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p><strong>“We make a living by what we get, but we make a life by what we give.“ </strong></p><p>Winston Churchill</p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/vk6sdysg">Startup HR Pitch &amp; Round Table</a> | <strong>APG + 351</strong> - Feb 11: People Management, Change, and Innovation is an after‑work session celebrating the chaotic and brilliant side of leading people in Startups vs. Corporate. With Nuno Duarte, APG, and 351 Startups guiding an evening of rapid‑fire pitches and open conversation about the future of work</p><p>🔷  <strong>Co-working Day for Designers </strong>by LisboaUX <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/gkghnhxh">this Friday</a> at Casa do Impacto</p><p>🔷  Final reminder to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.competition.southsummit.io/calls/south_summit_2026">apply until Feb 14</a> to the <strong>South Summit Madrid 2026 Startup Competition</strong>, one of Europe’s leading global startup &amp; investment events</p><p>🔷  Cohort 19 of <strong>Hub71 programs, Unicorn Factory Lisboa's</strong> international partner in the UAE. Startups <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.hub71.com/program/access-programme">can apply until Feb 15</a> for the Access program or Hub71+ Life Sciences, both aimed at scalable tech startups between Seed and Series A</p><p>🔷 <strong>Community Council</strong> is a 4 day retreat in a Normandy chateau for founders and execs building community-led businesses. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.communitycouncil.co/">Apply until Feb 15</a>  (The croissants await!)</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏  Portugal has been ranked 1st worldwide in the Global Mobility &amp; Openness category of the <strong>StartupBlink Innovators Business Environment Index (IBEI) 2026</strong></p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://eco.sapo.pt/opiniao/espaco-aos-empreendedores/">Espaço aos empreendedores</a> por Rodolfo Condessa</p><p>📚 The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://jaimefjorge.com/posts/the-death-of-code-wont-matter">Death of Code Won’t Matter</a> by Jaime Jorge</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/navigating-eu-grants-takeaways-from-2025-what-expect-2026-granterai-isbke/">Navigating EU Grants</a>: takeaways from 2025 and what to expect in 2026 by Granter</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.weforum.org/publications/advancing-responsible-ai-innovation-a-playbook/">Advancing Responsible AI Innovation</a>: A Playbook by World Economic Forum</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://goncalopedrogil.com/two-lives-one-thread/">Two Lives, One Thread</a> by Goncalo Gil</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/00EUwqhjQypPldc9Fs8orp?si=qzvTfxcZSvSlmrpduQxbdw">App EIGHT</a> no Empreendedores</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/6My9Bxs5iQpn5aDpfbVUUp?si=z0XFJGdtRROi9k-uJjsfGA">Winning by Design</a> w/ GTM legend Jacco Van der Kooij</p><p>🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/lL6GdUHIBsM">Adora Cheung on How to Set KPIs and Goals</a>: YC Partner Adora Cheung covers the importance of defining and tracking KPIs to understand how effectively your startup is reaching your goals</p><p>🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/UdDsje6NRKk?si=yB4uBrbRZobZH4Oa">Bootstrap</a>: A Revolução Silenciosa do Empreendedorismo em Portugal! c/ Afonso Gonçalves e Tiago Ferreira</p><p>🎥 Lessons from <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/nyRIA3glbSY?si=6UF-sWfxZu2NkBnu">8-Figure Amazon Brand Exits and The Decisions That Matter Most</a> by Fireside Lisbon</p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Build Together | Week 5</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/build-together-week-5</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/build-together-week-5</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 02 Feb 2026 11:36:07 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>The Founder Institute Portugal ’s first cohort wrapped last week, and once again it proved something we often forget: ecosystems don’t grow by accident. They grow because people invest time, energy, and belief into helping new founders take their first real steps. FI is one of the few programs that…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>The <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong>’s first cohort wrapped last week, and once again it proved something we often forget: ecosystems don’t grow by accident. They grow because people invest time, energy, and belief into helping new founders take their first real steps.</p><p>FI is one of the few programs that consistently turns raw ambition into structured progress. It demands clarity, discipline, and accountability, three things every founder thinks they have until they’re truly tested. And that’s exactly why programs like this matter. They shorten the learning curve, reduce avoidable mistakes, and give founders a support network that doesn’t vanish after Demo Day.</p><p>If we want a stronger Portuguese startup ecosystem, we need more of this: more programs that challenge, more mentors who show up, more founders who dare to start. Cohorts like this one are proof that the pipeline is alive, diverse, and full of potential.</p><p>My colleagues Elisa, Fernando, and I took on this mission with a simple belief: that Portugal needs more places where early‑stage founders can grow with structure, ambition, and community. Over 50 mentors joined us, a powerful reminder of the generosity, quality, and openness that define our startup community. Their willingness to give back is one of our ecosystem’s greatest strengths.</p><p>Every time a cohort ends, the ecosystem gets a little stronger. Not because of the curriculum alone, but because of the people who choose to build together.</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/vk6sdysg">Startup HR Pitch &amp; Round Table</a> | <strong>APG + 351</strong> - Feb 11: People Management, Change, and Innovation is an after‑work session celebrating the chaotic and brilliant side of leading people in Startups vs. Corporate. With Nuno Duarte, APG, and 351 Startups guiding an evening of rapid‑fire pitches and open conversation about the future of work</p><p>💡 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fi.co/core">Portugal Spring 2026 Program</a> is accepting applications</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://money-talks.pt/"><strong>Money Talks</strong></a> the biggest financial literacy event in the country, takes place on April 11 &amp; 12. Tickets are now on sale</p><p>💡 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf9cBXjPyZF-inWyCP7yP1KhgZWD3I0RJiYOiQdZOzlN8a3Jw/viewform">Pitch Competition</a> – <strong>WOMAN SUMMIT 2026 </strong>is looking for startups founded or co‑founded by women</p><p>📝 JEEFEUC (Junior Enterprise from Coimbra University) are diving deep into market validation for <strong>Silveiratech - Re_generation Village </strong>(a regeneration-focused project based in Lousã)! They've launched a survey to validate Silveira Tech's model and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfDBLVgew5-w_BF02OMXiGfsscGUz_JV0eeV8BW4DmsjmcTBQ/viewform">wait your input</a>!</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“Great things in business are never done by one person. They’re done by a team of people.”</p><p>Steve Jobs</p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 <strong>João Afonso</strong> (Uptec) has launched a new platform to help entrepreneurs find co-founders with complementary skills by combining online matching tools with in-person pitch and networking events. Join <strong>Matching Founders</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://matchingfounders.cc/">if you haven't, yet and/or help spread the word</a>  </p><p>🔷  <strong>LisboaUX</strong> job board includes job positions for designers who live outside of Lisbon. For now, Porto and Braga. You can check some of the job opportunities <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://jobs.lisboaux.com/">here</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>Porto Tech Hub</strong> has a new face, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://portotechhub.com/">take a look</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>Community Council</strong> is a 4 day retreat in a Normandy chateau for founders and execs building community-led businesses. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.communitycouncil.co/">Apply until Feb 15</a>  (The croissants await!)</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Dealroom.co"><strong>Dealroom.co</strong></a> raises 7M</p><p>👏  <strong>Sword Health </strong>aquires <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/kaiahealth/"><span><strong>Kaia Health</strong></span></a></p><p>👏  <span><strong>Bleap</strong> raises 5M</span></p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.algarveevolution.pt/pt/blog/algarve-evolution-community-6/inovacao-no-velho-continente-11"> Inovação no ‘Velho Continente’</a> por Joaquim Nascimento</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.algarveevolution.pt/pt/blog/algarve-evolution-community-6/inovacao-no-velho-continente-11"> </a>Uma Semana na Vida de um <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://caixacentral.mcdigital.tech/uma-semana-na-vida-de-um-innovation-specialist-na-mc-digital-7f41538fa6b4">Innovation Specialist</a> por João Fernandes</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.algarveevolution.pt/pt/blog/algarve-evolution-community-6/inovacao-no-velho-continente-11"> </a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://hardwarejourney.substack.com/p/prototype-success-is-the-trap">“Prototype success</a>” is the trap by Francisco Tenente</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.algarveevolution.pt/pt/blog/algarve-evolution-community-6/inovacao-no-velho-continente-11"> </a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://medium.com/impact-shakers/new-impact-funds-in-europe-in-2025-22999066fe8b">New Impact Funds in Europe in 2025</a> by Yonca Braeckman</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.algarveevolution.pt/pt/blog/algarve-evolution-community-6/inovacao-no-velho-continente-11"> </a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/why-most-startups-fail-before-ever-get-chanceand-what-fernandes-nd3ge">Why Most Startups Fail Before They Ever Get a Chance</a>—and What MIT Gets Right About Entrepreneurship by Michelle Fernandes</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.algarveevolution.pt/pt/blog/algarve-evolution-community-6/inovacao-no-velho-continente-11"> </a>The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/first-designer-longer-early-theyre-foundational-rui-barroca-2flse/">First Designer Is No Longer “Early” They’re Foundational</a> by Rui Barroca</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.algarveevolution.pt/pt/blog/algarve-evolution-community-6/inovacao-no-velho-continente-11"> </a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://web.stanford.edu/~chadj/AIandEconomicFuture.pdf">A.I. and Our Economic Future</a> by Charles I. Jones</p><p>🎧 Founders by David Senra: Excellent <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/5ilZL35OkcOBadelSce6KS?si=f33c440d86fb4374">advice for living</a> w/ Kevin Kelly</p><p>🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/Xh6l39k3ngE?si=q2PXQ_h7V1En3GI5">Inside the Mind of Jamie Dimon</a>, JP Morgan CEO: Lessons from a Top CEO</p><p>🎥 Founder Tales: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJlgkxKAhQk">De Founder a VC</a> com Carolina Amorim (Bloq.it)</p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>🚀 Startup Voucher: Proof It Works, and One Week Left</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/startup-voucher-proof-it-works-and-one-week-left</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/startup-voucher-proof-it-works-and-one-week-left</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 27 Jan 2026 19:35:10 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Fernando Fraga</dc:creator>
      <description>There&apos;s a recurring complaint in Portugal&apos;s startup ecosystem: too much support for companies that already exist, not enough for people still figuring things out. Accelerators want traction. Investors want revenue. Incubators want a team and a prototype. But what about the person with a solid idea…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>There's a recurring complaint in Portugal's startup ecosystem: too much support for companies that already exist, not enough for people still figuring things out. Accelerators want traction. Investors want revenue. Incubators want a team and a prototype.</p><p><strong>But what about the person with a solid idea and no safety net to test it?</strong></p><h3><strong>The Early-Stage Gap</strong></h3><p>This gap matters more than we often admit. Globally, around <strong>90% of startups fail</strong>, with lack of product demand responsible for 34% of those failures (CB Insights). Most don't even get to test the idea properly.</p><p>In Europe, the funding gap at the earliest stages is well documented. The <em>State of European Tech</em> report shows that while European startups start as strong as their US counterparts, they're far less likely to keep scaling.</p><p><strong>Portugal has made real progress:</strong></p><ul><li><p>The <strong>2025 Startup &amp; Entrepreneurial Ecosystem Report</strong> shows 5,091 active startups (+8% from 2024).</p></li><li><p>The sector accounts for around <strong>28,000 jobs</strong> and <strong>€2.856 billion</strong> in turnover.</p></li><li><p>Average salaries in startups are 81% higher than the national average.</p></li></ul><p>The <strong>Startup Voucher</strong> exists precisely to address the people still figuring things out. And after being part of the first cohort's evaluation process, I can say it works.</p><p></p><hr><h3><strong>What I Saw From the Inside</strong></h3><p>I was part of the jury for the selection of projects and for the interim evaluation in Fátima, where we heard 45-second pitches from all the projects. It was spectacular:</p><ul><li><p>Around <strong>60 beneficiaries</strong> across roughly 48 projects.</p></li><li><p>People who, a few months earlier, had only an idea were now articulating value propositions and identifying target markets.</p></li><li><p>The program includes a <strong>Bootcamp</strong>, thematic sessions, and technical deep-dives into ESG and Sustainable Development Goals.</p></li></ul><p>The initiative also got airtime on <u>CNN Portugal's Innovation segment</u> — worth watching to see how mainstream media is framing startup support.</p><p></p><hr><p></p><h3><strong>A Wish for 2026: More Bets on People, Not Just Products</strong></h3><p>If there's one thing the ecosystem should carry into 2026, it's this: we need more programs willing to bet on people before they have anything to show.</p><p>The Startup Voucher doesn't ask for a prototype or a team of five; it asks for an <strong>idea, a commitment, and willingness to be held accountable.</strong> Portugal has the infrastructure; now it needs to give people permission to try.</p><p></p><hr><p></p><h3><strong>Why This Should Matter to You</strong></h3><p>If you're <strong>under 30</strong>, hold a degree, aren't currently employed or studying, and have a tech-based idea, the Startup Voucher meets you where you are.</p><p><strong>Key Details:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Location:</strong> You need to have fiscal residence in the <strong>North, Center, or Alentejo</strong> regions. (Lisbon, Algarve, and the islands are not covered).</p></li><li><p><strong>Financial Component:</strong> * <strong>€900/month</strong> for up to 9 months per beneficiary.</p><ul><li><p>Two milestone bonuses of <strong>€1,500</strong> each.</p></li><li><p>An additional <strong>€2,000 bonus</strong> if you create your own job.</p></li><li><p><em>Total:</em> Up to <strong>€13,100 per person</strong>.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Beyond the Money:</strong> Mentorship through the National Mentors Network and incubation at accredited facilities.</p></li></ul><p></p><hr><p></p><h3><strong>⏳ One Week Left</strong></h3><p>Applications for the second call (Aviso 2025-02) close on <strong>Friday, January 30th, 2026, at 18:00.</strong></p><p>👉 <strong>Submit your application here:</strong> <u>IAPMEI Platform - Startup Voucher</u></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Europe is Moving | Week 4</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/europe-is-moving-week-4</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/europe-is-moving-week-4</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 26 Jan 2026 11:30:01 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>This week brought two strong signals that Europe is finally accelerating in the right direction for those who build, invest, and scale technology on this continent. First, the President of the European Commission announced progress on EU‑Inc , the long awaited pan-European corporate structure…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>This week brought two strong signals that Europe is finally accelerating in the right direction for those who build, invest, and scale technology on this continent.</p><p>First, the President of the European Commission announced progress on <strong>EU‑Inc</strong>, the long awaited pan-European corporate structure designed to simplify life for anyone operating across borders. A Europe where a company is born European from day one, without navigating 27 bureaucratic realities is a Europe that becomes more competitive, more coherent, and more aligned with the global stage where our founders already operate. </p><p>Second, we witnessed the launch of the <strong>Digital Enterprise Wallet</strong>, a decisive step toward reducing administrative friction, strengthening information security, and improving how companies interact with the State. And it’s worth highlighting: <strong>Portugal was a pioneer</strong>. Before it became a European trend, we had already shown that it’s possible to digitalize, simplify, and deliver real value to businesses. At a time when competitiveness, productivity, and scale are at the center of every debate, these two initiatives point toward a future where creating and operating a company in Europe stops being an act of endurance and becomes an act of ambition.</p><p>And third, the announcement of the <strong>European Scale‑Up Fund</strong> marks a long overdue shift in how Europe supports high‑growth companies. For years, founders and investors have argued that Europe doesn’t lack talent or ambition; it lacks scale‑stage capital at European scale. This fund is a concrete step toward closing that gap and giving our most promising companies the financial firepower they need to compete globally.</p><p>At a time when competitiveness, productivity, and scale are at the center of every debate, these initiatives point toward a future where creating and operating a company in Europe stops being an act of endurance and becomes an act of ambition.</p><p>If Europe wants to remain relevant in the next decade, this is the path: fewer barriers, more trust, more interoperability, and more vision.</p><p>And we, as an ecosystem, must keep doing what we’ve always done best: <strong>push, challenge, and build</strong>.</p><p>💡 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal - Meet the Portugal Startup Ecosystem</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.meetup.com/lisbon-startup-founder-101/events/312911334/">Demo Day</a> on Jan 29 with Bloqit and Granter on stage for a talk about our ecosystem</p><p>💡 Calling all MSc, Ph.D., and Postdoc students in STEM areas or fields of study! Are you ready to turn your innovative ideas into the next big thing? Join <strong>Faber</strong>'s exclusive <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ep.faber.vc/">Entrepreneurship Program</a> (deadline Mar 01) and learn from the real-life experiences of successful entrepreneurs who have turned their dreams into thriving businesses</p><p>📝 JEEFEUC (Junior Enterprise from Coimbra University) are diving deep into market validation for <strong>Silveiratech - Re_generation Village </strong>(a regeneration-focused project based in Lousã)! They've launched a survey to validate Silveira Tech's model and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfDBLVgew5-w_BF02OMXiGfsscGUz_JV0eeV8BW4DmsjmcTBQ/viewform">wait your input</a>!</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“Simplicity is the ultimate sophistication”  </p><p>Leonardo da Vinci</p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 <strong>EDP’s Energy Starter</strong> open innovation program is <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://theenergystarter.com/">accepting applications</a></p><p>🔷 all <strong>Catolica students</strong>! Don’t miss the Startup Safari on January 30th, Co-organized between the Career and Talent department and CLEC. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://catolica-lisbon-csm.symplicity.com/students/?s=event&amp;ss=is&amp;mode=form&amp;id=9bf34e13cf6510c511294044e1caf981&amp;signin_tab=0">Apply here</a></p><p>🔷 How can I speak at <strong>Productized Conference</strong>? Have a story to tell? A project that inspires? A perspective the world needs to hear?  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScI4Dcrk20Li6wyIjWG90a0fHKHhHcB1CI5GO2_moiKt-Hm8g/viewform">Applications to speak are now open</a></p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏  <strong>RAID</strong> ranked #2 at the EUDIS Hackathon 2025 Autumn Edition (EUDefence and #EUSpace innovators)</p><p>👏  <strong>Enhaced Fertilty</strong>; <strong>Granter</strong>; <strong>Uwasa</strong>; <strong>Vericasa</strong>; and <strong>Virtualeap </strong>have been selected by Startup Portugal and Plug and Play for the Scale Up program, supported by the U.S. Commercial Service </p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 Ursula von der Leyen <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ec.europa.eu/commission/presscorner/detail/en/speech_26_150">just announced EU-Inc at Davos</a> </p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/open-innovation-altice-labs-road-ahead-jo%C3%A3o-ramos-rm1he/">Open Innovation at Altice Labs</a> – The Road Ahead by João Ramos</p><p>📚 Using the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://longform.asmartbear.com/needs-stack/">Needs Stack for competitive strategy</a></p><p>📚 This AI tool helped me <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://mitsloan.mit.edu/ideas-made-to-matter/ai-tool-helped-me-choose-right-market-my-startup">choose the right market for my startup</a></p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://x.com/joshgans/status/2013235537621012713">Gen AI shows a pattern</a>: it excels at some tasks but fails at seemingly similar ones. This "jagged" performance creates a fundamental problem for users trying to decide when to rely on AI</p><p>📚 American Bar Association: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.americanbar.org/content/dam/aba/administrative/center-for-innovation/ai-task-force/2025-ai-task-force-year2-report.pdf">ABA Task Force on Law and Artificial Intelligence</a></p><p>📚 Choose <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://mitsloan.mit.edu/ideas-made-to-matter/choose-human-path-ai">the human path for AI</a> (Future of Work)</p><p>🎧 </p><p>🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/qACjfWKeVSM?si=DEIPnNuDCR2NWIBo~">Pricing Your AI First Product</a>: Why Transactional Models Are on the Rise with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Defy.VC">Defy.VC</a>'s Medha Agarwal</p><p></p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Erasmus for Young Entrepreneurs</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/erasmus-for-young-entrepreneurs</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/erasmus-for-young-entrepreneurs</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 20 Jan 2026 18:08:03 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Chris Barton</dc:creator>
      <description>A Launchpad for Portuguese Founders to Go Global In Portugal’s vibrant, ever-evolving startup landscape, the difference between an idea and a thriving business often comes down to experience, network, and confidence. That’s exactly where Erasmus for Young Entrepreneurs steps in — an EU-funded…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span><strong>A Launchpad for Portuguese Founders to Go Global</strong></span></p><p>In Portugal’s vibrant, ever-evolving startup landscape, the difference between <em>an idea</em> and <em>a thriving business</em> often comes down to experience, network, and confidence. That’s exactly where <strong>Erasmus for Young Entrepreneurs</strong> steps in — an EU-funded programme that offers aspiring Portuguese founders the opportunity to learn directly from seasoned business owners in other European ecosystems, expand their horizons, and accelerate their entrepreneurial journey. (Overview)</p><p>At its core, the programme pairs you — a motivated <em>New Entrepreneur (NE)</em> — with an established <em>Host Entrepreneur (HE)</em> for a period of exchange in another participating country. It’s more than just travel: it’s an immersive mentorship experience <span>backed by EU financial support</span> and practical guidance, designed to deepen your business understanding, broaden your global outlook, and build meaningful cross-border networks.</p><p><span><strong>Why This Matters for Portuguese Founders</strong></span></p><p>Portugal’s startup ecosystem is buzzing — from Lisbon and Porto to Braga and beyond — but connecting with seasoned operators and international markets can still be a challenge. Erasmus for Young Entrepreneurs bridges that gap by placing you shoulder-to-shoulder with experienced entrepreneurs abroad, letting you <em>learn by doing</em> rather than reading. You gain hands-on skills in areas such as operations, marketing, product development, client acquisition, financing, and more — all while living and working in a new cultural context.</p><p>And the support is real: NEs receive a monthly EU grant to help cover travel and living costs during the exchange. That means you can focus on growth, not financial stress.</p><p><span><strong>Real Success Stories — Portuguese Entrepreneurs Who Took the Leap</strong></span></p><p>There’s no better testimony than lived experience. Over recent years, Portuguese entrepreneurs have embraced Erasmus for Young Entrepreneurs with inspiring results:</p><ul><li><p><strong>David Nabeiro</strong>, 23, co-founder of <em>NovaGate Solutions</em>, developed international consulting expertise while working with a software engineering host — sharpening both his technical and business acumen. (Success Story - David Nabeiro)</p></li><li><p><strong>Humberto Bastos, </strong>20, developer of an app focussed on supporting elderly people to combat loneliness, benefited from the sage advice of his US-based Host Tom Paprocki. (Success Story – Humberto Bastos)</p></li><li><p><strong>Nuno Cunha</strong>, founder at <em>Aavanz</em> in Lisbon, hosted and collaborated with an exchange entrepreneur from Turkey, enriching his local operation with fresh perspectives and cross-cultural workflows. (Success Story - Nuno Cunha)</p></li><li><p><strong>Richard Brook</strong>, at <em>Moinhos Velhos Yoga Detox Center</em>, mentored a health-and-wellness specialist from Spain, strengthening offerings and discovering new customer niches thanks to the exchange. (Success Story - Richard Brook)</p></li><li><p><strong>Filipa Cabrita’s</strong> work with a visiting architect allowed both host and NE to enhance sustainable construction practices and prototyping methods — a brilliant example of practical skills exchange. (Success Story - Filipa Cabrita)</p></li><li><p>Portuguese NE <strong>Pedro Pereira</strong>, aged 25 and active in international relocation services, leveraged the programme to deepen his global business insight — building both competence and confidence. (Success Story - Pedro Pereira)</p></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>Video testimonial from Lisbon-based host in the fashion textile sector.</p></li><li><p>Video testimonial from Portuguese New Entrepreneur from the fitness / nutrition sector who participated in an exchange in Singapore.</p></li></ul><p>These stories reflect a powerful theme: when you step into new contexts with guidance and structure, your entrepreneurial trajectory can fundamentally shift.</p><p><span><strong>How to Get Started</strong></span></p><p>If you’re a Portuguese founder or soon-to-be founder with ambition and curiosity, now is the time to take action. The <strong>British-Portuguese Chamber of Commerce (BPCC)</strong> is the <em>Intermediary Organisation</em> supporting Portuguese participants — helping you register, apply, and match with an appropriate Host Entrepreneur.</p><p>To kickstart your EYE journey:</p><p><strong>Register with BPCC as your nominated Intermediary Organisation</strong><br> Contact <strong>Chris Barton</strong> at <strong>c.barton@bpcc.pt</strong> for details, eligibility guidance, and support throughout the application process.</p><p>Whether your focus is tech, sustainability, wellness, architecture, design, or any other field, Erasmus for Young Entrepreneurs gives you access to the insights and networks that <em>successful founders</em> often pay years (and thousands of euros) to acquire.</p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Startups &amp; Corporates | Week 3</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/startups-corporates-week-3</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/startups-corporates-week-3</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 19 Jan 2026 18:00:42 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>I’ve been following the Scale Up Now initiative from Startup Portugal. Their ambition is clear and aligned with what our ecosystem needs: a bigger and more powerful presence in the USA. On day one, one of the topics on the table was Startups &amp;amp; Corporates — a partnership still undervalued, in my…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>I’ve been following the Scale Up Now initiative from Startup Portugal. Their ambition is clear and aligned with what our ecosystem needs: a bigger and more powerful presence in the USA. On day one, one of the topics on the table was Startups &amp; Corporates — a partnership still undervalued, in my opinion. Some of the insights shared by Ana Simões (Brisa) and Pedro Santos (Sonae) led me to this week’s topic.</p><p>In every mature tech ecosystem, startups and corporates don’t just coexist, they need each other. And when they finally realise it, everyone wins. In Portugal, we’re getting better, but we’re still far from unlocking its full potential. Too often, corporates see startups as “interesting” instead of “strategic,” and startups see corporates as “slow” instead of “scalable.” Both are missing the point.</p><p>Startups are R&amp;D engines. Corporates are distribution machines. Together, they compress time.</p><p><strong>What Corporates Gain:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Speed: Startups move fast because they must. Corporates move fast when they partner with them</p></li><li><p>Talent proximity: the best founders don’t apply for jobs; they build companies. Corporates that collaborate early stay close to the next generation of problem‑solvers</p></li><li><p>New revenue lines: not “innovation labs,” not “hackathons,” but real pilots that turn into real contracts</p></li><li><p>Cultural oxygen: nothing shakes up internal teams like seeing a three‑person startup out‑execute a big organisation</p></li></ul><p><strong>What Startups Gain:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Credibility: a corporate logo on your deck is a cheat code for trust</p></li><li><p>Distribution: one corporate deal can equal large number of SME clients</p></li><li><p>Data &amp; domain expertise: Startups bring the agility; corporates bring the context</p></li><li><p>A path to scale: not every startup needs VC. Some just need a corporate that believes in them</p></li></ul><p>When these two worlds collaborate with intention, ecosystems accelerate.</p><p>You get: faster adoption of new technologies; more competitive industries; stronger local talent pipelines; culture where innovation is a behaviour</p><p>This is how countries move from “emerging ecosystem” to “innovation leader", through partnerships that actually ship.</p><p>This matters because Portugal is at an inflection point </p><ul><li><p>We have founders building relevant companies.</p></li><li><p>We have corporates hungry for transformation.</p></li></ul><p>What we lack is structured collaboration, repeatable, scalable, mutually beneficial. More Corporates with the vision already materialized by Brisa, Sonae, Fidelidade, Galp, Semapa, Delta, Microsoft, to name a few of the most active. </p><p>When one Startup x Corporate partnership works, it becomes a story, and stories spread faster than funding rounds; other Founders hear about it and think, “Maybe this is possible.”; other Corporates hear about it and think, “Maybe we should try this too.” Investors hear about it and think, “Maybe this ecosystem is maturing.”</p><p>And once the flywheel starts turning, everything accelerates: Startups stop building in isolation and start building with real market insight; Corporates stop fearing change and start shaping it; talent stops leaving and starts believing; and, policymakers stop reacting and start enabling. This is how momentum forms.</p><p>💡 <strong>LandingJobs  </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://landingjobs.typeform.com/ttt2026">The Tech Talent Trends 2026 is ON</a>! the study made by the tech community for the tech community is counting on you again!</p><p>💡 <strong>Scale Up Now</strong> Demo Day by Startup Portugal, this Friday</p><p>💡 Calling all MSc, Ph.D., and Postdoc students in STEM areas or fields of study! Are you ready to turn your innovative ideas into the next big thing? Join <strong>Faber</strong>'s exclusive <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ep.faber.vc/">Entrepreneurship Program</a> (deadline Mar 01) and learn from the real-life experiences of successful entrepreneurs who have turned their dreams into thriving businesses</p><p>💡 <strong>Founder Institute Portugal</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.meetup.com/lisbon-startup-founder-101/events/312911334/">Demo Day</a> on Jan 29 </p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“Speed is a leadership decision. Faster is better than perfect"</p><p>Andy Jassy</p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 <strong>LisboaUX </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://jobs.lisboaux.com/">just launched a brand new job board</a>. A growing list of Design Jobs already live; take the chance to join the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://whatsapp.com/channel/0029VbBgMmb6hENv6HkmMt2R">WhatsApp channel</a> and the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://lisboaux.com/slack">Slack Community</a>.</p><p>🔷 Are you a student entrepreneur from NOVA? The <strong>Starters Academy</strong> is the right opportunity. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://forms.office.com/Pages/ResponsePage.aspx?id=ZXEus-oUfUu5KvBRH_ptJ8bBXKHXvbBIkFiGvTkzrA1UQlJVT0E4VUhDMk1ZUUlCWlNOVTJHMUdVVyQlQCN0PWcu">Apply until</a> Jan 26.</p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏   <strong>Chrono Health</strong> has raised 2.7M.</p><p>👏   <strong>Ana Martins</strong> (MELLA Supply), <strong>Daniela Hernández </strong>(Equivalence), <strong>Inês Freire de Andrade </strong>(No Bully Portugal), and <strong>Tiago Fortuna </strong>(Access Lab) awarded by the European Commission.</p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 As startups portuguesas têm de saber <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://tek.sapo.pt/noticias/negocios/artigos/as-startups-portuguesas-tem-de-saber-quando-vir-para-os-eua">quando vir para os EUA</a> with Miguel Aguiar.</p><p>📚 A <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sedefsahin.notion.site/A-Founder-s-Guide-to-Building-a-Team-Prepared-for-Founder-Institute-2d7c2c24530880e98d2cc0769f9b465b">Founder’s Guide to Building a Team</a> by Sedef Şahin, Founder <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.talentbased.co/">Talent Based</a>.</p><p>📚 Viewpoint: The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sciencebusiness.net/viewpoint/start-ups/viewpoint-missing-pillar-eus-start-strategy-risk">missing pillar of EU’s start-up strategy is risk</a> by Paulo Andrez.</p><p>📚 Be <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://x.com/jaynitx/status/2011712639790170236">Palmer Luckey</a> (serial entrepreneur).</p><p>📚 AI Prompts for <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://productacademy.notion.site/AI-Prompts-for-JTDB-and-Persona-Research-28a71b32838480f28d8cfc814f439afc">JTDB and Persona Research</a> (Product Academy).</p><p>🎧 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://expresso.pt/podcasts/liga-dos-inovadores/2026-01-14-criamos-a-nossa-empresa-quase-por-raiva-muitos-desistem-de-se-candidatar-a-fundos-europeus-por-causa-da-burocracia-94c3f3d5">Liga dos Inovadores</a>: with Bernardo Seixas, Granter.</p><p>🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sS8Q2mRdtWE">Previsões 2026 (Tech, AI, Robots, Negócios)</a>: Alvaro Samagaio talk with Humberto Ayres Pereira and Henrique Cruz from Rows.com.</p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>What Venture Studios Actually Do and Why Started Studios.pt was created</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/what-venture-studios-actually-do-and-why-started-studios-pt-was-created</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/what-venture-studios-actually-do-and-why-started-studios-pt-was-created</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 15 Jan 2026 19:59:09 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Rui Gouveia</dc:creator>
      <description>In 2024 at a Web Summit side-event for venture studios, something became obvious: the gap between American and European studios, and Portuguese studios was huge. We were behind… way behind. Portugal has maybe 10 to 15 venture studios right now. That&apos;s not enough. Not even close. So myself and João…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span>In 2024 at a Web Summit side-event for venture studios, something became obvious: the gap between American and European studios, and Portuguese studios was huge. We were behind… way behind.</span></p><p><span>Portugal has maybe 10 to 15 venture studios right now. That's not enough. Not even close.</span></p><p><span>So myself and João Pereira from </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://builduplabs.com/"><span>Build Up Labs</span></a><span> together with João Neves Monteiro and João Santos from </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.cron.studio/"><span>Cron Studio</span></a><span>, Miguel Fernandes and Jorge Cabaço from </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.dengun.com/pt-pt/"><span>Dengun</span></a><span>, Ricardo Macedo from </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.laikaventures.co/"><span>Laika</span></a><span>, Pedro Coutinho from THV.vc, Rui Neves Ferreira from </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://novalegal.pt/"><span>Nova Legal</span></a><span>, João Silva from </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupportugal.com/"><span>Startup Portugal</span></a><span>, Nuno Lopes Gama and Marta Egídio Pereira, decided to do something about it and launched Studios.pt.</span></p><h2><span><strong>What's a Venture Studio?</strong></span></h2><p><span>A venture studio is a company that builds companies.</span></p><p><span>It plays three roles at once:</span></p><p><span>🚀 <strong>Entrepreneur</strong> – coming up with ideas (or sourcing those from external entrepreneurs) and validating them<br> 📈 <strong>Investor</strong> – putting in the initial capital<br> ⚙ <strong>Builder/Operator</strong> – providing the team and shared resources</span></p><p><span>Here's what that actually means for founders: they get accounting, legal, HR, design, tech, and marketing support without having to hire anyone. They get tested methodologies and accumulated knowledge from all the startups the studio built before. They get office space and initial funding.</span></p><p><span>This lets the founders focus on what matters: validating and differentiating the business idea.</span></p><h2><span><strong>How Venture Studios Compare</strong></span></h2><p><span>People ask me all the time: "Isn't this just an incubator?" No. Here's the real difference:</span></p><p><span><strong>Venture Studio</strong></span></p><ul><li><p><span><strong>Primary Role:</strong> Hands-on: Cofounder, Team, Shared Resources, Capital</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Typical Investment:</strong> €50K-€500K</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Equity Stake:</strong> 20-60%</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Value Proposition:</strong> Higher success rate, Systematic company building, Shared resources &amp; Expert team</span></p></li></ul><p><span><strong>Incubator</strong></span></p><ul><li><p><span><strong>Primary Role:</strong> Mentoring, Community and Network</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Typical Investment:</strong> €0K-€15K</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Equity Stake:</strong> 0-10%</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Value Proposition:</strong> Safe environment for idea development</span></p></li></ul><p><span><strong>Accelerator</strong></span></p><ul><li><p><span><strong>Primary Role:</strong> Growth catalyst, Pilot opportunities, Fundraising</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Typical Investment:</strong> €20K-€150K</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Equity Stake:</strong> 5-15%</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Value Proposition:</strong> Business model validation, Rapid scaling, Investor readiness</span></p></li></ul><p><span><strong>VC Fund</strong></span></p><ul><li><p><span><strong>Primary Role:</strong> Financial investor, Strategic advisor</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Typical Investment:</strong> Pre-Seed: up to €500K; Seed: €1-5M; Series A: €5-15M</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Equity Stake:</strong> 10-20% per round</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Value Proposition:</strong> Growth capital, Strategic connections for scaling</span></p></li></ul><p><span>The key difference? Studios are in the trenches with founders. Not just writing checks or giving advice twice a month.</span></p><h2><span><strong>What We're Doing</strong></span></h2><p><span>Our mission at the Association is simple: to make venture studios a logical option for anyone who wants to create innovative businesses - entrepreneurs, corporations, universities, investors, and public institutions.</span></p><p><span>Here's our agenda:</span></p><ul><li><p><span><strong>Support New Venture Studios </strong>– Help new venture studios launch and succeed</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Advocacy &amp; Awareness </strong>– Explain the model and its impact on innovation</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>Attract capital</strong> – Bring institutional investors and family offices to this new asset class</span></p></li><li><p><span><strong>International</strong> <strong>collaboration</strong> – Connect Portuguese studios with a global network</span></p></li></ul><h2><span><strong>Why It Matters</strong></span></h2><p><span>We believe the next decade will position venture studios as the right context for building successful startups. The progression makes sense: creating startups in garages taught us about passion, incubators added mentorship and network, and now studios bring systematic, repeatable processes backed by experienced professionals.</span></p><h2><span><strong>Ready to Get Involved?</strong></span></h2><p><span>Whether you're an investor looking for a new asset class, or a corporation wanting to innovate systematically, or a University willing to better bridge research and market, or a public institution wanting to upscale its entrepreneurial ecosystem, there's a place for you in the Association. Visit us at </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://studios.pt"><em>studios.pt</em></a><span>. Let's build the next generation of successful Portuguese startups together.</span></p><p></p><hr><p></p><p><span><em>Rui Gouveia is CEO of Build Up Labs and President of </em></span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://studios.pt"><span><em>studios.pt</em></span></a><span><em> .</em></span></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Solo Founder? Why not? | Week 2</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/solo-founder-why-not-week-2</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/solo-founder-why-not-week-2</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 12 Jan 2026 17:26:30 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>For years, the startup core ideology was clear: you need a co‑founder. YC said it. Founder Institute said it. Investors repeated it so often it became muscle memory. Even I, wearing my investor hat, instinctively flagged solo founders as “riskier.” But something is shifting and not slightly, it’s…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>For years, the startup core ideology was clear: you need a co‑founder. YC said it. Founder Institute said it. Investors repeated it so often it became muscle memory. Even I, wearing my investor hat, instinctively flagged solo founders as “riskier.”</p><p>But something is shifting and not slightly, it’s more a structural change in how companies are being built.</p><p>This week I stumbled on a piece of data that grabbed my attention, even more due to the last session of the Founder Institute Portugal was about 'How to find your Co-Founder'; more than one‑third of all new startups in 2025 were founded by solo founders. Not as an exception. As a trend. As a new normal.</p><p>And suddenly, the session I ran with my fellow partners Elisa and Fernando at Founder Institute Portugal on “how to find your co‑founder” felt… incomplete. Not wrong but incomplete.</p><p>Because the truth is that the world that created the “mandatory co‑founder” rule is not the world we’re building in today.</p><ul><li><p>AI has changed the cost of execution</p></li><li><p>No‑code has changed the cost of prototyping</p></li><li><p>Global talent has changed the cost of scaling</p></li></ul><p>And founders themselves have changed. I've seen it myself on different programs with I work with; they’re more experienced, more technical, more resourceful, and often more capable of carrying the early weight alone than the ecosystem gives them credit for. This doesn’t mean co‑founders are obsolete. Far from it. But it does mean the old dogma “solo = red flag” is starting to feel outdated.</p><p>What we’re seeing now is a more nuanced reality:</p><ul><li><p>Some founders thrive alone and only need a team later.</p></li><li><p>Some founders force a co‑founder relationship too early and regret it.</p></li><li><p>Some founders are better off solo than with the wrong partner.</p></li><li><p>And some of the most resilient companies start with one person obsessed enough to push through the first impossible miles.</p></li></ul><p>Maybe the real question isn’t “Do you have a co‑founder?”</p><p>Maybe it’s “Do you have what you need to build the first version of your company?”</p><p>As an ecosystem, we need to evolve with the times. As investors, we need to update our filters. And as founder‑support organizations, we need to stop treating co‑founders as mandatory and start treating them as strategic one option among many, not a checkbox.</p><p>The rise of the solo founder is a reflection of the tools, the talent, and the times.</p><p>And if one‑third of new startups are being built this way, maybe it’s time we stop calling it an exception and start calling it what it is: a legitimate path to building great companies.</p><p><strong>💡 </strong>Save the date! <strong>StartupWeekend Women Loulé</strong> will take place next March 6, 7 &amp; 8. An inclusive event open to anyone who wants to support and empower women founders and innovators!</p><p>💡 <strong>LandingJobs  </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://landingjobs.typeform.com/ttt2026">The Tech Talent Trends 2026 is ON</a>! the study made by the tech community for the tech community is counting on you again!</p><p>💡 <strong>Hackaboa</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://hackaboa.com/">is a community-run group</a> of indie makers / coders / designers / hardware hackers who build their own independent apps/startups, meeting up every Thursday for weekly co-working (and demos) at Unicorn Factory Lisboa</p><p>💡 Calling all MSc, Ph.D., and Postdoc students in STEM areas or fields of study! Are you ready to turn your innovative ideas into the next big thing? Join <strong>Faber</strong>'s exclusive <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ep.faber.vc/">Entrepreneurship Program</a> (deadline Mar 01) and learn from the real-life experiences of successful entrepreneurs who have turned their dreams into thriving businesses.</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a>.</p><h2>✍ Quote of the week</h2><blockquote><p>“It’s not about ideas. It’s about making ideas happen.”</p><p>Scott Belsky</p></blockquote><h2>Highlights of the week</h2><p>🔷 SCALE UP NOW, promoted by <strong>Startup Portugal </strong>in collaboration with <strong>Plug and Play</strong>, is a program designed to prepare Portuguese startups for the challenges and opportunities of expanding into the United States market - the world’s largest innovation ecosystem. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupportugal.com/programs/scale-up-now-en/">Apply here</a></p><p>🔷&nbsp;<strong>Cobuntu</strong>,&nbsp;a&nbsp;platform&nbsp;where&nbsp;communities&nbsp;become&nbsp;co-creation engines&nbsp;of&nbsp;aligned&nbsp;sustainability&nbsp;promote&nbsp;the&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/z8guen6g">Community&nbsp;Campfire</a>&nbsp;with&nbsp;free&nbsp;practical&nbsp;strategies&nbsp;and&nbsp;insights&nbsp;drawn&nbsp;from&nbsp;real-world&nbsp;experience. </p><h2>Congrats</h2><p>👏  <strong>Lampsy</strong>, <strong>Manie</strong>, <strong>DOJO AI</strong> and <strong>Windcredible</strong> <span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);">made WIRED's 100 Hottest Startups in Europe list.</span></p><p>👏  Le Ticket (french media for PMs) has featured <strong>PRODUCTIZED Conference </strong>as one of the leading product events for 2026.</p><p>👏  <strong>Pedro Nunes Institute</strong> is now joined by <strong>Instituto Superior Técnico</strong> in managing the European Space Agency’s (ESA) business incubation programme.</p><h2>Something to read, listen and watch</h2><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/europes-beer-crisis-isnt-why-future-fmcg-decided-nuno-fernandes-zzlfe/">Europe’s Beer Crisis Isn’t About Beer</a> or Why the Future of FMCG Will Be Decided in Restaurants by Nuno Fernandes (DIG-IN).</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://addyosmani.com/blog/21-lessons/">21 Lessons From 14 Years at Google</a> by Addy Osmani.</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://stratechery.com/2026/ai-and-the-human-condition/">AI and the Human Condition</a> by Ben Thompson.</p><p>📚 EIT <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eit.europa.eu/news-events/news/eit-health-annual-report-2024-advancing-health-innovation-across-europe">Health Annual Report</a> 2024.</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eu-startups.com/2026/01/ai-for-healthcare-admin-meet-the-startups-that-are-providing-the-right-tech-at-the-right-time/">AI for healthcare</a> admin.</p><p>📚 A multimodal <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-025-04133-4">sleep foundation model for disease prediction</a> by Nature Medicine.</p><p>🎧 Modem Futura on Technosphere and Solarpunk: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://podcasts.apple.com/tn/podcast/technosphere-and-solarpunk-designing-energy-futures/id1771688480">Designing Energy Futures That Let Us Thrive</a> with Clark Miller.</p><p>🎥 Interview with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/gpp08b_zL28?si=y4taK0y3AkLaU-nA">founder of Statista and CEO of ECDB</a> Friedrich Schwandt.</p><p>🎥 João Cotter Salvado aborda<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/OA95jS1pTlc?si=EvSm0-coZj1JMd6W"> empreendedorismo e o crescimento do Católica-Lisbon Entrepreneurship Center</a> (CLEC).</p><p>🎥 Adora Cheung (YC Partner) on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/lL6GdUHIBsM">How to Set KPIs and Goals.</a></p><p></p><p>Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Hello 2026 👐 | Week 1</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/hello-2026-week-1</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/hello-2026-week-1</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 05 Jan 2026 10:24:03 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>Last year, I highlighted how Portuguese startups continue to prove the country’s ability to turn bold ideas into real, impactful solutions and how that momentum is setting a global standard for innovation. I also noted how investors are paying closer attention to Portugal, drawn by our strategic…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Last year, I highlighted how Portuguese startups continue to prove the country’s ability to turn bold ideas into real, impactful solutions and how that momentum is setting a global standard for innovation. I also noted how investors are paying closer attention to Portugal, drawn by our strategic location, strong talent pool, and increasingly pro‑business environment. And of course, EU funding remains a true game‑changer, helping startups scale faster and compete globally.</p><p>Now, 2026 opens with an interesting duality in our ecosystem: we’re more mature than ever, yet still strangely hesitant to call ourselves mature. Over the past decade, we’ve built talent pipelines, accelerators, funds, and communities that simply didn’t exist before. We’ve demonstrated that we can build global companies from Lisbon, Porto, Braga, Coimbra; you name it. And still, we often talk about ourselves as if we’re “almost there”.</p><p>This year, it’s time to drop the “almost”.</p><p>Founders entering 2026 face a landscape that’s tougher, sharper, and more exciting than anything we’ve seen. Capital is cautious but available. Talent is abundant but more selective. AI is rewriting every playbook. And the founders who win will be the ones who stop waiting for permission and start building with urgency. This will be an unforgiving year for those relying on wishful thinking and an incredibly generous one for those relying on work.</p><p><strong>What should founders expect?</strong></p><p>• <strong>Fundraising will be possible but only for the prepared.</strong> Investors want evidence, not adjectives.<br>• <strong>AI will widen the gap between fast teams and slow ones.</strong> Those who adopt AI early will outpace those who “wait to see”.<br>• <strong>Talent will follow clarity.</strong> People want to join missions, not experiments.<br>• <strong>Regulation will matter more than ever.</strong> Especially in health, fintech, and AI, ignoring it will be costly.<br>• <strong>The more you give, the more you get back.</strong> Founders who mentor, share, and collaborate will see it come back tenfold.</p><p>In 2026, we can expect more venture capital and private equity firms strengthening their presence in Portugal. As more capital flows into startups, we’ll likely see more success stories, more companies going global, more meaningful exits, and more founders proving what’s possible from here. Initiatives like Startup Portugal and Unicorn Factory Lisbon will continue to play a crucial role, offering resources, mentoring, and visibility that push Portuguese startups onto the world stage.</p><p>And as always, community remains one of our greatest assets. Organizations like the 351 Portuguese Startup Association, Startup Grind, and the Founder Institute Portugal continue to shape the ecosystem by supporting founders at every stage. Events such as Web Summit, Startup Week Guimarães, Portugal Tech Week, Techstars Weekend, Algarve Summit, and SIM Conference keep creating spaces for founders to connect, learn, and showcase their work.</p><p>But it’s not just the big stages that matter. The ecosystem also thrives thanks to the communities that support the builders behind the scenes from LisboaJS to LisboaUX, and the many groups that meet every month to share knowledge, solve problems, and push each other forward. These grassroots communities are often where the real innovation culture is forged.</p><p>Our goal for 2026 is to keep you updated with the all relevant information regarding the Portuguese Startup ecosystem.</p><p>I wish you all the success to achieve your personal and Startup business goals.</p><p>Enjoy, and all the best for 2026!</p><p><strong>💡LandingJobs &amp; Damia Portugal </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://landingjobs.typeform.com/ttt2026">The Tech Talent Trends 2026 is ON</a>! the study made by the tech community for the tech community is counting on you again!</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a> </p><p></p><h1>✍ Quote of the week</h1><blockquote><p>“Ever tried. Ever failed. No matter. Try again. Fail again. Fail better.”</p><p><strong>Samuel Beckett</strong></p></blockquote><h1></h1><h1>Highlights of the week</h1><p>🔷 SCALE UP NOW, promoted by <strong>Startup Portugal </strong>in collaboration with <strong>Plug and Play</strong>, is a program designed to prepare Portuguese startups for the challenges and opportunities of expanding into the United States market - the world’s largest innovation ecosystem. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupportugal.com/programs/scale-up-now-en/">Apply here</a></p><p> </p><h1>Congrats</h1><p>👏 <strong>MYLeukaemia</strong>, <strong>ProSpec</strong>, and <strong>SmartRoads</strong> won EIT Jumpstarter awards </p><p></p><h1>Something to read, listen and watch</h1><p>📚How <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.thevccorner.com/p/sequoia-playbook-vc-discipline-systems">Sequoia Actually Makes Decisions</a></p><p>📚AI strength meets correction risk: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://pitchbook.com/news/articles/ai-strength-meets-correction-risk-whats-next-for-european-vc-in-2026">what’s next for European VC in 2026</a></p><p>📚Partech’s Alison Imbert on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupsmagazine.co.uk/article-partechs-alison-imbert-shifting-seed-strategies-and-taking-smarter-risks">shifting seed strategies and taking smarter risks</a></p><p>📚How <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.readtrung.com/p/how-hermes-sells-time">Hermès Sells "Time"</a></p><p>📚Can a social app <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/01/04/can-a-social-app-fix-the-terrible-devastation-of-social-media/">fix the ‘terrible devastation’ of social media</a>?</p><p>🎧<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jpGYBcDy4c4">Founder Tales</a>: Quanto custa o Bitalk e como construir a maior rede nacional de scouts de startups com Tocha</p><p>🎥 Peter Thiel gave a 1-hour masterclass <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://x.com/jaynitx/status/2004586855480856925">on how to build a monopoly from scratch</a></p><p>🎥&nbsp;Sam Altman on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.the-ai-corner.com/p/sam-altman-openai-interview-ai-deployment-memory-enterprise">Where AI Is Actually Going</a></p><p></p><p>💡Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Startup Xmas | Week 43</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/startup-xmas-week-43</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/startup-xmas-week-43</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 15 Dec 2025 14:23:52 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>As 2025 comes to an end, I keep coming back to one thing: this ecosystem grows because people show up. Founders who push through uncertainty, mentors who give without expecting anything back, and a community that keeps raising the bar year after year. We’ve had our share of challenges, but we’ve…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>As 2025 comes to an end, I keep coming back to one thing: this ecosystem grows because people show up. Founders who push through uncertainty, mentors who give without expecting anything back, and a community that keeps raising the bar year after year.</p><p>We’ve had our share of challenges, but we’ve also seen ideas mature, teams evolve, and connections turn into real momentum. That’s the part that makes this work meaningful.</p><p>2026 is already shaping up to be a year of bold bets and new opportunities. Let’s carry forward the creativity, collaboration, and ambition that define this community and keep building the ecosystem we want to see. </p><p>I’ll be back on January 6 and until then, I hope this holiday season brings rest, joy, and a bit of inspiration to you and your loved ones. And because this is a time for meaningful gestures, I want to finish with a few Christmas ideas for a gift with purpose and small actions that support founders, creators, and the communities that make this ecosystem stronger.</p><p>🎅 <strong>Productized Lisbon 2026</strong> | Tickets on Sale starting December 16th, and to celebrate the season, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ti.to/productized/conf2026">with an exclusive 50% Christmas Discount</a> </p><p>🎅 <strong>Purrmi</strong> 🐱 launched a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://purrmi.com/products/purrmi-surprise-box-natal-gato">Xmas Surprise Box</a>. For each Box sold, one meal will be donated to Associação Animais de Rua</p><p>🎅<strong>FLAMAID </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.flamaid.com/">Personal safety grenade</a> with 110 dB alarm and real-time GPS</p><p>🎅<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href=" https://narizvermelho.pt/">Nariz Vermelho</a></p><p>🎅Associação <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://associacaosalvador.com/">Salvador</a> </p><p>🎅Associação de Portadores de <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.apatris21.org/">Trissomia 21 do Algarve</a></p><p>🎅<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.casa-qui.pt/">CasaQui</a></p><p>🎅<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.cvidaepaz.pt/ajudar/">Comunidade Vida e Paz</a> </p><p>🎅and why not send <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/">your favorite Newsletter</a> to a friend? </p><p>Together, as a startup or individual, we have the power to amplify the reach and impact of these incredible efforts, creating a season that will truly be unforgettable.</p><p>Let’s take action together!</p><p><strong>💡</strong>This <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://forms.monday.com/forms/ab8c02cb25b6631782533a600ba609e8?r=euc1">questionnaire</a> from a PhD researcher from a Catolica-Lisbon seeks to understand the local innovation ecosystem in Portugal and identify the needs, challenges, and opportunities. Please take a few minutes to complete it, your input matters. </p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a> </p><p></p><h1>✍ Quote of the week</h1><blockquote><p>“<strong><em>We&nbsp;make&nbsp;a&nbsp;living&nbsp;by&nbsp;what&nbsp;we&nbsp;get.&nbsp;We&nbsp;make&nbsp;a&nbsp;life&nbsp;by&nbsp;what&nbsp;we&nbsp;give"</em></strong></p><p>Winston&nbsp;Churchill</p></blockquote><h1></h1><h1>Highlights of the week</h1><p>🔷 Como <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/8w8wyb35">negociar uma ronda de investimento</a>? by Angels Way this Wednesday</p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/y8qe9gcc">LisboaJS Christmas Edition</a>: JS Under Pressure </p><p>🔷 <strong>LisboaUX Christmas Dinner </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/bquhz2yv">this Friday</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>Portugal &amp; USA: Learnings from an Operator</strong> with João Camarate, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://membrz.club/abc/events/startups-portugal-usa-learnings-from-an-operator">Dec 19 @UPTEC</a></p><p> </p><h1>Congrats</h1><p>👏 <strong>sheerME </strong>has been spotted by Sifted a Financial Times company as the Fastest Growing Consumer Startup in Southern Europe</p><p>👏 <strong>351 Portuguese Startup Association </strong>was awarded the "Rising Star" recognition, by International Chamber of Commerce (ICC)</p><p>👏 <strong>ApneaScreener </strong>distinguished by SheLeads Ventures</p><p>👏 <strong>Coreflux</strong> raised 1.2M</p><p>👏 <strong>FlashGuard </strong>project won the 3rd edition of the Business Acceleration Program – LISPOLIS IGNITE</p><p></p><h1>Something to read, listen and watch</h1><p>📚Reforma do Estado avança com <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.portugal.gov.pt/pt/gc25/comunicacao/noticia">Estratégia Digital e Agenda para a Inteligência Artificial</a></p><p>📚O dinheiro faz nascer startups. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://thenextbigidea.pt/opinioes/o-dinheiro-faz-nascer-startups-os-anjos-certos-fazem-nas-voar/">Os anjos certos fazem-nas voar</a> by Bruno Gutman</p><p>📚The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://scaleupporto.pt/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Characterizationoftheecosystem_final_comp.pdf">Startup Ecosystem in the region of Porto</a> </p><p>📚Lisboa <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://lisboainnovation.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Lisboa-Startup-Ecosystem-Report-2025.pdf">Startup Ecosystem Report</a></p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.deloitte.com/content/dam/assets-zone2/pt/pt/docs/about/2025/fast50-2025/ranking-fast50-2025.pdf">Deloitte Technology</a> Fast 50</p><p>📚The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.productmarketfit.tech/p/the-revolut-investors-who-won-big">Revolut Investors Who Won Big</a> by Guillermo Flor</p><p>📚AI as a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://medium.com/the-square-lisbon/ai-as-a-partner-to-unlock-human-creativity-in-business-e68f4ee17a81">partner to unlock human creativity in business</a> by Joana Guimaraes</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://agetechx.com/blog/lab-data-is-the-missing-rail-for-longevity-inside-openhealths-mission-to-make-health-data-ai-ready">Lab Data is the Missing Rail for Longevity</a>: Inside OpenHealth Technologies' </p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://commission.europa.eu/document/09579818-64a6-4dd5-9577-446ab6219113_en">Cloud Sovereignty</a> Framework</p><p>🎧&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/19BR9dw3lWmZQsnN68hUG4">AI: a tool or the enemy</a> w/ Jake Seid</p><p>🎧&nbsp;CEO of Original ChopShop, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/2ObETeEjvBWAOcVsyqDMd3?si=ZUi1c_bBSrK4sFbBlIT5Ew">discuss the brand's unique fast casual offerings</a> and growth strategy</p><p>🎥&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.rtp.pt/play/p14282/e887009/sociedade-civil">Pensamento Critico na Inteligência Artificial</a>. Num mundo que, em breve, promete ser dominado por algoritmos, será que ainda sabemos questionar? Pode a máquina substituir o discernimento humano? No Sociedade Civil.</p><p>🎥&nbsp;Nuno Loureiro | <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qHvrDq8vKnY">On Failure</a></p><p>🎥&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/PqVbypvxDto?si=Gffb4IOybwh1rrwO">The future of intelligence</a> | Demis Hassabis (Co-founder of DeepMind)</p><p></p><p>💡Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Sweet as a Pastel de Nata | Week 42</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/sweet-as-a-pastel-de-nata-week-42</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/sweet-as-a-pastel-de-nata-week-42</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 08 Dec 2025 23:25:09 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>According to The Economist , our country was named Economy of the Year among 36 developed economies. Strong GDP growth, low inflation, and a stock market up more than 20% are clear signs that we’re attracting talent and investment, and that the economy is gaining real momentum. Good news, and great…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>According to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.economist.com/finance-and-economics/2025/12/07/which-economy-did-best-in-2025">The Economist</a>, our country was named Economy of the Year among 36 developed economies. Strong GDP growth, low inflation, and a stock market up more than 20% are clear signs that we’re attracting talent and investment, and that the economy is gaining real momentum. Good news, and great publicity.</p><p>But let’s stay grounded. This isn’t a medal to over‑celebrate; it’s a signal that we’re a little bit economic healthier than before. The real challenge is to use this moment as a springboard for reforms and to push toward consistent &gt;2% growth. Momentum is momentum but it only matters if we channel it into structural change.</p><p>Recently, the 2025 Entrepreneurial Universities Ranking placed Portuguese institutions in strong positions (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/posts/entrepreneurial-universities-from-campus-to-startup-week-41">Adamastor Week 41</a>), marking a milestone in how we measure the role of academia in building entrepreneurial capacity. Twenty years ago, Portugal was seen as a lagging innovator. Today, it’s one of Europe’s fastest improving innovation ecosystems, and our universities are part of that story.</p><p>For the startup community, this recognition matters. It strengthens Portugal’s brand as a place where founders can build globally competitive companies. It helps attract international talent, investors, and partners who might not have looked our way before. And it validates the work of ecosystem builders, mentors, and innovation intermediaries who’ve been stitching this fabric together piece by piece.</p><p>The benefit is clear: if we align policy, academia, and founders around this momentum, Portugal can move from being “sweet as a pastel de nata” in the headlines to being consistently strong in the metrics that matter; scale‑ups, exits, and global impact.</p><p>Momentum is precious, but it only matters if we use it to build something lasting.</p><p></p><p><strong>💡Productized Lisbon 2026</strong> | Tickets on Sale starting December 16th, and to celebrate the season, with an exclusive 50% Christmas Discount </p><p><strong>💡SCALE UP NOW</strong>, promoted by Startup Portugal in collaboration with Plug and Play, is <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupportugal.com/programs/scale-up-now-en/">a program designed to prepare Portuguese startups</a> for the challenges and opportunities of expanding into the United States market - the world’s largest innovation ecosystem. </p><p><strong>💡</strong>This <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://forms.monday.com/forms/ab8c02cb25b6631782533a600ba609e8?r=euc1">questionnaire</a> from a PhD researcher from a Catolica-Lisbon seeks to understand the local innovation ecosystem in Portugal and identify the needs, challenges, and opportunities. Please take a few minutes to complete it, your input matters.</p><p>🎅 Dec 16 will be the final edition of the year. Kindly take this into account when submitting requests for dissemination.</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a> </p><p></p><h1>✍ Quote of the week</h1><blockquote><p>“The essence of strategy is choosing what not to do”</p><p>Michael Porter</p></blockquote><h1></h1><h1>Highlights of the week</h1><p>🔷 <strong>E.STORIES@TÉCNICO</strong>, today</p><p>🔷 <strong>Ask Me Anything | Scale Up Now</strong> by Startup Portugal and <strong>Ask Santa for a Unicorn - XMAS Quiz</strong> by Startup Grind this Wednesday</p><p>🔷 <strong>Community Leaders Year-End Reflection &amp; Celebration</strong> organized by Led by Community, this Friday</p><p>🔷 <strong>Discoveries</strong>, the acceleration program that helps tourism startups grow, connect and go global powered by Fabrica de Startups <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.startupdiscoveries.com/">Last days !!</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>Fundação Jornada</strong> has opened applications for its support program for projects led by or focused on young people aged 15..35 with grants of up to 30K. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fundacaojornada.pt/oportunidades/">Apply until</a> Dec 16</p><p>🔷 <strong>Portugal &amp; USA: Learnings from an Operator</strong> with João Camarate, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://membrz.club/abc/events/startups-portugal-usa-learnings-from-an-operator">Dec 19 @UPTEC</a></p><p></p><p> </p><h1>Congrats</h1><p>👏 <strong>Shine</strong> (fintech) acquired by Cegid </p><p>👏 <strong>GreenDash</strong> is the winner of the Investor Arenas Final</p><p>👏 <strong>B</strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://loq.it"><strong>loq.it</strong></a>, <strong>i-charging</strong> and <strong>Coverflex </strong>make the Deloitte's “Technology Fast 50 Portugal” Top 3</p><p>👏 <strong>Otitest</strong> and <strong>ablute</strong> won Bologna Innomed Catalyst </p><p>👏 <strong>Spotlite</strong> raises 35M</p><p></p><h1>Something to read, listen and watch</h1><p>📚Which <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.economist.com/finance-and-economics/2025/12/07/which-economy-did-best-in-2025">economy did best in 2025</a>?  by The Economist</p><p>📚Portugal <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://comunicacoes.apdc.pt/portugal-xr-report-2025/70875018">XR Report 2025 </a> by Luis Bravo Martins </p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.allthingsdistributed.com/2025/11/tech-predictions-for-2026-and-beyond.html">Tech predictions</a> for 2026 and beyond</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.deloitte.com/content/dam/assets-zone2/pt/pt/docs/about/2025/fast50-2025/ranking-fast50-2025.pdf">Deloitte - Fast 50</a> 2025</p><p>📚The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://thekernel.news/articles/dawn-of-the-renaissance-developer/">Dawn of the Renaissance Developer</a> by Werner Vogels</p><p>📚Juniper Research Unveils the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.juniperresearch.com/press/juniper-research-unveils-the-top-10-trends-set-to-shape-fintech-payments-in-2026/">Top 10 Trends Set to Shape Fintech &amp; Payments</a> in 2026</p><p>📚EU agrees on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2025/11/27/payment-services-council-and-parliament-agree-to-step-up-the-fight-against-fraud-and-increase-transparency/">new rules for online fraud protection</a></p><p>🎧&nbsp;Alvaro Mayer - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/0pRSDlNSnLpvBUvyS6BAPV">Sair de um buraco e alcançar o sucesso</a> </p><p>🎥&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ihWU-ets1f0">A verdadeira ameaça representada pela IA</a>: Fukuyama entrevista Alex Stamos</p><p>🎥&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/PKb3cCwUteA?si=08_uszbQK9kurQuC">Reinventing Organizations with Product Thinking</a> - Productized </p><p></p><p>💡Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Entrepreneurial Universities: from Campus to Startup | Week 41</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/entrepreneurial-universities-from-campus-to-startup-week-41</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/entrepreneurial-universities-from-campus-to-startup-week-41</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 02 Dec 2025 10:35:13 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>The new 2025 Entrepreneurial Universities Ranking is a milestone in how we measure higher education’s impact in Portugal. How a nation’s universities are valued has long been determined by their research output, academic standing or global rankings. Today, the model is moving: how many startups…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>The new <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupportugal.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Portugals-Entrepreneurial-Universities-Ranking25.pdf">2025 Entrepreneurial Universities Ranking</a> is a milestone in how we measure higher education’s impact in Portugal. How a nation’s universities are valued has long been determined by their research output, academic standing or global rankings. Today, the model is moving: how many startups come out of their halls, how much investment those companies attract and what enterprise value they provide to our economy.</p><p>Topping this year’s ranking is Universidade de Lisboa (ULisboa) with an impressive 1.292 alumni-founded startups, of which 326 have raised investment and a total combined enterprise value of 30B. Both of these are not just statistical wins; it signals the scale at which Portugal’s largest university is shaping entrepreneurial talent. Close behind, Universidade Católica Portuguesa (UCP) and Universidade Nova de Lisboa (NOVA) demonstrate that entrepreneurial excellence is not confined to size. UCP’s 807 startups and NOVA’s 760 highlight how diverse academic environments are contributing to Portugal’s innovation narrative.</p><p>Honestly, this isn’t news to us. We’ve seen this firsthand, founders telling us their classrooms were the real launchpads and we've been talking about it for a while. Earlier this year, we brought in Luis Lamy, a student who made the leap from the classroom to the startup world to tell his story. He made it clear: “entrepreneurial university” isn’t just a buzzword. It’s real. Classrooms can become launchpads. Students turn into founders. And when these founders go out there, they carry their university’s reputation everywhere they go. By sharing stories like Luis’s, we’re proving that this ranking isn’t just a list of numbers. It’s about ambition. It’s about people deciding to build something new.</p><p>Startup Portugal unveiled its latest university ranking at Web Summit 2025, using data from its <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupportugal.dealroom.co/intro">Ecosystem Mapping Platform</a> (Dealroom) and direct input from the schools themselves. It’s a big moment, Portugal’s top tech event shining a light on the institutions that help launch the country’s founders. But there’s something telling hidden in the numbers: only 13 universities even bothered to send in their data. That’s a red flag. Are these schools really ready to put entrepreneurship at the heart of what they do, or are they just not paying attention?</p><p>So why does any of this really matter? Because universities aren’t just places to sit through lectures, they’re where big dreams start. When a graduate’s startup goes global, it’s not just their win; it’s a win for their university, too. A unicorn out of ULisboa doesn’t just make headlines, it puts the school on the map and gets future students excited about what’s possible.</p><p>For the ecosystem, this ranking is both a celebration and a challenge. Celebration, because it validates the maturity of Portugal’s startup scene: founders are no longer isolated dreamers but products of structured environments. Challenge, because it demands that universities across the country step up. Entrepreneurial education cannot be an optional add-on; it must be embedded into every course, supported by incubators, and celebrated as much as academic research.</p><p>As Portugal positions itself on the global innovation map, the role of universities will be decisive. The 2025 ranking is more than a scoreboard, it is a mirror reflecting how knowledge is being transformed into companies, jobs, and economic value. The next step is clear: ensuring that every university, from Algarve to Minho, sees entrepreneurship not as a side effect but as a defining mission.</p><p></p><p>💡are you a <strong>Porto University student</strong>? this is for you! <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://uptec.up.pt/board-of-students/">BOSS: Board of Students</a> is accepting applications until Dec 03</p><p>💡<strong>StartUP Voucher</strong> <strong>25/26 </strong>supports young entrepreneurs in creating tech-based businesses is still accepting applications</p><p><strong>💡SCALE UP NOW</strong>, promoted by Startup Portugal in collaboration with Plug and Play, is a program designed to prepare Portuguese startups for the challenges and opportunities of expanding into the United States market - the world’s largest innovation ecosystem. 🇺🇸</p><p></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a> </p><p></p><h1>✍ Quote of the week</h1><blockquote><p>“Only the humble become learners, and only learners adapt.” </p><p>John C. Maxwell</p></blockquote><h1></h1><h1>Highlights of the week</h1><p>🔷 every Thursday - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.coworkingthursdays.pt/">Coworking Thursdays</a> Lisboa &amp; Porto</p><p>🔷 Meet Up <strong>LISPOLIS</strong>: “1500M€ de oportunidades para PMEs e startups na Defesa em 2026”, this Thursday</p><p>🔷 <strong>Protechting</strong> open innovation program is looking for Startups in Insurtech, Healthtech, Tech, and Sustainability. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.protechting.com/">Apply until</a> Dec 05</p><p>🔷 <strong>Discoveries</strong>, the acceleration program that helps tourism startups grow, connect and go global powered by Fabrica de Startups <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.startupdiscoveries.com/">is open</a> until Dec 12</p><p>🔷 <strong>Fundação Jornada</strong> has opened applications for its support program for projects led by or focused on young people aged 15..35 with grants of up to 30K. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fundacaojornada.pt/oportunidades/">Apply until</a> Dec 16</p><p>🔷 <strong>Portugal &amp; USA: Learnings from an Operator</strong> with João Camarate, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://membrz.club/abc/events/startups-portugal-usa-learnings-from-an-operator">Dec 19 @UPTEC</a></p><p>🔷 Applications are now opened for the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/029e-1f054e5b434d-c337400f106a-1000--champions-innovate-budapest-2026/">UEFA’s innovation programme</a>, <strong>Champions Innovate</strong>.</p><p> </p><h1>Congrats</h1><p>👏 <strong>TUMO</strong> awarded the WISE prize for Education</p><p>👏 <strong>Lampsy</strong> is the winner of the Epilepsy Foundation Accelerator</p><p>👏 <strong>Luca</strong> raised 6.8M</p><p>👏 <strong>Indie Seguros</strong> is expanding to Spain with Hiscox and OSCAR</p><p>👏 <strong>PCI · Creative Science Park Aveiro Region</strong> launch Digital Factory</p><p></p><h1>Something to read, listen and watch</h1><p>📚Portugal’s <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupportugal.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Portugals-Entrepreneurial-Universities-Ranking25.pdf">Entrepreneurial Universities Ranking 2025</a> report</p><p>📚From Lecture Halls to Startup Calls: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/posts/144">The Journey of Being a University Founder</a> by Luis Lamy</p><p>📚Júnior Empresa: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://eco.sapo.pt/opiniao/dia-mundial-da-junior-empresa-o-futuro-constroi-se-desde-cedo/">o futuro constrói-se desde cedo</a> by Carlos Rebelo</p><p>📚What Web Summit Really Gives Us and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://withagrainofsalt.substack.com/p/what-web-summit-really-gives-us">Why We Keep Coming Back</a> by Sal</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/08-building-resilient-execution-culture-how-survive-first-mendes-bt7pf/">Building Resilient Execution Culture</a>: How to Survive the First Big Hits by Carlos Mendes</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://foreignpolicy.com/2025/05/23/apple-china-foxconn-factories/">How China Captured Apple</a>: A giant firm and a superpower have become deeply entangled.</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://read.technically.dev/p/databricks-is-apparently-worth-100b">Databricks is apparently worth</a> $100B. What do they even do?</p><p>🎧&nbsp;Masters of Scale: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/3zdShWikGzeYnTktEMlVzP?si=yKJ34wdPS5-uLWKvPBbaJA">the power of mentors</a></p><p>🎥&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/3x0bTzGWJ18">Startups x Healthcare</a>: Driving the future of health</p><p>🎥&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/RpklS78GX0Y?si=pOGqX6dWmeY6izV0">Building an AI Startup in Portugal with João Graça</a> (Co-Founder, Unbabel)</p><p></p><p>💡Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Portugal’s Sword Health and the Future of Care | Week 40</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/portugal-s-sword-health-and-the-future-of-care-week-40</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/portugal-s-sword-health-and-the-future-of-care-week-40</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 24 Nov 2025 14:22:41 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>Sword Health has announced a landmark partnership with the Greek government to deploy its AI care solutions in the Greek National Health System. This bold step points to a future where artificial intelligence and human clinical teams work side by side, breaking barriers of access, cost, and…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Sword Health</strong> has announced a landmark partnership with the Greek government to deploy its AI care solutions in the Greek National Health System. This bold step points to a future where artificial intelligence and human clinical teams work side by side, breaking barriers of access, cost, and geography to deliver high‑quality care. </p><p>Virgílio Bento, Sword’s founder, framed it clearly: this partnership is not just about Greece. It’s a blueprint for how nations can adopt AI at scale in healthcare. For systems long constrained by inefficiency and inequity, change requires more than vision it demands courage to break with the status quo. Greece has shown that courage, and in doing so, may inspire others to follow.</p><p>For Portugal’s ecosystem, this is more than a proud moment. It’s proof that our startups are not only competing globally, but redefining what’s possible. Sword Health is exporting not just technology, but a philosophy: that healthcare can be universal, affordable, and human‑centered; if we dare to reimagine it.</p><p>And as momentum builds from Web Summit, Lisboa AI Week, and Portugal Tech Week, this announcement reminds us why we build: innovation is not an end in itself but a lever to transform lives. When a Portuguese startup partners with a European government to reshape healthcare, it signals that our ecosystem is ready to lead—because Portugal’s startups aren’t just building companies, they’re building the future of healthcare and showing Europe how it’s done.</p><p><strong>💡StartUP Voucher</strong> <strong>25/26 </strong>supports young entrepreneurs in creating tech-based businesses is still accepting applications</p><p><strong>💡SCALE UP NOW</strong>, promoted by Startup Portugal in collaboration with Plug and Play, is a program designed to prepare Portuguese startups for the challenges and opportunities of expanding into the United States market - the world’s largest innovation ecosystem. 🇺🇸</p><p></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a> </p><p></p><h1>✍ Quote of the week</h1><blockquote><p>"Life is too short to waste the talent we are given"</p><p><strong>Virgilio Bento</strong></p></blockquote><h1></h1><h1>Highlights of the week</h1><p>🔷 every Thursday - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.coworkingthursdays.pt/">Coworking Thursdays</a> Lisboa &amp; Porto</p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://forms.office.com/pages/responsepage.aspx">CyberIgnite</a>: Workshop de Aceleração @ BSides Porto next Nov 28 &amp; 29</p><p> 🔷 <strong>Nova Startup Club </strong>pitch session this Thursday</p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://point-and.involve.me/better-mobility-for-eurovision">European Call for Mobility &amp; Tourism Innovations</a>, apply until Nov 30 -New Date!- </p><p>🔷 <strong>Madeira Startup Retreat</strong>, will take place between Feb 9 and Mar 20 and is accepting applications <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://retreat.startupmadeira.eu/">until Nov 30</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>Protechting</strong> open innovation program is looking for Startups in Insurtech, Healthtech, Tech, and Sustainability. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.protechting.com/">Apply until</a> Dec 05</p><p>🔷 <strong>Discoveries</strong>, the acceleration program that helps tourism startups grow, connect and go global powered by Fabrica de Startups <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.startupdiscoveries.com/">is open</a> until Dec 12</p><p>🔷 <strong>Fundação Jornada</strong> has opened applications for its support program for projects led by or focused on young people aged 15..35 with grants of up to 30K. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://fundacaojornada.pt/oportunidades/">Apply until</a> Dec 16</p><p>🔷 <strong>Copenhagen</strong>’s new AI-first hackathon <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/zmho1iqy">is accepting applications</a> </p><p>🔷 Applications are now opened for the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/029e-1f054e5b434d-c337400f106a-1000--champions-innovate-budapest-2026/">UEFA’s innovation programme</a>, <strong>Champions Innovate</strong>.</p><p> </p><h1>Congrats</h1><p>👏 <strong>Sword Health</strong> announced a partnership with the Greek government to deploy Sword's AI care solutions in the Greek National Health System</p><p>👏 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://STUDIOS.PT"><strong>STUDIOS.PT</strong></a> – Portuguese Venture Studio Association was official launched </p><p>👏 <strong>Portugal Tech Week</strong> had more than 300 events nationwide and over 30.000 people impacted!</p><p>👏 <strong>i-charging</strong> awarded with Prémio PME Inovação COTEC-BPI 2025</p><p>👏 launch of <strong>Critical FlyTech</strong>, a joint venture between Airbus and Critical Software</p><p>👏 <strong>Usawa Care </strong>(Nova spin-off) is the winner of the Global eAwards 2025</p><p>👏 <strong>BrainR </strong>selected for the Sifted's Future 50 2025</p><p>👏 <strong>Henri Horlitz, Leonard Deburba, Diogo Carvalho</strong> and <strong>Ricardo Pereira</strong> won FORGE, Portugal’s biggest AI hackathon by NOVAe.</p><p>👏 <strong>Trash4Goods</strong> won ARA Award, an award created by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://AI9.PT">AI9.PT</a> - Associação Portuguesa para a Inovação e Empreendedorismo Social e Digital </p><p>👏 <strong>Phama&amp;Go</strong> powered by Sensei opened their store, 1st of its kind in Europe</p><p>👏 all the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.portuguesewomenintech.com/awards25">Portuguese Women in Tech</a> winners </p><p></p><h1>Something to read, listen and watch</h1><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://expresso.pt/iniciativaseprodutos/projetos-expresso/2025-10-31-a-vida-e-demasiado-curta-para-perder-o-talento-que-nos-e-dado-ec81a627">A vida é demasiado curta para perder o talento que nos é dado</a> w/ Virgilio Bento</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.publico.pt/2025/11/10/sociedade/noticia/espera-visto-criacao-ia-treina-empatia-historia-fahima-sina-2153799">Da espera por visto à criação de IA que treina empatia</a>: a história de Fahima e Sina (WiseWorld)</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/posts/87">Why the Startup Voucher Matters</a> — And Why You Should Apply Now by Fernando Fraga</p><p>📚Sifted <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://sifted.eu/leaderboards/sifted-future-50-2025/*pass50*">Future 50</a> (2025)</p><p>📚Linus Torvalds is OK with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.theregister.com/2025/11/18/linus_torvalds_vibe_coding/">vibe coding</a> as long as it's not used for anything that matters</p><p>📚So <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ivanoel_why-angels-invest-activity-7388854569436532737-e3AG/">why would business angels (BA) write checks</a> instead of investing in a venture capital (VC) fund? by Ivanoel Rodrigues</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://zenodo.org/records/17333919">Augmented urban analysis</a>: integrating open data and collective intelligence for decision support in Lisbon with "O Meu Bairro" by Afonso Santos in collaboration with Unlockit</p><p>🎧&nbsp;Inovadores convida <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/0qscuMjV6bZ0dTgYIDVUqE?si=32862c14456e4bfa">Tiago Cunha Costa &amp; BloodFlow</a></p><p>🎥&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/qiXH0y2V3_8?si=swwwlvKi2fXUYYff">Daniel Ek, Spotify</a> | David Senra<strong> </strong></p><p>🎥&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/ucuXB5p9WWg?si=ljtSF1PzkOySnI-J">How AI Is Changing Grants</a> | OWners E03 with Bernardo Seixas</p><p>🎥&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/wsGVeja2Ub4?si=cr0geGn8fREr1oBl">Inside Microsoft's AI Superfactory</a> with Scott Guthrie</p><p></p><p>💡Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>From Lecture Halls to Startup Calls: The  Journey of Being a University Founder</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/from-lecture-halls-to-startup-calls-the-journey-of-being-a-university-founder</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/from-lecture-halls-to-startup-calls-the-journey-of-being-a-university-founder</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 15 Nov 2025 20:28:10 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Luís Lamy</dc:creator>
      <description>Degrees and Dreams Balancing the demands of your studies with the challenges of building a startup is not a common path, yet it’s an incredibly rewarding one. More and more students are starting to ask themselves: “Why wait until graduation to create real impact?” Being a founder while studying can…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<h3>Degrees and Dreams</h3><p>Balancing the demands of your studies with the challenges of building a startup is not a common path, yet it’s an incredibly rewarding one. More and more students are starting to ask themselves: “Why wait until graduation to create real impact?”</p><p>Being a founder while studying can (and will) be chaotic, exhausting and, at times, extremely overwhelming. But it provides a set of opportunities and learning experiences that a single place couldn’t give by itself. Universities provide a chance to be part of many communities to know like-minded people for whichever goal you may have, and the ecosystem always provides opportunities to connect with inspiring people.</p><p>In my case, I’m currently in my final year of the MSc in Computer Science and Engineering at NOVA FCT, engaging in the past in incredible initiatives that allowed me to grow in many ways.</p><h3>Prior to University</h3><p>I began building small businesses by the age of 17. I was a tutor from the 12th grade to the 2nd year of my BSc. I worked with over 60 students, from 5th to 12th grade, to help them achieve academic success. I was also into Marketing, and started to manage social media for a few organizations (including the baseball team I played for almost 9 years). My goal was to get a grasp for the fundamentals of building a small business and being able to grow it. Along the way, many mistakes were made, but it’s part of the game. If you come back to those same mistakes, that’s where it gets bad for you, because you’re simply not learning from them.</p><p>Every founder has a moment that triggers action. For many students, it’s the realization that university is more than lectures and exams, but a playground for ideas. The environment exposes us to diverse people, multidisciplinary thinking and problems just asking to be solved. Sometimes the spark comes from frustration, other times, from curiosity. What matters is the decision to build, rather than wait.</p><h3>Junior Enterprises: The Training Grounds for Tomorrow’s Leaders</h3><p>During the 2nd year of my BSc and before building SafetyScope, I joined a Junior Enterprise named In-Nova, an organization run entirely by university students. The core business of In-Nova is IT Consulting, where we developed websites, full-stack applications and performed robotics projects. It was in In-Nova where I got to build digital products for the first time.</p><p>Although it’s not directly the same as founding a startup, Junior Enterprises act as a sandbox for experimentation. You learn to manage teams, deal with clients, must meet deadlines and experience leadership dynamics.</p><p>In my case, I was a Projects Department Member, developing digital products, then became a Project Manager, managing teams to deliver projects to our clients, and then became Director of that same department, managing around 40 students. This type of experience with this level of experimentation isn’t easily available, so if you’re a student and read about an opportunity like this, grab it.</p><p>Currently, there are 27 junior enterprises in Portugal, engaged in a federation called Junior Enterprises Portugal, with over 1400 junior entrepreneurs generating a turnover over 600 thousand euros. This is a global movement. JE Portugal is part of JE Europe and JE Global, the latter with over 35 million USD in turnover with 23 thousand annual projects.</p><p>While most Junior Enterprises operate in consulting (IT, business, marketing, etc.), they’re valuable because they expose students to structured problem-solving and real-world responsibility early. Importantly, it gives you a taste of entrepreneurship. But grit, the relentless resilience required to be a founder, is largely intrinsic. The JE amplifies it, but it rarely creates it from scratch.</p><h3>What Junior Enterprises <em>Can</em> Teach About Founding</h3><p>When you’re a 1st time founder and currently studying, in your earliest stages you have to prove why you and your team are the best to solve a specific pain and explain why people should join you for the long term. Although we have incredible energy to move forward, we’re still very inexperienced in many ways. We should start from somewhere though.</p><p>JEs are not startups, but they instill professionalism, accountability, teamwork under pressure, client communication and product delivery mindset. These experiences reduce the shock of founding a company. When challenges appear, you respond with confidence because you’ve already tasted responsibility.</p><p>Still, the leap from JE to founder requires internal drive: persevering when no professor, manager or client holds you accountable, only your vision does.</p><h3>How SafetyScope was Born</h3><p>NOVA FCT has an Executive Education Program. Since my 1st year of the BSc I was eyeballing a course in Artificial Intelligence powered by Samsung Innovation Campus. I already knew Lucas (Co-Founder &amp; CTO at SafetyScope) from my BSc and we decided to sign up for the course in our 2nd year. We were accepted and started what for us were the 5 longest months until the end. We were still studying in our main degree, Computer Science and Engineering.</p><p>After presenting our final project (a Machine Learning Approach to Detect Physical Violence in Video), me, Lucas and Francisco (former Co-Founder of SafetyScope) were faced with the question “What now?”. We still had a long way into our degrees, but it felt too good to just end the project there. That’s where SafetyScope was born.</p><h3>The Hardest Challenges No One Warns You About</h3><p>Once you’re in, the only way to go is forward. No one really prepares you for what it means to be fully immersed in building something from scratch, no matter your current situation.</p><p>What most people don’t tell you is that being a founder rewires you. Some things aren’t to be said, but felt and learned. Being a founder changes your tolerance for uncertainty. You stop expecting structure and instead begin creating it. You stop waiting for permission and you start moving even when things feel incomplete. You’re constantly thinking about the next step, the next risk, the next challenge.</p><p>When things go wrong, you’re not just failing a test, you’re failing something you built, something that carries a piece of who you are. Yet, paradoxically, it’s exactly in those moments that you grow the most.</p><p>Being a university founder requires navigating three fronts simultaneously:</p><ul><li><p>Academic pressure: Your assignments don’t pause just because you’re building.</p></li><li><p>Time management: Every hour spent on your startup is an hour not spent studying, or resting.</p></li><li><p>Mental resilience: Friends and family may not fully understand why you choose difficulty over comfort. Professors might not know how to support students who are building companies instead of simply consuming knowledge.</p></li></ul><p>I’m truly lucky to be surrounded by people who understand and support us along the way.</p><h3>The Grit Factor: The Personal Attribute No Curriculum Can Teach</h3><p>At the core of entrepreneurship lies grit, the ability to keep pushing when everything suggests giving up. No course teaches it. No textbook captures it.</p><p>Being a student founder tests stamina (physically and psychologically), courage to take non-traditional career steps, humility when learning from failure and adaptability as everything changes weekly, or daily.</p><p>Beneath it all, most founders, though it’s rarely spoken out loud, carry a chip on their shoulder: a quiet need to prove something, either to themselves, their peers or to the world. It’s that inner tension that fuels the refusal to settle for just “good enough”.</p><p>Grit is about moving forward despite feeling doubtful and uncertain on how things might look up for the future. Every founder learns the hard way.</p><h3>Support Systems That Matter (And Those We Still Need)</h3><p>Along the way, I received help from mentors, entrepreneurial centers and networks. The most impactful support often came from events that connect students with founders and incubators willing to take risks on young talent like Madan Parque.</p><p>However, universities could do more:</p><ul><li><p>Introduce an entrepreneurship program or experience in each degree.</p></li><li><p>Recognize startup work as academic credits.</p></li><li><p>Offer legal/accounting/marketing support offices.</p></li><li><p>Encourage cross-faculty collaboration.</p></li></ul><p>I’m happy to be part of a university that is already taking real steps toward many of the points I’ve just mentioned. NOVA FCT hosts one of the largest Entrepreneurship Programs in Europe for students, and other NOVA campuses are also evolving, whether through dedicated degrees or core initiatives led by the NOVA Impact Office and the Haddad Entrepreneurship Institute. Each campus also has its own office focused on intellectual property and knowledge transfer, ensuring that research and innovation can move beyond academic walls and into the real world.</p><p>NOVA University has the largest number of Junior Enterprises in the country, with In-Nova (NOVA FCT), Junior Data Consulting (NOVA IMS), NOWACE (NOVA Medical School), and NOVA Junior Consulting (NOVA SBE). It also has incredible student-led entrepreneurship clubs such as START Lisbon (although independent, it’s led by many NOVA students), NOVAe and NOVA Startup Club, all of which play a vital role in introducing the entrepreneurial mindset across the university community.</p><p>This just shows that opportunities are everywhere, making the student-founder pipeline look significantly less intimidating.</p><h3>Why Start Now?</h3><p>There is no better moment than during university to build.</p><p>You are surrounded by brilliant peers. You get to challenge assumptions together with people that come from fields far outside your own. You can walk into a coffee break and walk out with a potential co-founder, a designer or your first beta tester.</p><p>Your learning curve is steep. Every mistake becomes a crash course in leadership, communication or self-discipline. You’re constantly forced to learn outside your academic comfort zone.</p><p>Your network grows faster than ever. Universities are fertile ground for serendipity: professors with industry connections, alumni eager to mentor, accelerators hunting for new talent.</p><p>But perhaps most importantly, starting now teaches you that building is learning. Every setback, every prototype, every conversation becomes part of your education.</p><p>The worst-case scenario? You learn skills 90% of students never touch. The best case? You create something truly meaningful.</p><p>So if you have an idea, don’t wait for the perfect moment. It doesn’t exist. Start where you are, with what you have. Because university isn’t just a place to study, it’s a place to start.</p><p>The best time to plant a tree was 20 years ago. The second best time is now.</p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Emotional and cultural impact | Week 39</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/emotional-and-cultural-impact-week-39</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/emotional-and-cultural-impact-week-39</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 14 Nov 2025 11:30:42 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>I return from this week with a reinforced conviction: the local ecosystem matters. Deeply. It’s where we start, test, fail, and build the resilience needed to reach bigger stages. It’s where founders learn to pitch without slides, build without sleep, and dream without limits. And it’s where global…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>I return from this week with a reinforced conviction: the local ecosystem matters. Deeply. </p><p>It’s where we start, test, fail, and build the resilience needed to reach bigger stages. It’s where founders learn to pitch without slides, build without sleep, and dream without limits. And it’s where global ambition is born; not in isolation, but in community. That’s why initiatives like Portugal Tech Week and Web Summit matter. They’re not just events, they’re bridges; Between local and global, Between early and late stage, Between what we’ve built, and what we’re building next.</p><p><strong>Infrastructure, capital, talent, &amp; policy</strong>. These four elements are the structural beams of any serious tech ecosystem and Portugal is aligning the pieces.</p><ul><li><p>the announcement of Microsoft’s 10B investment in AI infrastructure is more than a headline, it’s a signal that Portugal is ready to host the next wave of compute heavy, data driven innovation. Add to that the growing network of innovation hubs, coworking spaces, and university linked incubators, and you have a country that’s it’s building the roads.</p></li><li><p>venture landscape is maturing, local funds are growing in sophistication and size, and international investors are no longer just flying in for Web Summit, they’re staying, investing, and co-building. The conversation is shifting from not only “how do we raise?” to “how do we scale?” Portugal is proving it can generate returns and ambition.</p></li><li><p>Portugal has been positioning like a magnet for global talent. The TISRI regime,with its 20% flat tax and 10-year foreign income exemption is a game-changer for attracting founders, operators, and remote workers. But beyond incentives, there’s a cultural shift: young people are choosing entrepreneurship earlier, universities are embracing startup culture (see Luis Lamy's article on Adamastor), and the diaspora is starting to look homeward with fresh eyes (initiatives like Outono are helping).</p></li><li><p>and Policy. It's evolving from passive support to active enablement. From startup visas to tax reform, from digital nomad frameworks to public-private partnerships, there’s a growing recognition that innovation needs air to breathe, and that regulation can be a catalyst, not just a constraint. The government’s role is evolving from gatekeeper to enabler, and I'm quite confident that entities like 'Secretaria de Estado da Digitalização' will play a key role in this next chapter.</p><p> </p></li></ul><p>Where there’s consistent startup activity, talent and capital follow. And that cycle seems to be gaining momentum here in Portugal.</p><p><strong>Talent follows opportunity. Capital follows talent. Ecosystems follow belief. </strong>And belief? We've got plenty of that.</p><p>My last notes for this week:</p><p><strong>Granter’s win at Pitch 2025</strong> — out of 2,725 startups — is a testament to the strength and creativity emerging from our ecosystem. It’s not just about visibility; it’s about validation.</p><p><strong>Web Summit’s future in Portugal matters.</strong> The current agreement runs until 2028, but the conversation about what comes next should start now. The event is more than a big stage, it’s a window into the future and a source of inspiration for thousands. It’s a magnet for talent, capital, and ideas. And it’s a chance for Portugal to keep showing the world what we’re capable of. Ten years in, and the spark hasn’t faded. If anything, it’s burning brighter. Let’s make sure it stays!</p><p></p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a> </p><p></p><h1>✍ Quote of the week</h1><blockquote><p>"If you're not prepared to be wrong, you'll never come up with anything original"</p><p><em>Ken Robinson</em></p></blockquote><h1></h1><h1>Highlights of the week</h1><p>🔷 <strong>Deep-tech startups </strong> this one’s for you! The EIC Pre-Accelerator is open. If your innovation is lab-validated (TRL 4+) and you’re ready to scale, don’t miss this chance to boost your journey. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://eic.ec.europa.eu/eic-funding-opportunities/eic-pre-accelerator_en">Apply by 18 Nov</a> </p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/movember-pth">Movembering Porto Tech Hub</a> happening on different locations in Porto</p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://launchpad.drivenvb.pt/">Launchpad</a> Ignition program Apply by Nov 21</p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://point-and.involve.me/better-mobility-for-eurovision">European Call for Mobility &amp; Tourism Innovations</a>, apply until Nov 23</p><p>🔷 Responsible AI Forum 2025 | <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eventbrite.pt/e/responsible-ai-forum-2025-demo-day-tickets-1968220463389">Demo Day </a>(Nov 25) by Center for Responsible AI </p><p>🔷 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://forms.office.com/pages/responsepage.aspx">CyberIgnite</a>: Workshop de Aceleração @ BSides Porto next Nov 28 &amp; 29</p><p>🔷 <strong>Protechting</strong> open innovation program is looking for Startups in Insurtech, Healthtech, Tech, and Sustainability. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.protechting.com/">Apply until</a> Dec 05</p><p>🔷 <strong>Discoveries</strong>, the acceleration program that helps tourism startups grow, connect and go global powered by Fabrica de Startups <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.startupdiscoveries.com/">is now open</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>Copenhagen</strong>’s new AI-first hackathon <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/zmho1iqy">is accepting applications</a> </p><p> </p><h1>Congrats</h1><p>👏 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://STUDIOS.PT"><strong>STUDIOS.PT</strong></a> – Portuguese Venture Studio Association was official launched </p><p>👏 <strong>Microsoft</strong> announced 10B investment in Sines</p><p>👏 <strong>WindCredible</strong> won Global Pitch Sprint @Startup Portugal stand </p><p>👏 Portugal’s <strong>Granter</strong> secured the top spot at Web Summit 2025’s PITCH competition</p><p>👏 <strong>Lampsy </strong>won the UniVerse Pitch Competition</p><p>👏 <strong>FlamAid </strong>lança aplicação gratuita durante a Web Summit</p><p>👏 <strong>Galaxies </strong>won Electrico Pitch</p><p>👏 <strong>Cíntia Mano</strong> won the Golden Aurora Award 2025</p><p>👏 <strong>Health Hub </strong>was officially launched in Lisbon   </p><p></p><h1>Something to read, listen and watch</h1><p>📚AI funding assistant Granter wins <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://websummit.com/blog/news/ai-funding-assistant-granter-wins-web-summit-2025-pitch/">Web Summit 2025 PITCH</a></p><p>📚Startup SafetyScope usa IA e visão por computador para <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://dinheirovivo.dn.pt/brand-story/startup-safetyscope-usa-ia-e-viso-por-computador-para-tornar-videovigilncia-mais-eficiente">tornar videovigilância mais eficiente</a></p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupportugal.com/startup-entrepreneurial-ecosystem-report-2025/">Startup &amp; Entrepreneurial Ecosystem Report </a>2025</p><p>📚Community for educational innovation - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/f5dcff17-bac5-11f0-b37f-01aa75ed71a1/language-en">Entrepreneurial skills and mindsets in education</a></p><p>📚Startup Go to Market Strategy: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.pmf.show/blog/startup-go-to-market-strategy-how-to-build-a-category-creating-company-from-zero-real-case-study/">How to Build a Category-Creating Company</a> From Zero (Real Case Study)</p><p>🎧&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/2jOJJg2EYGZwRhytWtLOeD?si=ecf5ece895514926">Fundadores</a>: a trajetória de Belmiro de Azevedo by Vitor Soares</p><p>🎥&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TZMavDMKOfc">Electrico Pitch</a> by Portugal Tech Week (12 pitches)</p><p>🎥&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://summit.co/videos/films-about-summit/leading-through-disruption-how-onlyfans-is-changing-the-internet-with-keily-blair-4fiDGqruCoVBf7K9WO4eN3">Leading Through Disruption</a>: How OnlyFans is Changing the Internet with Keily Blair</p><p>🎥&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/S6yTvvAp0Do?si=YOFd9xXm01KVwP4A">Celebrating with People</a> Choice Rita Kastrati - doing the double by Canopy Community</p><p>💡Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Where the tech world meets | Week 38</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/where-the-tech-world-meets-week-38</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/where-the-tech-world-meets-week-38</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 03 Nov 2025 16:25:52 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>&quot;The best way to predict the future is to invent it&quot;. The quote I selected for this week resonates perfectly with the spirit of Web Summit, where innovation shapes the future of technology and ideas. The Web Summit is right around the corner!! There are a few days for the event that puts all eyes…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>"The best way to predict the future is to invent it". The quote I selected for this week resonates perfectly with the spirit of Web Summit, where innovation shapes the future of technology and ideas. The Web Summit is right around the corner!! There are a few days for the event that puts all eyes on entrepreneurship in Lisbon!</p><p>There is a fantastic selection of events around Web Summit, if you want to connect with the local ecosystem at the Web Summit, you must be part of it. For the Web Summit schedule <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://websummit.com/schedule/">take a look here</a> and side events <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://innovationscene.pt/websummit/events/">here</a></p><p>Similarly, anyone looking to explore Portugal's tech landscape can access a full lineup of Portugal Tech Week events<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://portugaltechweek.com/"> here</a>.</p><p>Our highlights for the following days:</p><p>-<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://lisbonaiweek.com/"> Lisbon AI Week</a> (Nov 1-9): Lisbon has a strong and active community of developers, startups, companies and VCs working on new and exciting AI initiatives. The team of volunteers behind the Lisbon AI Week felt the need to assemble them in a week where we all ideas are welcome, access is democratized, and bridges are built with talent and companies from abroad.</p><p>- <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://algarvesummit.com/">Algarve Tech Hub Summit</a> (Nov 6–7, Lagos): A two-day celebration of innovation across tourism, agrofood, health, energy, and digital culture. The Algarve positions itself as a global tech hub, and it’s not just talk.</p><p>- <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://portugaltechweek.com/">Portugal Tech Week</a> (Nov 7–16): 300+ free events across 20 cities, including Lisbon’s Tech Run, the one and only <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://portugaltechweek.com/eletrico-pitch/">Electrico Pitch</a>, and workshops on AI, Web3, and sustainability. It’s not a conference, it’s a movement.</p><p>- <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://websummit.com/schedule/">Web Summit Lisbon</a> (Nov 10–13): The heavyweight. 70,000+ attendees, 800+ speakers, and the world’s tech elite descending on Altice Arena. If you’re building, investing, or dreaming, this is your arena.</p><p>- <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupportugal.com/pt/">Innovation Tracks</a> (Nov 10): join Startup Portugal and Lisboa's team for an exciting morning designed to ignite inspiration and collaboration. Startups can choose to visit one out of five dynamic hubs focusing on Fintech, Green Technology, Gaming, and AI sectors, gaining valuable insights and engaging with investors, public entities, startups, and founders. Listen to testimonials from startups across various sectors, showcasing their journeys and innovations. Register <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eventbrite.com/cc/innovation-tracks-2025-4757893">here</a></p><p>- <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://startupportugal.com/pt/">Welcome to the Global Stage</a>: Lisboa and Portugal (Nov 10): flagship event will gather over 500 participants, creating a unique platform that connects Portuguese institutions with the international innovation community. Join us for an in-depth exploration of how Portugal and Lisbon are emerging as global innovation hubs. Gain insights from leading policymakers, ecosystem builders, and international investors as they discuss how Web Summit drives collaboration, growth, and opportunity across borders. Register <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.eventbrite.pt/e/welcome-to-the-global-stage-lisboa-and-portugal-tickets-1857633414549">here</a></p><p>- <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/gm4igntt">Web Summit Tech Fado Dinner</a> (Nov 12): connect with brilliant Tech minds while immersing yourself in the magic of Fado, Portugal’s soulful singing. 10€ discount for the community with the code TECHFADISTA</p><p>- <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.canopy.community/websummit-2025-showcase">DemoNightLx</a> (Nov 12): Canopy Community<span style="color: rgb(89, 89, 89);"> hosts </span><em>DemoNightLx</em><span style="color: rgb(89, 89, 89);">, signature showcase for early-stage founders. Expect energy, ideas, and inspiration as brilliant startups&nbsp; demo live and you get an opportunity to ask your questions</span></p><p>- <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://swordhealth.com/">Sword AI Summit</a> (Nov 15): from responsible AI to human-machine collaboration; all the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://aisummit.swordhealth.com/#agenda">agenda here</a> </p><p>To make the most of Web Summit, follow this simple yet powerful tip: bring a pair of comfortable shoes 👟, a fully charged phone 📱, a water bottle 💧, and something to take notes 📝</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a> , Adamastor will return on Nov 17.</p><p></p><h1>✍ Quote of the week</h1><blockquote><p>The best way to predict the future is to invent it</p><p>Alan Kay</p></blockquote><p></p><p>🔷 <strong>Tech Run</strong> (Nov 09) Get ready to run through Lisbon’s innovation district! From the iconic Unicorn Factory Lisboa to Parque das Nações. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://techrun.live/lisbon/">All the info here</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>Startup Guide Europe</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://summit.startupguide.com/">Launch</a> @ <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.tickettailor.com/events/startupguideworldaps/1865971">Startup Guide Summit 2025</a> Nov 09 at Casa do Impacto</p><p>🔷 <strong>Deep-tech startups </strong> this one’s for you! The EIC Pre-Accelerator is open. If your innovation is lab-validated (TRL 4+) and you’re ready to scale, don’t miss this chance to boost your journey. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://eic.ec.europa.eu/eic-funding-opportunities/eic-pre-accelerator_en">Apply by 18 Nov</a> </p><p>🔷 <strong>Protechting</strong> open innovation program is looking for Startups in Insurtech, Healthtech, Tech, and Sustainability. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.protechting.com/">Apply until</a> Dec 05</p><p>🔷 <strong>Discoveries</strong>, the acceleration program that helps tourism startups grow, connect and go global powered by Fabrica de Startups <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.startupdiscoveries.com/">is now open</a></p><p></p><p></p><h1>Congrats</h1><p>👏  Coworking <strong>Spaces Matosinhos</strong> to open this week</p><p> </p><h1>Something to read, listen and watch</h1><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://report.portugalfintech.org/2025">Portugal Fintech Report </a>2025</p><p>📚&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em><u>What&nbsp;will&nbsp;the&nbsp;future&nbsp;jobs&nbsp;be,&nbsp;and&nbsp;how&nbsp;can&nbsp;regions&nbsp;like&nbsp;the&nbsp;Algarve&nbsp;create&nbsp;them</u></em></strong>?&nbsp;by&nbsp;Miguel&nbsp;Fernandes</p><p>🎧&nbsp;Andre&nbsp;Marquet&nbsp;talk&nbsp;w/&nbsp;Blagoja&nbsp;Golubovski,&nbsp;VP&nbsp;of&nbsp;Product&nbsp;at&nbsp;UserCentrics,&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/5RpbBcyyyfmSrTO6B0TJqK?si=tugcTej0Swe60PUM4b7tFw"><strong><em><u>about&nbsp;what&nbsp;it&nbsp;really&nbsp;means&nbsp;to&nbsp;lead&nbsp;product&nbsp;with&nbsp;clarity,&nbsp;courage,&nbsp;and&nbsp;alignment</u></em></strong></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/19SMW5vhDIqPdXjWSvmNN2?si=BVAE0BwlRS-F5yNq_beoGA"><u>&nbsp;</u></a></p><p>🎥&nbsp;<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/jhWNdKUjwZU?si=enY-N-Mv2udOEgCP"><strong><em><u>SafetyScope:&nbsp;Humanos&nbsp;vs.&nbsp;máquinas</u></em></strong></a>!&nbsp;A&nbsp;Inteligência&nbsp;artificial&nbsp;revoluciona&nbsp;videovigilância.&nbsp;by&nbsp;Inovadores</p><p>💡Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>What will the future jobs be, and how can regions like the Algarve create them?</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/what-will-the-future-jobs-be-and-how-can-regions-like-the-algarve-create-them</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/what-will-the-future-jobs-be-and-how-can-regions-like-the-algarve-create-them</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 31 Oct 2025 12:18:30 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Miguel (Rocha) Fernandes</dc:creator>
      <description>An open call to design the future of work, together. Asking the Right Question What will people do when machines can do almost everything? It’s the question that keeps many of us(at least me…) awake at night,&amp;nbsp; not just as entrepreneurs or policymakers, but as parents, teammates, and citizens…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span><em>An open call to design the future of work, together.</em></span></p><h2><span><strong>Asking the Right Question</strong></span></h2><h3><span><strong><em>What will people do when machines can do almost everything?</em></strong></span></h3><p><span>It’s the question that keeps many of us(at least me…) awake at night,&nbsp; not just as entrepreneurs or policymakers, but as parents, teammates, and citizens trying to make sense of what’s coming next.</span></p><p><span>Artificial intelligence and robotics are transforming work faster than any industrial revolution before. Cars are learning to drive themselves. Humanoid Robots are stepping into hospitals and factories. Algorithms are now writing, designing, and creating products that once depended entirely on human imagination.</span></p><p><span>So the real question isn’t whether this will change jobs(it will), it’s how smaller regions like ours can adapt, respond, and build new ones.</span></p><p><span>For the Algarve, and for Portugal as a whole, this is about more than economics. It’s about purpose, courage, and identity. How does a region known for its beauty and hospitality turn that same creativity into innovation? How can we keep our brightest minds here, attract new ones, and build a future that goes beyond seasonal work?</span></p><p><span>No one has all the answers. What matters now is starting the right conversation… openly, collaboratively, and with the humility to learn together.</span></p><h3><span><strong>The Coming Disruption</strong></span></h3><p><span>The scale of what’s unfolding is hard to grasp. Over the next decade, millions of roles will shift. Some will disappear. Others, entirely new ones, will take their place.</span></p><p><span>Even jobs once seen as “future-proof” are being redefined. Take software development. For years it was the safest career path imaginable. But today, entry-level coders are struggling to keep pace with AI-augmented senior engineers who can deliver in days what once took teams weeks.</span></p><p><span>This isn’t a collapse. It’s a shift. And if it’s happening in one of the most complex, cognitive fields, it will spread quickly to every other.</span></p><p><span>At the same time, new types of work are emerging,&nbsp; jobs that mix human judgment, creativity, and systems thinking with machine intelligence.</span></p><h3><strong>1. Hospitality &amp; Tourism 2.0 – Future Roles</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>Experience Curator (2025–2030 · High Impact)<br></strong>Designs tech-enhanced, authentic travel experiences.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI Hospitality Manager (2025–2030 · High Impact)<br></strong>Manages robot- and AI-assisted guest services.</p></li><li><p><strong>Sustainability Host (2025–2030 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Leads eco-certification and circular practices in resorts.</p></li><li><p><strong>Cultural Mediator / Heritage Interpreter (2028–2035 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Uses AR/VR to bring local culture and heritage to visitors.</p></li><li><p><strong>Robot Operations Assistant (2030–2040 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Maintains service robots across hotels and attractions.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>2. Care, Health &amp; Wellbeing – Future Roles</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>Elder Companion / Assisted Living Coordinator (2025–2030 · High Impact)<br></strong>Combines empathy with AI monitoring to support an aging population.</p></li><li><p><strong>Health &amp; Wellness Coach (2025–2035 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Uses wearable and app data to guide healthier lifestyles.</p></li><li><p><strong>Community Health Navigator (2028–2035 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Connects citizens with digital healthcare systems.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI-Assisted Caregiver (2028–2035 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Works alongside assistive robots in clinics and homes.</p></li><li><p><strong>Mental Health Facilitator (2030–2040 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Combines human counseling with AI-supported therapy tools.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>3. Education &amp; Human Development – Future Roles</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>AI-Assisted Teacher / Learning Facilitator (2025–2030 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Blends digital tutors with personal, emotional teaching.</p></li><li><p><strong>Vocational Mentor / Lifelong Learning Coach (2025–2035 · High Impact)<br></strong>Supports adults to reskill as technology evolves.</p></li><li><p><strong>Community Maker Instructor (2028–2035 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Teaches practical creation and repair skills (3D printing, crafts).</p></li><li><p><strong>Learning Experience Designer (2030–2040 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Builds hybrid learning paths combining human and AI mentorship.</p></li><li><p><strong>Educational Data Analyst (2035–2045 · Low Impact)<br></strong>Monitors learning systems and personalizes education.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>4. Community, Culture &amp; Sustainability – Future Roles</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>Green Space Steward / Urban Ranger (2025–2030 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Maintains natural and coastal areas using drones and sensors.</p></li><li><p><strong>Smart City Facility Manager (2028–2035 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Oversees energy, waste, and mobility systems integrated with IoT.</p></li><li><p><strong>Coastal Resilience Coordinator (2030–2040 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Leads adaptation projects protecting beaches and towns.</p></li><li><p><strong>Community Coordinator / Neighborhood Liaison (2025–2035 · High Impact)<br></strong>Strengthens inclusion between citizens, services, and governance.</p></li><li><p><strong>Ethical Mediator (2035–2045 · Low Impact)<br></strong>Balances innovation with community well-being and fairness.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>5. Technology, Robotics &amp; Skilled Trades – Future Roles</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>Conversational &amp; Agentic Experience Designer (CXD/AXD) (2025–2030 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Designs and manages how humans interact with AI agents, robots, and intelligent systems.</p></li><li><p><strong>Robotics Technician (2025–2030 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Maintains and adapts humanoid and service robots across industries.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI Supervisor (2025–2035 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Oversees automated systems and ensures safe, ethical human–AI collaboration.</p></li><li><p><strong>Data Curator (2028–2035 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Cleans and organizes the data AI systems rely on.</p></li><li><p><strong>Smart Plumber / Electrician (2025–2045 · High Impact)<br></strong>Installs and maintains connected systems in smart buildings.</p></li><li><p><strong>Construction Robotics Operator (2028–2040 · Medium Impact)<br></strong>Uses semi-autonomous machinery and drones for precision construction.</p></li></ul><p>These new professionals don’t build interfaces. They design interactions, curating conversations between humans and intelligent systems, guiding AI behavior, and orchestrating networks of digital agents that can act and think alongside us.</p><p><span>And these skills aren’t being taught in traditional classrooms. They’re being learned by doing, through R&amp;D, experimentation, and creative play.</span></p><p><span>That’s the lesson for regions like ours: those who experiment first, discover the new jobs first.</span></p><h2><span><strong>Why the Algarve Must Act, and 5 suggestions for the future</strong></span></h2><p><span>The Algarve lives in a unique balance between privilege and pressure. We have incredible quality of life, access to international talent, and a solid university network. Yet many of our most talented young people still leave.</span></p><p><span>AI and robotics can either make that problem worse or help us turn it around. If we wait, our seasonal jobs will slowly be automated and managed from elsewhere. But if we move now, we can create new industries rooted in our creativity, empathy, and technical skill.</span></p><p><span>The Algarve doesn’t need to compete on size. We can compete on agility. On collaboration. On the power of being a living lab, a place where tourism, technology, science, and education meet to explore how humans and machines can work better together.</span></p><p><span>This transformation has already begun. The Algarve Tech Hub is bringing together entrepreneurs, researchers, and public and private partners around a shared mission: to make the region a magnet for innovation and a birthplace of meaningful jobs for future generations.</span></p><p><span>And, as <u>Adamastor.blog</u> reminds us, Portugal’s journey has always involved facing our own fears, and turning them into fuel for discovery. The mythic Adamastor once symbolized the great unknown that Portuguese navigators feared beyond the Cape of Storms. But it was only through science, specialization, and courage that we found a way around it and reached new worlds.</span></p><p><span><strong>Today, our “Adamastor” isn’t the ocean… It's the challenge of building a more diverse economy with innovative companies and future-ready jobs</strong>. The challenge is the same: to look at the storm, not with fear, but with focus and innovation. The future will belong to those who, dare to learn fast, work together, and keep sailing forward.</span></p><h3><span><strong>1 - The Algarve Innovation Lab: Learning by Building</strong></span></h3><p><span>To prepare people for these new jobs, education and industry must move closer together.</span></p><p><span>The Algarve Innovation Lab is a framework to make that happen. It’s not a new school or building. It’s a shared platform that aligns the University of the Algarve, technical schools, private academies, and companies around one mission: learning by building.</span></p><p><span>Students and researchers work directly with businesses on real-world challenges, designing a marine robot, building an AI hospitality system, or developing predictive health tools.</span></p><p><span>This turns education into co-creation and classrooms into living labs, where research, business, and innovation meet in practice, not just in theory.</span></p><p><span>This approach must start early. We need to bring <strong>STEAM(E) education</strong> (science, tech, engineering, arts, math and ENTREPRENEURSHIP<strong>)</strong> into public schools so that creativity, problem-solving, and teamwork become second nature.</span></p><p>Alongside this, <strong>venture studios</strong> can play a key role — acting as turnkey company builders that transform ideas and research into startups ready to scale. This model, now being promoted through <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="http://Studios.pt">Studios.pt</a>, gives structure and speed to innovation, turning learning into ventures and ventures into real jobs for the region. Studios.pt will <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://luma.com/g3xa4jq1">officially launch soon</a>, aiming to support regional innovation through this structured approach.</p><p><span>And we need to <strong>change the cultural mindset</strong>: in Portugal/Europe, creating new companies must be seen as <strong>something exciting and respected</strong>. Without that, we’ll never grow the next generation of bold innovators.</span></p><p><span><strong>To create future jobs, education and industry must work as one.</strong></span></p><p><span>References: </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://algarvetechhub.com/"><span><u>Algarvetechhub.com</u></span></a><span> , </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://studios.pt/">Studios.pt , </a><span><u>Wizpress.io</u> , </span><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.museu0.pt/en/"><span><u>museu0.pt</u></span></a></p><h2><span><strong>2 - The Knowledge Layer: Building the Foundation</strong></span></h2><p><span>Every sector, tourism, health, the ocean economy, depends on one thing: <strong>knowledge.</strong></span></p><p><span>The Algarve needs a <strong>Knowledge Layer</strong>: a connected network of developers, researchers, and experts in AI, data, and robotics who support all sectors. It’s not another institution, it’s a shared capability that links universities, private labs, and entrepreneurs to apply advanced technology locally.</span></p><p><span>In the short term, we’ll attract <strong>remote workers, digital nomads, and global experts</strong> already living here , connected to the region and new ones. Through the<strong> Algarve Evolution</strong> network, many are already collaborating to bring world-class experience/investment into local projects.</span></p><p><span>In the long term, the <strong>Algarve Innovation Lab</strong> will train a new generation of experts locally, turning this knowledge layer into a self-sustaining ecosystem of talent and innovation.</span></p><p><span>Small regions don’t win by scale. They win by <strong>connection, collaboration, and trust.</strong></span></p><p><span>References: <u>AlgarveEvolution.pt</u> ,<u>ualg.pt</u>, <u>ccmar.ualg.pt</u></span></p><h3><span><strong>3 - Hospitality 2050: Reinventing Our Core Industry</strong></span></h3><p><span>Tourism will always be the heart of the Algarve, but it can also be our testbed for innovation.</span></p><p><span>Imagine hotels where humanoid robots manage check-ins, deliveries, and maintenance while human hosts focus on storytelling, empathy, and local culture. Picture AI omni-channel concierges that anticipate guests’ needs before they arrive, guided by creative professionals who design experiences with intention and care.</span></p><p><span>These aren’t distant ideas. They’re the next generation of roles:</span></p><ul><li><p><span>Customer experience designers</span></p></li><li><p><span>AI hospitality managers</span></p></li><li><p><span>Data experience curators</span></p></li><li><p><span>Robotic operations leads</span></p></li></ul><p><span>A Smart Hospitality Network could unite hotels, universities, and startups to test and refine these ideas.</span></p><p><span>This isn’t about replacing people. It’s about creating better jobs, ones that celebrate what humans do best: connect, create, and care.</span></p><p><span>References: <u>https://kipt.pt/</u>, <u>svaito.com</u>, <u>TieSports.com</u></span></p><h3><span><strong>4 - Health Tech: Aging, Care, and Collaboration</strong></span></h3><p><span>Portugal’s aging population is one of its greatest challenges, but also one of its biggest opportunities.</span></p><p><span>AI can already detect diseases early, manage chronic conditions remotely, and support doctors in diagnosis. But technology alone isn’t enough. Care will always need empathy. Machines can assist, but they can’t comfort.</span></p><p><span>The Algarve is perfectly positioned to pioneer AI-assisted care models, training health professionals to use these tools responsibly and effectively. With the new central hospital and medical university as anchors, we could develop pilot programs in telehealth, rehabilitation robotics, and predictive medicine.</span></p><p><span>A Health Innovation Program, connecting hospitals, research teams, and startups, would not only improve quality of care, it would create high-value jobs and a stronger local ecosystem.</span></p><p><span>References: <u>https://algarvebiomedicalcenter.pt/</u>, <u>ExpressTec.pt</u>, <u>sea4us.pt</u></span></p><h3><span><strong>5 - Blue Economy: From Fishermen to Ocean Technologists</strong></span></h3><p><span>The sea has always defined the Algarve. Now it can define our next chapter.</span></p><p><span>Marine robotics, sustainable aquaculture, and ocean data are emerging as billion-euro industries. The Algarve has the geography, talent, and research base to lead them.</span></p><p><span>Imagine fleets of autonomous vessels monitoring ocean health or maintaining offshore energy platforms. Behind them are teams of marine robotics engineers, ocean data scientists, and AI sustainability analysts.</span></p><p><span>This is where tradition meets technology, where fishermen work side by side with data experts to protect livelihoods and ecosystems at the same time.</span></p><p><span>Reference: <u>https://www.culatra2030.pt/</u> , <u>sparos.pt</u>, <u>sea4us.pt</u>, <u>necton.pt</u></span></p><h2><span><strong>A Call for Courage and Collaboration</strong></span></h2><p><span>Portugal has always been a land of explorers. The challenge today isn’t to cross new oceans, but to navigate the unpredictable waters of technology.</span></p><p><span>The Algarve may be small, but that’s its strength. Small regions can move faster, adapt quicker, and learn by doing.</span></p><p><span>This transformation won’t be easy. It requires coordination, trust, and persistence. But if we get it right, we’ll create the kinds of jobs our children will thank us for, meaningful, creative, and future-ready.</span></p><p><span>Come see what’s unfolding in the Algarve. Join us in Lagos on <strong>6–7 November</strong> for <u>AlgarveSummit.com</u>.</span></p><p><span>The Summit brings together entrepreneurs, educators, policymakers, investors, and researchers from across Portugal and beyond. But it’s not another conference. It’s a working platform to turn ideas into strategy and strategy into action.</span></p><p><span>So, whether you’re a teacher, founder, student, or policymaker, this is your moment to join in and help design what comes next.</span></p><p><span>Let’s design the future of work, not someday, but now, together, where the land meets the sea.</span></p><p></p><hr><p></p><p><span><strong>Miguel Fernandes</strong></span></p><p><span>Founder CEO <u>Dengun.com</u> | Building an Agentic Conversational AI | Investor | Global Speaker | Startup Studio | Global Ecosystem Builder: <u>AlgarveEvolution.pt</u> / <u>AlgarveTechHub.com</u>&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title> The Power to Build: Portugal’s Startup Season | Week 37</title>
      <link>https://adamastor.blog/posts/the-power-to-build-portugal-s-startup-season-week-37</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://adamastor.blog/posts/the-power-to-build-portugal-s-startup-season-week-37</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 27 Oct 2025 10:09:14 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Carlos Resende</dc:creator>
      <description>Two weeks ago, the 2025 Nobel Prize in Economics was awarded to the groundbreaking research on innovation-driven economic growth. The work confirms what many founders already know: entrepreneurship isn’t a buzzword, it’s the engine of prosperity. Through the lens of creative destruction, they’ve…</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Two weeks ago, the 2025 Nobel Prize in Economics was awarded to the groundbreaking research on innovation-driven economic growth. The work confirms what many founders already know: entrepreneurship isn’t a buzzword, it’s the engine of prosperity. Through the lens of creative destruction, they’ve shown how new ideas, startups, and technologies fuel long-term progress.</p><p>Few months before, a new study made waves: “Nationwide Entrepreneurship Content in Secondary Schools: Impact on Entrepreneurial Careers.” The findings? When students are exposed to entrepreneurship early; not just as a concept, but as a mindset, they’re significantly more likely to launch ventures later in life. </p><p>These two findings; the Nobel Prize and the study on entrepreneurship education, are powerful reminders of how deeply entrepreneurship shapes economies. And they couldn’t have landed at a better time.</p><p>Last week, Lisbon lit up with one of the most meaningful moments of the year for Portugal’s startup ecosystem: the Entrepreneurship Awards 2025, hosted by Unicorn Factory Lisboa at the Técnico Innovation Center. Seven categories honored the builders, dreamers, and doers shaping our future, with the most wanted João Vasconcelos Award spotlighting the Entrepreneur of the Year. More than just a ceremony, it was a statement: Portugal is no longer emerging, it’s leading.</p><p>I had the pleasure of serving as a jury member, and I can tell you firsthand: the level of ambition, creativity, and execution on display was nothing short of world-class. As Gil Azevedo put it: “<em>The Entrepreneurship Awards celebrate the remarkable and inspiring work carried out by entrepreneurs, investors, and leaders in driving innovation in Portugal — a key force for economic growth. Lisbon and Portugal continue to establish themselves as one of Europe’s most important innovation hubs. The startup ecosystem has attracted talent, investment, and created qualified jobs, proving that innovation is now a transformative force for the country.</em>”.</p><p>But the energy doesn’t stop there. November is stacked with events that will keep the ecosystem buzzing:</p><p>-<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://lisbonaiweek.com/"> Lisbon AI Week</a> (Nov 1-9): Lisbon has a strong and active community of developers, startups, companies and VCs working on new and exciting AI initiatives. The team of volunteers behind the Lisbon AI Week felt the need to assemble them in a week where we all ideas are welcome, access is democratized, and bridges are built with talent and companies from abroad.</p><p>- <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://algarvesummit.com/">Algarve Tech Hub Summit</a> (Nov 6–7, Lagos): A two-day celebration of innovation across tourism, agrofood, health, energy, and digital culture. The Algarve positions itself as a global tech hub, and it’s not just talk.</p><p>- <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://portugaltechweek.com/">Portugal Tech Week</a> (Nov 7–16): 300+ free events across 20 cities, including Lisbon’s Tech Run, the one and only <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://portugaltechweek.com/eletrico-pitch/">Electrico Pitch</a>, and workshops on AI, Web3, and sustainability. It’s not a conference, it’s a movement.</p><p>- <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://websummit.com/schedule/">Web Summit Lisbon</a> (Nov 10–13): The heavyweight. 70,000+ attendees, 800+ speakers, and the world’s tech elite descending on Altice Arena. If you’re building, investing, or dreaming, this is your arena.</p><p>This is the season where Portugal shows up and shows off. Let’s make sure we’re not just attending, we’re participating!</p><p>Keep following <strong>Adamastor</strong> to stay up to date with our ecosystem.</p><p>See you<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"> at the next event</a></p><p>🔔 Founders, students, builders: this one's for you The applications for<strong> SantanderX</strong> 𝐏𝐨𝐫𝐭𝐮𝐠𝐚𝐥 𝐀𝐰𝐚𝐫𝐝𝐬 𝟐𝟎𝟐𝟓 are still open. Up to €30,000 in prizes. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://app.santanderx.com/workgroups/351-associaco-start-ups/64a6d8faf9d752f0ea3fb19f">Last day to apply</a></p><p></p><h1>✍ Quote of the week</h1><blockquote><p>Entrepreneurship Awards are about recognizing the courage to build, the resilience to grow, and the vision to transform Port<em>ugal into a global innovation hub.” </em></p><p><strong>Unicorn Factory Lisboa </strong></p></blockquote><p></p><p>🔷 <strong>Portugal Fintech Report 2025</strong> Official Launch Event next Nov 04</p><p>🔷 <strong>Startup Guide Europe</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://summit.startupguide.com/">Launch</a> @ <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.tickettailor.com/events/startupguideworldaps/1865971">Startup Guide Summit 2025</a> Nov 09 at Casa do Impacto .Send me a message to get the discount code</p><p>🔷 <strong>Deep-tech startups </strong> this one’s for you! The EIC Pre-Accelerator is open. If your innovation is lab-validated (TRL 4+) and you’re ready to scale, don’t miss this chance to boost your journey. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://eic.ec.europa.eu/eic-funding-opportunities/eic-pre-accelerator_en">Apply by 18 Nov</a> </p><p>🔷 <strong>Lisbon AI week</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://lisbonaiweek.com/">Applications are now open</a> </p><p>🔷 <strong>Santander X Portugal Awards</strong> - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://app.santanderx.com/workgroups/351-associaco-start-ups/64a6d8faf9d752f0ea3fb19f">submissions for both categories; university &amp; startups</a> </p><p>🔷 <strong>NDC Porto</strong>: 5-Day Workshop Event for Software Developers <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://ndcporto.com/">happening this week</a>  We still have exclusive discounts available for our community, send me an email</p><p>🔷 <strong>Tech Run</strong> (Nov 09) Get ready to run through Lisbon’s innovation district! From the iconic Unicorn Factory Lisboa to Parque das Nações. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://techrun.live/lisbon/">All the info here</a></p><p>🔷 <strong>Protechting</strong> open innovation program is looking for Startups in Insurtech, Healthtech, Tech, and Sustainability. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.protechting.com/">Apply until</a> Dec 05</p><p>🔷 <strong>Discoveries</strong>, the acceleration program that helps tourism startups grow, connect and go global powered by Fabrica de Startups <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.startupdiscoveries.com/">is now open</a></p><p></p><p></p><h1>Congrats</h1><p>👏  <strong>Felipe Ávila da Costa</strong> (Infraspeak) won João Vasconcelos – Empreendedor do Ano</p><p>👏  <strong>Isabel Carapeta</strong> (Simplifyer) won Rising Female Award </p><p>👏  <strong>Veronica Orvalho </strong>(Didimo) won International Personality Award</p><p>👏  <strong>Ana Casaca</strong> (Galp) won Ecosystem Award</p><p>👏  Startups: <strong>Lampsy</strong> won the Most Promising Startup; <strong>Ubbu </strong>won Impact Startup; and <strong>ROOTkey </strong>awarded with Rising Startup </p><p>👏  <strong>Cíntia Mano </strong>Among Finalists for the Golden Aurora Award 2025</p><p> </p><h1>Something to read, listen and watch</h1><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/posts/a-startup-in-54-hours-repboost-wins-techstars-startup-weekend-viseu">a Startup in 54 hours: RepBoost Wins Techstars Startup Weekend Viseu</a> a talk with the winning team</p><p>📚Eles querem <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://observador.pt/especiais/eles-querem-fazer-de-lisboa-a-capital-da-inteligencia-artificial-durante-uma-semana/">fazer de Lisboa a capital da inteligência artificial</a> durante uma semana</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.publico.pt/2025/10/27/ciencia/noticia/portugal-pedidos-patentes-desde-2000-continua-aquem-parceiros-europeus-2152031">Portugal tem mais pedidos de patentes desde 2000</a>, mas continua aquém dos parceiros europeus</p><p>📚 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.theportugalnews.com/news/2025-10-16/portugals-innovation-spirit-to-invest-in-the-future-of-technology/901456">Portugal’s Innovation Spirit</a> to Invest in the Future of Technology by Paulo Lopes</p><p>📚 The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://implementconsultinggroup.com/article/the-ai-opportunity-for-egovernment-in-portugal">AI opportunity for the eGov</a> in Portugal </p><p>📚Best of the Best <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.thetechedvocate.org/best-of-the-best-ar-vr-3d-educational-experiences-2026/">AR/VR/3D Educational Experiences</a> 2026</p><p>📚The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.siliconcontinent.com/p/the-ai-becker-problem">AI Becker problem</a>: Who will train the next generation?</p><p>📚For Some Recent Graduates, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/30/technology/ai-jobs-college-graduates.html">the A.I. Job Apocalypse</a> </p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://news.crunchbase.com/sales-marketing/ai-era-marketing-problem-islam-optimizely/">Marketing In The AI Era</a> Has A Marketing Problem</p><p>📚<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://pitchbook.com/news/articles/vcs-step-up-funding-for-european-defense-hard">VCs in European defense</a> sharpen focus on weapons and hardware</p><p>🎧 Elad Gil <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/0fJQVEKvaSgeaNbUe3lyZI?si=DrJONHMnS1uIju86a6Eh9A">on the power of peer groups</a></p><p>🎧 Marc Andreessen, cofounder of Netscape and Andreessen Horowitz, sits down for a Cheeky Pint with John Collison and Charlie Songhurst <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/19SMW5vhDIqPdXjWSvmNN2?si=BVAE0BwlRS-F5yNq_beoGA">to discuss the history of Silicon Valley</a></p><p>🎥 Bitalk - <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tcnOlPjOiS8">SEGREDOS JURÍDICOS QUE SÓ OS ADVOGADOS SABEM</a> c/ Luís Roquette Geraldes </p><p>🎥 Techstars: Co-Founder &amp; CEO David Cohen <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/SmAs7V8-EXk?si=2b0nWZCDL577vVsL">on Secrets of Startup Success</a> </p><p>🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://www.rtp.pt/play/p14282/e885117/sociedade-civil">Sociedade Civil (RTP2): Startups com Impacto</a> c/ intervenção de Startup Portugal, UPTEC, ILof, Intuitivo, Rubynanomed, Unicorn Factory Lisboa, Gotech Antimicrobial, Junicoders, and Startup Braga</p><p></p><p>💡Looking for your next spark of inspiration or connection? Discover what’s happening in the ecosystem—check out the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:text-primary transition-colors cursor-pointer" href="https://adamastor.blog/events"><strong>Adamastor Events Calendar</strong></a> and find the perfect event that fits your goals, your vibe, and your stage. From founder meetups to investor talks, there’s something for everyone.</p><p></p><p></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
  </channel>
